E["item:alien-egg"] = {t="item",n="Alien Egg",z="thousandneedles",s="Wind serpents guard an unfamiliar clutch in Thousand Needles, and tauren scouts at Freewind Post want to know why.",h="Wind serpents guard an unfamiliar clutch in Thousand Needles, and tauren scouts at Freewind Post want to know...",sec={{t="A Serpent's Brood",b="Alien Egg lies at the base of spires south and northeast of Freewind Post. Native wind serpents guard it beside their own nests, though such a clutch is strange among the life on the canyon floor. Hagar Lightninghoof, a tauren brave watching from Freewind Post, wants to retrieve it. He hopes to learn whether it threatens the mesa settlements or is simply an unusual local reptile.",sp=0},{t="The Spawn of Arikara",b="At Freewind Post, Alien Egg opens under closer inspection. Arikara, the red wind serpent of tauren legend, emerges from the shell. The tauren believe Arikara is a spirit of vengeance. The young serpent takes flight, and a shaken Hagar declares that vengeance has come to Thousand Needles. Local defenders set out to confront her.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the egg called 'alien'?",a="The tauren scouts call Alien Egg alien because it is completely foreign and unfamiliar to them. Its colors and markings differ from ordinary wind serpent clutches in Thousand Needles.",al={"alien egg name","why alien","is it from space"},it="name"},{q="Where can the Alien Egg be found?",a="Alien Egg lies on the canyon floor near mesa walls south and northeast of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Hostile wind serpents surround and guard it.",al={"egg location","where is alien egg","find alien egg"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the local serpents guard the egg?",a="No one knows why the local serpents guard Alien Egg. They protect it as if it were their own, and those who have seen it have not come close enough to examine it.",al={"why do serpents protect it","serpents guarding egg"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What happens when you bring the egg to Hagar Lightninghoof?",a="When you bring Alien Egg to Hagar Lightninghoof at Freewind Post, it hatches before his eyes. What emerges shakes Hagar so badly that he immediately seeks counsel from Motega Firemane.",al={"hagar egg turn in","what hatches"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is the Alien Egg?",a="The Alien Egg is an unusual, mysterious clutch found resting among the wild wind serpents of Thousand Needles. Unlike typical serpent eggs of the region, its strange appearance caught the attention of scouts and shamans at Freewind Post. Despite its foreign nature, the local serpents protect it fiercely as if it were their own brood.",al={"what is alien egg","alien egg info","about alien egg"},it="identity",add="9259de71"},{q="Why does Hagar Lightninghoof want the Alien Egg?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof at Freewind Post heard rumors of a bizarre egg guarded by local serpents that none of his scouts could get close enough to study. Driven by curiosity and caution, he asks brave adventurers to recover the egg so he can inspect it directly and uncover what kind of creature might hatch from it.",al={"why want alien egg","why does hagar want the egg","alien egg purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="e10e9f00"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you keep watch over the canyon from Freewind Post. Unknown creatures can seem like an omen or a direct threat to your precarious cliffside home.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know wind serpents are among the most revered beasts of the Kalimdor barrens. Tracking one of their rarest and most guarded clutches tests your instincts."},kw={"alien egg","freewind post","hagar lightninghoof","thousand needles","wind serpent"},rel={"quest:4821","quest:5088","npc:hagar-lightninghoof","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Alien Egg","Alien Egg (quest)"}}
E["item:arnak-s-hoof"] = {t="item",n="Arnak's Hoof",z="thousandneedles",s="On Darkcloud Pinnacle, Arnak Grimtotem awaits execution for murder and kidnapping. Freewind Post's defenders marked him for death after he killed a fellow tauren and took the tauren's sister.",h="On Darkcloud Pinnacle, Arnak Grimtotem awaits execution for murder and kidnapping.",sec={{t="Bounty on an Outcast",b="Across Thousand Needles, Arnak Grimtotem is feared as an outlaw. His brutality has crossed even the bitter divisions among tauren clans. He murdered a fellow tauren and abducted the victim’s sister, Lakota Windsong.\n\nSo the defenders of Freewind Post marked him for execution and set a bounty on his death. Arnak took refuge on Darkcloud Pinnacle, guarded by Grimtotem. His severed hoof proves to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post that the murderer has answered for his crimes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Arnak's Hoof used for?",a="Arnak's Hoof proves that the outlaw Arnak Grimtotem is dead. You bring it to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post to fulfill the wanted bounty and claim the promised reward.",al={"arnak hoof turn in","what do i do with arnak's hoof","who wants arnak's hoof"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who was Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Arnak Grimtotem was a Grimtotem renegade wanted for murder and kidnapping. He killed a fellow tauren and held the victim's sister, Lakota Windsong, captive on the bluffs of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"who is arnak","arnak grimtotem lore","why is arnak wanted"},it="people"},{q="Where is Arnak Grimtotem found?",a="You find Arnak on the cliffs of Darkcloud Pinnacle in northern Thousand Needles. Rope bridges near the crags approaching Razorfen Downs lead there. Lakota Windsong is held captive on the same bluff.",al={"arnak grimtotem location","where is arnak","how to find arnak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Arnak's Hoof?",a="This severed hoof serves as undeniable proof that the outlaw tauren Arnak Grimtotem has been slain. Taken directly from his body atop the windswept mesas of Thousand Needles, it is carried back to Freewind Post to confirm that justice has finally caught up with the outcast rogue.",al={"arnak hoof","what is this hoof","arnaks hoof"},it="identity",add="8804d903"},{q="Where does Arnak's Hoof come from?",a="It is taken from Arnak Grimtotem, a renegade tauren lurking on the cliffs near Darkcloud Pinnacle. Rather than being forged or crafted, it is a physical trophy claimed after confronting and slaying him at his hideout overlooking the canyons.",al={"where do you get arnaks hoof","who made arnaks hoof","arnak hoof origin"},it="origin",add="a4f2e55c"},{q="Why does anyone want Arnak's Hoof?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn in Freewind Post posted a bounty demanding proof of Arnak's demise. Arnak committed heinous crimes—slaying an innocent tauren and kidnapping his sister, Lakota Windsong. Delivering his hoof fulfills the bounty and earns the gratitude and coin of Freewind Post's protectors.",al={"who wants arnaks hoof","why turn in arnak hoof","why want arnak hoof"},it="why_wanted",add="ffececdb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren of the plains, you bring tribal justice by taking Arnak's hoof. His murders brought dishonor and bloodshed to Thousand Needles.",["faction:Horde"]="By eliminating Arnak, you uphold Freewind Post's authority in Thousand Needles. You also weaken the treacherous Grimtotem influence threatening Horde supply routes."},kw={"arnak","arnak grimtotem","arnak's hoof","cliffwatcher longhorn","darkcloud pinnacle","freewind post","lakota windsong","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:5147","npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","npc:lakota-windsong","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","quest:4904","quest:5064","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Arnak's Hoof","Wanted - Arnak Grimtotem"}}
E["item:crate-of-crash-helmets"] = {t="item",n="Crate of Crash Helmets",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Shimmering Flats, Wizzle Brassbolts and his brother need helmets for their rocket car test drivers. Heavy dwarven Siege Engine headgear is bound for Thousand Needles to guard pilots against concussions.",h="At the Shimmering Flats, Wizzle Brassbolts and his brother need helmets for their rocket car test drivers.",sec={{t="Safety at High Speeds",b="Gnome engineers race rocket cars across the Shimmering Flats. Wizzle Brassbolts and his brother build machines that outrun their drivers’ ability to steer. Crashes leave test pilots with head injuries, and leather caps no longer suffice. So heavy dwarven Siege Engine helmets are shipped across the sea to keep the drivers conscious and alive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Crate of Crash Helmets?",a="The crate holds heavy Siege Engine helmets taken from dwarven military stocks. Their thick protection guards against concussive blasts and hard impacts during high-speed trials.",al={"crate contents","what helmets are these","crash helmets type"},it="identity"},{q="Who needs these helmets?",a="Wizzle Brassbolts and his brother need the helmets at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. Their designs leave test pilots with head injuries, so the drivers need serious protection.",al={"who gets the helmets","who is the crate for","helmet destination"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are the Brassbolts brothers crashing so much?",a="The Brassbolts brothers build for speed and push the limits of gnomish engineering, with little regard for stable handling. Their rocket car moves so fast that collisions on the salt flats are almost unavoidable.",al={"why do they crash","rocket car problems","gnome racing crashes"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the helmets being delivered?",a="The helmets are bound for the Shimmering Flats, a vast salt plain in southeastern Thousand Needles, Kalimdor.",al={"delivery location","where is wizzle","where do these go"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does the Crate of Crash Helmets come from, and who made it?",a="The crate is packed and provided by the dwarven engineer Pilot Longbeard in Dun Morogh. Longbeard gathered a supply of sturdy dwarven Siege Engine helmets to help his old friends, the Brassbolts brothers, who are desperately in need of head protection for their test pilots out in the Shimmering Flats.",al={"who made crate of crash helmets","where did crate of crash helmets come from","crash helmets origin"},it="origin",add="94078cd5"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers know the balance between propulsion and failure. They know how much heavy armor matters when safety features come second.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome at the Mirage Raceway, you see pilot concussions come with the work of out-innovating goblin rivals on the salt flats."},kw={"crate of crash helmets","mirage raceway","rocket car","shimmering flats","siege engine","thousand needles","wizzle brassbolts"},rel={"quest:1179","npc:wizzle-brassbolts","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},src={"Crate of Crash Helmets","The Brassbolts Brothers"}}
E["item:fragments-of-rok-alim"] = {t="item",n="Fragments of Rok'Alim",z="thousandneedles",s="Across Thousand Needles, Rok'Alim's stone fragments bear witness to a warrior's victory. Dorn Plainstalker at the Weathered Nook seeks them as proof Rok'Alim fell in single combat.",h="Across Thousand Needles, Rok'Alim's stone fragments bear witness to a warrior's victory.",sec={{t="Remnants of an Ancient Power",b="Rok'Alim the Pounder still walks the canyon flats south of the main thoroughfare. Most elementals faded from Azeroth after the Old Gods were banished, though a few powerful ones endured without mortal summoning. The local centaur know Rok'Alim by the crashes of his stone fists as they crush anything in his path. Defeat leaves jagged pieces of dense, animated rock, proof of a warrior's might.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of Might",b="Dorn Plainstalker needs the fragments for the Test of Strength. The tauren hermit holds spiritual and martial rites high in the Weathered Nook. An initiate must face a being of unyielding brute force. Bringing Dorn the battered pieces of Rok'Alim proves the bravery and might needed to survive Kalimdor's harshest perils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are the Fragments of Rok'Alim?",a="The Fragments of Rok'Alim are broken pieces of Rok'Alim the Pounder, an ancient earth elemental who prowls Thousand Needles' northwestern canyons. They prove he was defeated.",al={"fragments of rokalim","what are rokalim fragments","rokalims stone"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants these stone fragments?",a="Dorn Plainstalker wants the stone fragments for the Test of Strength. The tauren hermit lives at the Weathered Nook high along Thousand Needles' canyon cliffs.",al={"who takes rokalim fragments","turn in fragments of rokalim","dorn plainstalker quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Rok'Alim significant?",a="Rok'Alim has endured since the era of the Old Gods, though most elementals faded after their banishment unless mortals summoned them. Centaur tribes in the canyons know him as the Pounder for the crashes of his fists as they crush prey.",al={"why is rokalim special","rokalim lore","who is rokalim the pounder"},it="power"},{q="Where is Rok'Alim found?",a="Rok'Alim roams Thousand Needles' northwestern basin, south of the region's main road among the sandstone spires.",al={"rokalim location","find rokalim the pounder","where does rokalim spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where do the Fragments of Rok'Alim come from?",a="These fragments are shattered pieces of Rok'Alim the Pounder, a massive rock elemental wandering the north-western canyon floor of Thousand Needles. Unlike elementals conjured by mortal spellcasters, Rok'Alim is an ancient survivor from the era of the Old Gods, possessing enough innate power to remain tethered to the world even after his masters fell. They were not crafted by mortal hands, but broken directly from his living stone form.",al={"fragments of rokalim origin","where do rokalim fragments come from","who made rokalim fragments"},it="origin",add="ab6946f8"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, facing the land's most formidable hazards tests your harmony, fortitude, and strength against remnants of Azeroth's primordial past.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can study Rok'Alim's unyielding nature as an example of elemental tenacity. He is an ancient earth spirit bound to the world before modern shamanic pacts."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","elemental","fragments","pounder","rok'alim","test of strength","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"quest:1151","npc:dorn-plainstalker","subzone:weathered-nook","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1149","topic:old-god","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},src={"Fragments of Rok'Alim","Test of Strength"}}
E["item:grenka-s-claw"] = {t="item",n="Grenka's Claw",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, Grenka's Claw marks survival in the depths of Roguefeather Den. At the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker receives it as proof of an aspiring adventurer's endurance in the canyon heights.",h="In Thousand Needles, Grenka's Claw marks survival in the depths of Roguefeather Den.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Endurance",b="Harpies cache food in Roguefeather Den, west of Freewind Post, and fiercely guard their territory. Dorn Plainstalker sends young champions into the deep roosts to destroy the flock's food reserves and test their strength. Such an intrusion draws Grenka Bloodscreech's fury. Returning her wicked talon proves a warrior endured wave after wave of enraged harpies and survived their matriarch's vicious assault.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Grenka's Claw used for?",a="At the Weathered Nook in Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker accepts the claw as proof of victory. Giving it to him completes the Test of Endurance and shows you can survive a long fight.",al={"use of grenka claw","why do i need grenkas claw","grenkas claw quest"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Who is Grenka Bloodscreech?",a="Grenka Bloodscreech is a powerful harpy in Roguefeather Den, in Screeching Canyon along Thousand Needles' southern cliffs. She emerges when intruders threaten the flock by destroying its stored food.",al={"who is grenka","grenka bloodscreech lore","what is grenka"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I take the claw once I obtain it?",a="Take the claw to Dorn Plainstalker at the Weathered Nook in the bluffs of Thousand Needles. He accepts it as proof that you passed the trial of physical endurance.",al={"where to turn in grenka claw","who wants grenkas claw"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Dorn Plainstalker demand this specific trophy?",a="Dorn Plainstalker guides young travelers through hard trials to ready their minds, spirits, and bodies for greater perils. Slaying Grenka and claiming her claw proves a warrior can endure a swarm's ambush and the deadly leader's direct assault.",al={"why dorn wants claw","purpose of the claw"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Grenka's Claw?",a="Grenka's Claw is a physical trophy taken from Grenka Bloodscreech, a formidable harpy dwelling deep within the Roguefeather Den in Screeching Canyon. Severed from the vicious creature after provoking and surviving the wrath of her flock, the claw serves as undeniable proof that an aspiring adventurer possessed the stamina and martial prowess to withstand a brutal trial of combat.",al={"grenkas claw","what is grenka claw","about grenkas claw"},it="identity",add="cd538a11"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Elder Dorn Plainstalker sees it as his sacred duty to prepare young Horde champions for the wider, harsher world through the wisdom and grit of tauren rites.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing Roguefeather Den's deep reaches and killing Grenka Bloodscreech blunts the harpy threat that constantly harasses travelers around Freewind Post."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","grenka bloodscreech","grenka's claw","harpy","roguefeather den","screeching canyon","test of endurance","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"quest:1150","quest:1149","npc:dorn-plainstalker","subzone:roguefeather-den","subzone:weathered-nook","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post","topic:harpy"},src={"Grenka's Claw","Test of Endurance"}}
E["item:hardened-tortoise-shell"] = {t="item",n="Hardened Tortoise Shell",z="thousandneedles",s="Across the Shimmering Flats, racers seek shells tough enough for dangerous fuel. Gnomish racers at the Mirage Raceway prize Hardened Tortoise Shells from sparkleshell tortoises because they resist volatile, corrosive experimental fuels.",h="Across the Shimmering Flats, racers seek shells tough enough for dangerous fuel.",sec={{t="Natural Armor for High-Speed Hazards",b="Sparkleshell tortoises, from snappers to borers, roam the salt flats. Their carapaces shield them from the salt and wandering predators. Gnomish experimental chemistry can corrode or rupture metal fuel tanks. So mechanics such as Wizzle Brassbolts prize the shells as raw material for makeshift tanks that resist acid and hold volatile rocket propellants.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do you find Hardened Tortoise Shells?",a="Across the open salt expanses of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles, you can find Hardened Tortoise Shells on Sparkleshell Snappers, Borers, and common Sparkleshell Tortoises.",al={"where to get tortoise shells","hardened shell location","sparkleshell location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Wizzle Brassbolts want these shells?",a="Wizzle Brassbolts wants the shells for fuel tanks. Wizzle's brother is designing an extremely powerful, corrosive rocket fuel that threatens to melt their race car's chassis. Wizzle plans to hollow out and reinforce the durable carapaces.",al={"why need shells","wizzle shells use","what are shells for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can standard workshop tools easily shape them?",a="No. The carapaces are unnaturally hard. Gnomish mechanics expect to ruin a toolbox worth of metal implements carving, drilling, and shaping them into tanks.",al={"are shells hard to craft","bending tools shell"}},{q="What is a Hardened Tortoise Shell?",a="It is the exceptionally durable, natural outer carapace harvested from the large sparkleshell tortoises roaming the salt flats. These shells are known to be far tougher than ordinary beast hides or standard plating, resisting friction, salt, and intense chemical erosion.",al={"what is hardened tortoise shell","hardened tortoise shell item","hardened shell"},it="identity",add="cc86b908"},{q="Where does a Hardened Tortoise Shell come from?",a="These shells are completely natural rather than manufactured. They are harvested directly from the sparkleshell tortoises, snappers, and borers that thrive in the harsh, sun-baked salt wilderness of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",al={"origin of hardened tortoise shell","who made hardened tortoise shell","where do hardened shells come from"},it="origin",add="4ed6fee7"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see why organic carapaces might suit high-pressure fuel tanks. When gnome-brewed fuel melts standard alloy piping, durable natural materials can take its place.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you might look at a desert tortoise and see a lightweight, resilient container for dangerous rocket fuel."},kw={"hardened tortoise shell","mirage raceway","rocket car","shimmering flats","sparkleshell","wizzle brassbolts"},rel={"quest:1105","npc:wizzle-brassbolts","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},src={"Hardened Tortoise Shell","Hardened Shells"}}
E["item:highperch-venom-sac"] = {t="item",n="Highperch Venom Sac",z="thousandneedles",s="At Highperch, wyverns carry venom that buyers seek across Kalimdor. Their sacs draw trade even where the beasts do not fly.",h="At Highperch, wyverns carry venom that buyers seek across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Potent Harvest",b="Wild wyverns nest among Highperch's crags in Thousand Needles. Their barbed tails deliver venom that can paralyze or kill prey. The Horde often domesticates wyverns as wind riders. Across Kalimdor, alchemists, hunters, and merchants pay well for the venom sacs.",sp=0},{t="A Faraway Buyer",b="Highperch venom reaches buyers far from central Kalimdor. In Theramore, the high elf Fiora Longears pays well for fresh sacs gathered from Highperch broods. She seeks sacs swollen with venom, most often found on young wyverns or fertile females. Far from their desert home, she trades these dangerous reagents.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures carry these venom sacs?",a="Wild wyverns at Highperch carry the sacs. They include Highperch Wyverns, Patriarchs, Consorts, and the matriarch Heartrazor.",al={"where do venom sacs drop","who drops highperch venom","wyvern venom drop"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Fiora Longears want this venom in Theramore?",a="Fiora Longears knows wyvern venom is highly valued in some trading circles, sometimes more than the mounts. She pays travelers bound for Highperch in Thousand Needles to bring back intact sacs for trade.",al={"why fiora want venom","theramore venom buyer","who buys wyvern venom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are all wyvern venom sacs identical?",a="The sacs vary in potency and volume. The most prized are swollen with poison, usually those of young wyverns or fertile breeding females.",al={"wyvern venom quality","bursting venom sacs"}},{q="How does the Horde utilize these wyverns compared to the Alliance?",a="The Horde captures and breeds wyverns as aerial mounts and scouts called wind riders. Independent traders and Alliance contacts without domestic taming networks harvest the beasts for their lethal reagents.",al={"horde wyvern use","do orcs use the venom"}},{q="What is a Highperch Venom Sac?",a="A Highperch Venom Sac is an organ harvested from the wild wyverns that nest upon the towering mesa of Highperch in Thousand Needles. While wyverns are best known across Kalimdor as winged mounts utilized by the Horde, their venom is prized for its sheer potency. The sacs taken from the beasts atop Highperch are particularly rich and swollen with this deadly toxin, making them a lucrative prize for alchemists and traders who deal in exotic animal reagents.",al={"what is highperch venom sac","highperch venom sac","wyvern venom sac"},it="identity",add="98761a97"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can find some of Kalimdor's most potent natural toxins in the concentrated paralyzing venom of untamed wyverns in Thousand Needles.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can strike at Highperch's nests for valuable trade reagents and cull wild wyverns the Horde might otherwise capture and break as mounts."},kw={"fiora longears","heartrazor","highperch","poison","theramore","thousand needles","venom sac","wyvern"},rel={"quest:1135","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1132","subzone:theramore-isle","zone:dustwallow"},src={"Highperch Venom Sac","Highperch Venom"}}
E["item:highperch-wyvern-egg"] = {t="item",n="Highperch Wyvern Egg",z="thousandneedles",s="At Highperch, Horde trainees seek wyvern eggs to raise as mounts. The nests lie above the mesas of Thousand Needles.",h="At Highperch, Horde trainees seek wyvern eggs to raise as mounts.",sec={{t="Nests on the Mesa",b="Highperch gives native wyverns a place to roost and raise their young above Thousand Needles. Steep paths wind up the canyon walls to the nesting grounds, where adult wyverns guard their nests. Within sturdy, warm shells, hatchlings wait to face Kalimdor's harsh skies.",sp=0},{t="Raising New Wind Riders",b="The Horde needs more trained wyverns for its courier and scouting networks across Kalimdor. At Freewind Post, trainees such as the tauren Elu seek intact eggs from wild nests. They raise the hatchlings from the shell, hoping to form the bond that makes a trustworthy mount for a wind rider.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are these eggs found?",a="The eggs lie in nests across Highperch, a mesa along the western rock walls of Thousand Needles. A path climbs there from the canyon floor.",al={"egg locations","where to find wyvern eggs","highperch eggs location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde collect wild wyvern eggs?",a="The Horde's wind rider ranks are growing, and trained wyverns are in short supply. Trainees such as Elu gather eggs and raise the hatchlings from birth for aerial duty.",al={"why steal wyvern eggs","what are the eggs used for","elu egg quest purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the parent wyverns hostile to egg gatherers?",a="Yes. Wild wyverns fiercely guard their nests and attack intruders who trespass on Highperch to disturb their clutches.",al={"do wyverns attack","are wyverns protective"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="Who accepts these eggs in Freewind Post?",a="Elu, an aspiring wind rider stationed at Freewind Post, collects eggs to begin training a mount of his own.",al={"who takes wyvern eggs","elu freewind post"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is a Highperch Wyvern Egg?",a="These are the viable eggs of wild wyverns nesting high atop the canyon mesas of Thousand Needles. Within their sturdy shells rest the unhatched young of Kalimdor's winged predators, highly sought after by those wishing to raise loyal aerial mounts from infancy.",al={"what is highperch wyvern egg","wyvern egg info","what are these eggs"},it="identity",add="efbaa71b"},{q="Where do Highperch Wyvern Eggs come from?",a="They are laid by wild wyverns in their clifftop nests at Highperch, an elevated plateau rising above the canyons of Thousand Needles. The adult wyverns guard their aeries fiercely against predators and daring scavengers alike.",al={"where do highperch wyvern eggs come from","who laid the eggs","wyvern egg origin"},it="origin",add="bbfa5024"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know reliable air travel keeps communication and military readiness across Kalimdor's vast territories. Fresh wyverns matter to both.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you must read the fierce predators guarding Highperch. Adult wyverns defend their nests with claws and venomous stingers."},kw={"elu","freewind post","highperch","highperch wyvern egg","thousand needles","wind rider","wyvern"},rel={"quest:4767","subzone:highperch","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},src={"Highperch Wyvern Egg","Wind Rider (quest)"}}
E["item:hollow-vulture-bone"] = {t="item",n="Hollow Vulture Bone",z="thousandneedles",s="Across the Shimmering Flats, vultures circle the salt while goblin crews gather their bones. At the Mirage Raceway, mechanics use the hollow remains to lighten rocket cars without weakening them.",h="Across the Shimmering Flats, vultures circle the salt while goblin crews gather their bones.",sec={{t="Racing Materials on the Flats",b="At the Mirage Raceway, goblin pit crews look for every way to make their rocket cars faster. Weight slows a car, so they use what the desert provides alongside iron and copper. Hollow vulture bones are light yet sturdy enough for steering rigs, internal brackets, and small supports. Pozzik and the other chief tinkerers gather them from local scavengers to save seconds on the track.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do the goblins want vulture bones?",a="Pozzik and other goblin engineers use hollow vulture bones to lighten rocket cars. The bones are light and strong enough for steering rigs and small supports.",al={"why bones","goblin bones use","pozzik bone use"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do these bones come from?",a="Salt Flats Scavengers and Salt Flats Vultures provide the bones around the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles, especially near the giant skeletal remains scattered across the salt desert.",al={"where to find hollow vulture bone","vulture bone location","how to get vulture bones"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Pozzik?",a="Pozzik is a goblin engineer and lead mechanic at the Mirage Raceway. He tunes and modifies rocket cars to compete against the gnomish team led by Fizzle Brassbolts.",al={"who is pozzik","pozzik raceway","who takes the bones"}},{q="What is a Hollow Vulture Bone?",a="These are lightweight, sturdy bones scavenged from the carrion birds wheeling over the Shimmering Flats. Avian skeletons are naturally hollow to aid in flight, making them uniquely suited for mechanical engineering where shaving every extra pound matters. At the Mirage Raceway, goblin mechanics use them to craft resilient structural parts and steering components for their rocket cars.",al={"what is hollow vulture bone","hollow vulture bones"},it="identity",add="2d4c7633"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Goblin racers use hollow bird bones to save weight where iron and bronze would be heavy. Their choice shows a practical approach to racing design.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track the hardy carrion-feeding vultures across the blinding salt bed."},kw={"hollow vulture bone","load lightening","mirage raceway","pozzik","scavenger","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:1176","npc:pozzik","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin"},src={"Hollow Vulture Bone","Load Lightening"}}
E["item:hypercapacitor-gizmo"] = {t="item",n="Hypercapacitor Gizmo",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, the Hypercapacitor Gizmo lies among the wreckage of a goblin caravan. A caged panther wore it around its neck, and even its owner does not know what it does.",h="In Thousand Needles, the Hypercapacitor Gizmo lies among the wreckage of a goblin caravan.",sec={{t="A Caravan's Strange Relic",b="Centaur marauders ambushed a goblin caravan crossing Thousand Needles and plundered nearly everything. Wizlo Bearingshiner, the lone survivor, crawled to safety at Whitereach Post. He left his best gizmo behind, fastened around the neck of a ferocious, enraged panther locked in a transport cage. The centaur feared the beast and left the cage untouched in the burning wreckage.",sp=0},{t="Tinkering in the Dark",b="Wizlo proudly calls the Hypercapacitor Gizmo his best gizmo, though he admits he has no idea what it does. The device tangles ambition with volatile parts. Wizlo can only keep tinkering, unsure what practical use it might have.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hypercapacitor Gizmo?",a="The Hypercapacitor Gizmo belongs to Wizlo Bearingshiner, a goblin engineer. Even Wizlo does not know what it does, so he intends to study it until he discovers its purpose.",al={"what is gizmo","hypercapacitor","what does the gizmo do"},it="identity"},{q="How did the device end up around a panther's neck?",a="Centaur attacked and ransacked Wizlo's caravan in northern Thousand Needles. In the chaos, the device was fastened around the neck of an enraged panther in a traveling cage. The superstitious centaur feared the beast and left it alone.",al={"why panther has gizmo","how did panther get it"},it="history"},{q="Who wants the Hypercapacitor Gizmo back?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner wants the Hypercapacitor Gizmo back. The caravan's sole survivor has taken refuge at Whitereach Post, a Tauren encampment in northwestern Thousand Needles.",al={"who needs gizmo","wizlo gizmo"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why didn't the centaur steal it?",a="The centaur ransacked the caravan but feared the ferocious panther in its cage. They left the beast and its metal collar untouched among the ruins.",al={"why didn't centaur take it","centaur and panther"}},{q="Where does the Hypercapacitor Gizmo come from, and who made it?",a="The device was in the possession of the goblin tinkerer Wizlo Bearingshiner, traveling with a caravan through Thousand Needles before centaur ambushed them. While Wizlo claims it as his prized gizmo, its precise inventor remains a mystery—even Wizlo admits he does not fully understand what the curious machine actually does.",al={"who made hypercapacitor gizmo","hypercapacitor gizmo origin","where did wizlo get hypercapacitor"},it="origin",add="240fe489"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The gizmo has the feel of goblin engineering: an intricate device with a grand name, built with enthusiasm before anyone decided what it should do.",["faction:Horde"]="Travelers who aid Whitereach Post help drive off aggressive centaur and recover lost oddities from ruined caravans across the canyon floor."},kw={"centaur","enraged panther","gizmo","hypercapacitor","thousand needles","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"quest:5151","npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","item:panther-cage-key","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},src={"Hypercapacitor Gizmo","Hypercapacitor Gizmo (quest)"}}
E["item:kravel-s-crate"] = {t="item",n="Kravel's Crate",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard has a crate to send to the Nesingwary expedition in Stranglethorn Vale. It holds specialized ammunition for hunting the jungle’s deadliest game.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard has a crate to send to the Nesingwary expedition in Stranglethorn...",sec={{t="A Delivery to the Jungle",b="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard hands the crate to travelers. A wealthy dwarven patron ordered it weeks ago, but the shipment was delayed until the buyer had left Kalimdor. The patron had paid for forwarding, and Kravel wants to keep the favor of a wealthy customer. So he trusts passing travelers to carry it across continents to northern Stranglethorn Vale.",sp=0},{t="Special-Gauge Ammunition",b="Salt dust gathers on the crate as it waits in the Shimmering Flats. Inside are heavy, special-gauge rounds made for hunting rifles. The travelers deliver them to the expedition camp north of Grom'gol. The recipient says big-game hunters prize the potent ammunition. Against the predators roaming the jungle canopy, it is vital for survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Kravel's Crate?",a="Kravel's Crate holds heavy, special-gauge ammunition for hunting rifles. Big-game hunters use it against dangerous beasts in the wild.",al={"what's in the crate","crate contents","what is in kravels crate"},it="item"},{q="Who sent Kravel's Crate?",a="Kravel Koalbeard sent the crate. He is a dwarven merchant at the Mirage Raceway, amid the racing and gambling of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",al={"who gives the crate","who owns kravels crate"},it="origin"},{q="Where does this crate need to go?",a="The crate is bound for the Nesingwary hunting expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale. The camp lies along the river north of Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"where to deliver crate","crate destination","who gets kravels crate"},it="target"},{q="Why was the delivery delayed?",a="The parcel took weeks to reach the Thousand Needles salt flats. By then, the customer had packed up and left for the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"why did kravel take so long","why delayed"},it="motive"},{q="What is Kravel's Crate?",a="It is a heavy delivery package held by Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. Packed securely for long-distance transport across Kalimdor and the Great Sea, the crate holds specialized hunting supplies intended for an expedition out in the wilds of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"what is kravel's crate","kravels crate info","kravel crate item"},it="identity",add="3beca7b7"},{q="Why is Kravel's Crate wanted?",a="The crate contains special-gauge ammunition ordered specifically for big game hunting. The Nesingwary hunting expedition in Stranglethorn Vale relies on heavy, reliable munitions to bring down the jungle's fiercest beasts, making this delayed shipment an essential resupply for their camp.",al={"why does nesingwary want the crate","why is kravels crate important","kravel crate purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="6061fde3"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you find specialized heavy ammunition in the crate. It is made for high-end dwarven hunting rifles and big-game expeditions.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see Kravel Koalbeard's business in the salt flats linked to the renowned Nesingwary hunting party in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"ammunition","hemet nesingwary","kravel koalbeard","kravel's crate","mirage raceway","shimmering flats","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","quest:5762","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:stranglethorn","zone:thousandneedles","topic:hunter"},src={"Kravel's Crate","Hemet Nesingwary (quest)","Hemet Nesingwary Jr. (quest)"}}
E["item:legacy-of-the-aspects"] = {t="item",n="Legacy of the Aspects",z="thousandneedles",s="In the Horde trial, seekers must find Legacy of the Aspects and remember its lessons. The ancient tome lies in Dor'Danil Barrow Den in southern Ashenvale, where it holds lore about the Great Aspects who shaped ancient Azeroth.",h="In the Horde trial, seekers must find Legacy of the Aspects and remember its lessons.",sec={{t="A Test of the Mind",b="Braug Dimspirit sends aspirants to seek Legacy of the Aspects. Earlier trials set by tauren elders test endurance and resolve. This trial tests the mind. Braug waits at the entrance to the Talondeep Path in the Stonetalon Mountains, while the tome lies in the haunted barrow dens of Dor'Danil.\n\nRestless spirits of fallen druids and the vicious creatures that slew them guard the ancient text. It rests on a stone pedestal. Finding the volume is only the beginning. Before returning it, the seeker must commit its contents to memory. Then Braug tests them on its lessons in history.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the book located?",a="Legacy of the Aspects rests on a stone pedestal in the lower chambers of Dor'Danil Barrow Den in southern Ashenvale, south of Splintertree Post.",al={"find legacy of the aspects","book location","where is book"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Braug Dimspirit want this book?",a="Braug Dimspirit uses the tome for the Test of Lore. The trial tests whether an adventurer can study and recall vital historical knowledge, as well as wield physical strength.",al={"why braug wants book","test of lore purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens if you fail to study the text before speaking to Braug?",a="Braug questions seekers on the book's lore as soon as they collect it. A wrong answer brings swift magical banishment, sending the unprepared petitioner far away to Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.",al={"wrong answer consequence","failing the test"},gp=true},{q="What is Legacy of the Aspects?",a="The Legacy of the Aspects is an ancient and valuable tome resting deep within the Dor'Danil Barrow Den in southern Ashenvale. Guarded by the restless spirits of fallen druids and the vile creatures that slew them, the book contains historical lore concerning the Dragon Aspects, serving as an exacting test of wisdom and memory for those who dare retrieve it.",al={"what is legacy of the aspects","legacy of the aspects book","what is this book"},it="identity",add="32a02485"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you face a traditional rite of passage. It tests whether your wisdom and knowledge match your physical might.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find the text deep in Dor'Danil Barrow Den, among the tragic, tormented spirits of fallen night elf druids."},kw={"ashenvale","barrow den","braug dimspirit","dor'danil","legacy of the aspects","talondeep path","test of lore"},rel={"quest:1152","quest:1149","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","subzone:talondeep-path","zone:stonetalon","zone:ashenvale","subzone:camp-taurajo","topic:horde"},src={"Legacy of the Aspects","Test of Lore (2)"}}
E["item:lonebrow-s-journal"] = {t="item",n="Lonebrow's Journal",z="thousandneedles",s="At the base of the Great Lift, Henrig Lonebrow's journal records his final journey. He crossed the Barrens as danger gathered at Razorfen Kraul.",h="At the base of the Great Lift, Henrig Lonebrow's journal records his final journey.",sec={{t="A Dying Wish at the Great Lift",b="Henrig Lonebrow died near the base of the Great Lift, the passage between the Barrens and Thousand Needles. His bones rest on a rocky ledge with the weathered journal still in his grasp.\n\nThe pages recount his last travels and ask the finder to carry word to Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf druid at Thalanaar. The outpost lies on the border of Feralas. Lonebrow's notes warn of the quilboar threat growing in the southern Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Razorfen",b="Falfindel Waywarder receives records that confirm the Alliance's fears about the quilboar of Razorfen Kraul. Lonebrow's account calls for a strike at the heart of the thorny warren. Charlga Razorflank, the Crone of the Kraul, directs the threat.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Henrig Lonebrow?",a="Henrig Lonebrow was a dwarven traveler who died at the foot of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles. His journal remained in his hand, meant to carry his account to the night elves at Thalanaar.",al={"henrig lonebrow","who is lonebrow","dead dwarf lift"},it="people"},{q="Where is the journal found?",a="The journal lies beside Henrig Lonebrow's skeleton, on a low rocky ledge just off the ramp at the base of the Great Lift in northern Thousand Needles.",al={"where is lonebrow journal","find lonebrow journal","skeleton at great lift"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who should receive Lonebrow's Journal?",a="Carry Lonebrow's Journal west across Thousand Needles to Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf druid at Thalanaar on the border of Feralas.",al={"who do i bring journal to","falfindel waywarder","where to turn in journal"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What does the journal lead to?",a="The journal brings Falfindel Waywarder word of the quilboar. Its account calls for a strike on Razorfen Kraul and Charlga Razorflank.",al={"crone of the kraul quest","lonebrow journal follow up"},sp=1},{q="What is Lonebrow's Journal?",a="Lonebrow's Journal is a weathered personal log found clutched in the skeletal hands of the dwarf Henrig Lonebrow. Discovered at the foot of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles, it documents his travels and final wishes before he met his end in the canyon.",al={"lonebrow journal what is","what is this book","henrig lonebrows journal"},it="identity",add="a9190e03",nx={6}},{q="Where does Lonebrow's Journal come from, and who made it?",a="The journal was penned by Henrig Lonebrow, a dwarven traveler who journeyed through the treacherous canyons of Thousand Needles. He carried it with him until his death near the base of the Great Lift, where his remains and the volume were ultimately discovered.",al={"who wrote lonebrows journal","lonebrow journal author","where did the journal come from"},it="origin",add="090ee1d4"},{q="Why does anyone want Lonebrow's Journal?",a="Delivering the journal fulfills the fallen dwarf's final wishes. Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf druid stationed at Thalanaar on the border of Feralas, seeks to read its contents to understand Henrig's fate and uncover the dangers stirring in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"why deliver lonebrow journal","who needs lonebrows journal","why want lonebrows journal"},it="why_wanted",add="ea8f453f"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Finding a fallen dwarf in these remote, hostile lands reminds you of the dangers dwarven explorers face far from Khaz Modan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Henrig Lonebrow's last writings link Alliance scouts with the druids guarding the border to Feralas. They bring aid against the quilboar threat."},kw={"crone of the kraul","falfindel waywarder","great lift","henrig lonebrow","razorfen kraul","thalanaar","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:1100","quest:1101","subzone:great-lift","subzone:thalanaar","npc:falfindel-waywarder","zone:thousandneedles","zone:razorfenkraul","topic:dwarf"},src={"Lonebrow's Journal","Lonebrow's Journal (quest)"}}
E["item:panther-cage-key"] = {t="item",n="Panther Cage Key",z="thousandneedles",s="At Whitereach Post, Wizlo Bearingshiner guards the Panther Cage Key. It opens the cage left among the wrecked wagons of an ambushed caravan in Thousand Needles.",h="At Whitereach Post, Wizlo Bearingshiner guards the Panther Cage Key.",sec={{t="A Precarious Lock",b="Wizlo Bearingshiner is a goblin tinker who barely escaped a centaur attack on his caravan north of Whitereach Post. The raiders ransacked the wagons and cargo, yet left a sturdy cage untouched. A rare, ferocious panther waits inside. Around its neck hangs Wizlo’s prized invention, a hypercapacitor gizmo. The snarling beast kept the centaur at a distance, and only Wizlo’s key can open the cage and recover the device.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who provides the Panther Cage Key?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner, a goblin tinker resting at Whitereach Post in northwestern Thousand Needles, provides the key.",al={"who gives panther key","where to get panther cage key","panther cage key source"},it="origin"},{q="What does the key unlock?",a="The key opens an iron cage among the broken wagons of a ruined caravan just north of Whitereach Post. An enraged, dangerous panther is inside.",al={"what does panther key open","panther cage location","where is the cage"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't the centaur loot the cage?",a="The centaur ransacked the rest of the caravan but left the cage alone. The captive panther was too ferocious and threatening to approach.",al={"why did centaur leave panther","centaur afraid of panther"}},{q="What is inside the cage besides the beast?",a="Wizlo’s prized hypercapacitor gizmo hangs around the panther’s neck. To recover it, someone must unlock the cage and face the predator.",al={"why open the cage","what is on the panther"}},{q="Why does Wizlo Bearingshiner want the Panther Cage Key back?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner entrusts you with the key solely so you can open the cage at his wrecked caravan to slay the fierce panther within. The beast wears his prized hypercapacitor gizmo around its neck. He wants the key returned alongside his invention once the deed is done, ensuring the caravan's remnants and his dangerous property are fully accounted for.",al={"why panther cage key","why does wizlo need the key","why want panther cage key"},it="why_wanted",add="b335554a"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The key opens a cage holding a tinker's volatile prototype. Wizlo has left his delicate invention in a dangerous place.",["faction:Horde"]="Helping Wizlo can make the roads around Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles safer after centaur raids."},kw={"centaur","hypercapacitor gizmo","panther cage key","thousand needles","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","quest:5151","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},src={"Panther Cage Key","Hypercapacitor Gizmo (quest)"}}
E["item:rocket-car-parts"] = {t="item",n="Rocket Car Parts",z="thousandneedles",s="Across the Shimmering Flats, Rocket Car Parts lie scattered after mishaps at the Mirage Raceway. Gnome and goblin racers push their experimental speeders hard, and merchants gather wreckage to sell back to the teams.",h="Across the Shimmering Flats, Rocket Car Parts lie scattered after mishaps at the Mirage Raceway.",sec={{t="Speed, Wrecks, and Shrewd Commerce",b="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, gnome and goblin engineers compete fiercely. Their racers chase greater speed on land. Breakdowns, misfires, and crashes scatter metal across the salt flats, where scavengers and merchants soon gather what remains.\n\nThe dwarf Kravel Koalbeard hires travelers to search the bright expanse and collect the debris. Both racing teams need spare machinery for their next prototypes, so wreckage can return to the teams whose cars left it behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do all these rocket car parts come from?",a="Rocket Car Parts come from crashes, explosions, and mechanical failures at the Mirage Raceway. Gnome and goblin racers push experimental rocket-powered vehicles across the Thousand Needles salt flats until the cars break apart.",al={"why are there parts on the salt flats","rocket car scrap origin","where do the parts come from"},it="origin"},{q="Who buys these salvaged scraps?",a="Merchants such as the dwarf Kravel Koalbeard buy wreckage gathered by travelers. They sell gears, plating, and other parts back to gnomes and goblins, who need materials to repair and improve their racing cars.",al={"who wants rocket car parts","kravel koalbeard rocket parts","who buys the wreckage"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are the parts dangerous to scavenge?",a="The wreckage itself is inert, though metal may bear grim signs of crashes, including severed appendages caught in it. Basilisks, scorched scorpids, and predatory salt vultures prowl the salt flats near the debris.",al={"is it safe to pick up parts","threats while gathering parts"},it="danger"},{q="Do the gnomes and goblins care that the parts are from crashed cars?",a="Gnome and goblin racers readily use recycled parts. They want workable machinery, gears, and plating to build cars fast enough to outrun each other on the track.",al={"do racers care about wreckage","why do goblins reuse junk"}},{q="What are Rocket Car Parts?",a="They are the scattered debris of high-speed racing disasters across the Shimmering Flats. Made up of loose gears, cylinders, twisted metal plates, and salvaged gizmos, these scraps were once bolted to the roaring experimental contraptions built by goblin and gnome speedsters competing at the Mirage Raceway.",al={"what is rocket car parts","rocket car parts lore","what are these parts"},it="identity",add="9a01e74a"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Burnt gears and mangled exhaust assemblies litter the salt flats, reminders of the extremes gnome and goblin engineers reach.",["race:Dwarf"]="Gnomes and goblins focus on the race, while dwarves such as Kravel Koalbeard can profit by scavenging the wreckage left behind."},kw={"engineering","gnome","goblin","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","rocket car parts","salvage","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:1110","npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1105","quest:1104","quest:1176"},src={"Rocket Car Parts","Rocket Car Parts (quest)"}}
E["item:salty-scorpid-venom"] = {t="item",n="Salty Scorpid Venom",z="thousandneedles",s="Across Thousand Needles, Salty Scorpid Venom draws gnomes into a dangerous race for speed. Scorpids on the Shimmering Flats carry the desert floor's mineral salts in their venom, and gnomish racers seek it for fuel.",h="Across Thousand Needles, Salty Scorpid Venom draws gnomes into a dangerous race for speed.",sec={{t="A Volatile Combustion Agent",b="Scorpids on the mineral-rich Shimmering Flats carry salt in their venom. Scorpid Reavers and Scorpid Terrors have absorbed those local salts over generations. Fizzle Brassbolts and other gnomish tinkers prize the caustic venom as a possible additive for high-combustion engine fuel, not for antidotes or ordinary poisons.",sp=0},{t="Fueling the Raceway Rivalry",b="At the Mirage Raceway, gnomes and goblins test ever more dangerous materials in their rocket cars. Fizzle Brassbolts believes boiling down the salted venom, treating it with specialized catalysts, and mixing it into propellant tanks will give his car the fierce heat it needs to outrun goblin racers on the salt pans.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures produce Salty Scorpid Venom?",a="Scorpid Reavers and Scorpid Terrors on the Thousand Needles salt flats produce Salty Scorpid Venom.",al={"who drops salty scorpid venom","where to get scorpid venom","scorpid venom source"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the venom so salty?",a="The scorpids live on the mineral-crusted ground of the Shimmering Flats. Their bodies absorb the dried lakebed's dense salts, giving their venom a high saline concentration.",al={"why is it salty","salt flat venom explanation","scorpid salt lore"}},{q="Who wants this venom and why?",a="Fizzle Brassbolts, a gnome engineer at the Mirage Raceway, seeks the venom for an experimental fuel mixture. He believes it will burn hot enough to propel his rocket car to victory.",al={"who needs scorpid venom","why does fizzle want venom","fizzle brassbolts quest item"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Salty Scorpid Venom?",a="It is a potent, mineral-heavy fluid harvested from the scorpids stalking the Shimmering Flats. The harsh, dried-up salt basin has caused the local scorpid terrors and reavers to develop an unusually salt-saturated venom. While deadly as a natural toxin, its reactive chemical properties make it far more interesting to tinkers as an volatile raw reagent than a simple poison.",al={"what is salty scorpid venom","salty scorpid venom","scorpid venom flat"},it="identity",add="9840b612"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know the risks of turning lethal desert venom into rocket fuel with nega-catalysts, all to shave seconds off a lap.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you see inventors on the Shimmering Flats look beyond petroleum and coal. They test organic toxins as volatile accelerants."},kw={"fizzle brassbolts","mirage raceway","salty scorpid venom","scorpid reaver","scorpid terror","scorpid venom","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:1104","npc:fizzle-brassbolts","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},src={"Salty Scorpid Venom","Salt Flat Venom"}}
E["item:urgent-message"] = {t="item",n="Urgent Message",z="thousandneedles",s="Brave Moonhorn warns Freewind Post that centaur raids are growing across Thousand Needles. Travelers and the roads are in danger.",h="Brave Moonhorn warns Freewind Post that centaur raids are growing across Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Warning from the Heights",b="Near the Great Lift from the Barrens into Thousand Needles, Brave Moonhorn writes Urgent Message. From there, Moonhorn watches the jagged canyons below as centaur tribes renew their raids on Horde travelers.\n\nThe letter is bound for Cliffwatcher Longhorn atop Freewind Post. Moonhorn warns that attackers have grown bolder and strike near important roads. The garrison must prepare for more fighting and watch for the unpredictable Grimtotem clan.",sp=0},{t="Bloodshed on the Canyon Floor",b="At Freewind Post, Urgent Message confirms Cliffwatcher Longhorn's fears. Centaur raiders have ambushed a supply caravan crossing the canyon floor and slaughtered everyone aboard. This is more than a border skirmish.\n\nTauren leaders answer with organized counter-strikes against the tribes. They seek to stop the raids before Freewind Post is cut off from the rest of Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written in the Urgent Message?",a="Urgent Message warns that centaur raids are rising sharply across Thousand Needles. Travelers and roads face immediate danger, and Freewind Post must prepare for war.",al={"what does the letter say","urgent message contents","what is the message about"},it="item"},{q="Who wrote this message and who receives it?",a="Brave Moonhorn wrote Urgent Message near the Great Lift from the Barrens and addressed it to Cliffwatcher Longhorn, commander of Freewind Post.",al={"who wrote urgent message","sender of urgent message","who gets the urgent message"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the centaur attacking supply caravans?",a="The centaur tribes have long contested the arid lands of central Kalimdor with the tauren. They raid caravans on the canyon floor to seize provisions and deny the Horde safe passage through Thousand Needles.",al={"why centaur attacks","centaur motive thousand needles","why do centaurs raid"},it="motive"},{q="What warning does the scout give regarding the Grimtotem?",a="Brave Moonhorn warns the courier to avoid the nearby Grimtotem clan. Its warriors have grown aloof and suspicious toward other tauren.",al={"grimtotem warning","why avoid grimtotem","grimtotem acting strange"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Urgent Message?",a="The Urgent Message is a sealed written dispatch penned by Brave Moonhorn near the border of Thousand Needles. It reports an alarming surge in centaur aggression across the canyon floor, alerting tauren authorities to the growing danger threatening travelers and supply lines in the region.",al={"what is urgent message","urgent message item","urgent dispatch"},it="identity",add="d8ee5ef2"},{q="Why is the Urgent Message needed at Freewind Post?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn oversees the defense of Freewind Post and requires immediate intelligence on enemy movements. The dispatch warns him that centaur marauders have escalated their raids, allowing him to take decisive action before more supply caravans and patrols are ambushed and slaughtered.",al={"why deliver urgent message","who needs urgent message","why cliffwatcher longhorn message"},it="why_wanted",add="1e5b60e5"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Urgent Message shows how fragile Horde supply lines are across southern Kalimdor. Isolated outposts rely on runners and braves to cross hostile land.",["race:Tauren"]="For tauren, the letter recalls their ancient blood feud with the centaur and growing unease about their Grimtotem kin."},kw={"brave moonhorn","centaur","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","great lift","grimtotem","thousand needles","urgent message"},rel={"quest:4542","npc:brave-moonhorn","npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:freewind-post","quest:4841","quest:5064","topic:centaur","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Urgent Message","Message to Freewind Post"}}
E["npc:brave-moonhorn"] = {t="npc",n="Brave Moonhorn",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Barrens' southern border, Brave Moonhorn watches the Great Lift into Thousand Needles. From its heights, he warns travelers of dangers ahead.",h="At the Barrens' southern border, Brave Moonhorn watches the Great Lift into Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="Sentinel of the Lift",b="Brave Moonhorn guards the boundary between the northern plains and the canyonlands. From above Thousand Needles, he watches the canyon floor for threats, especially hostile centaur clans. Travelers often meet him before descending into the needles. He warns them of danger before they step onto the Great Lift's massive platforms.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Shadows",b="Brave Moonhorn distrusts the Grimtotem tauren. He tells traveling Horde allies to keep their distance because the tribe acts erratically and suspiciously around Thousand Needles. To help defend the region, he sends couriers to Freewind Post with warnings for Cliffwatcher Longhorn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Brave Moonhorn?",a="Brave Moonhorn is a tauren warrior and scout watching the approach to the Great Lift between the Barrens and Thousand Needles. He watches for enemy activity and warns passing travelers of nearby hazards.",al={"brave moonhorn role","who is moonhorn","lift tauren guard"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Moonhorn warn against the Grimtotem?",a="Moonhorn warns against the Grimtotem because they act strangely and unpredictably in the surrounding canyon. Though part of the tauren community, their aggressive insularity makes them untrustworthy to guards keeping order along the trail.",al={"grimtotem warning","why avoid grimtotem","moonhorn grimtotem"}},{q="What message does he want delivered to Freewind Post?",a="Moonhorn wants word carried about rising centaur activity in Thousand Needles. He asks dependable Horde runners to deliver the warning to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post.",al={"freewind post message","what is moonhorn's message","message to freewind post lore"},it="wants"},{q="Where is Brave Moonhorn located?",a="Brave Moonhorn stands near the plateau's edge at the top of the Great Lift, on the boundary between the Barrens and Thousand Needles.",al={"where is moonhorn","brave moonhorn location","great lift guard"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Brave Moonhorn on?",a="Brave Moonhorn serves Thunder Bluff and the Horde. Stationed atop the Great Lift between the Barrens and Thousand Needles, he keeps watch over the border and directs traveling Horde adventurers safely into the canyon below.",al={"is brave moonhorn horde","brave moonhorn faction","who does moonhorn serve"},it="side",add="9347caaf"},{q="Why is Brave Moonhorn stationed at the Great Lift?",a="Moonhorn is posted at the precipice of Thousand Needles to guard the descent and monitor nearby dangers. From this vantage, he keeps an eye on centaur aggression and the uneasy movements of the Grimtotem clan, making sure travelers descending into the canyon are properly warned.",al={"why is moonhorn here","what is moonhorn doing at the lift","why is brave moonhorn at the great lift"},it="why_here",add="ff589928"},{q="Who is Brave Moonhorn tied to?",a="Moonhorn answers to the tauren leadership of Thunder Bluff and works closely with Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post. When danger stirs along the canyon routes, Longhorn is the commander he relies upon to receive his scouting reports.",al={"moonhorn allies","who does moonhorn report to","brave moonhorn connections"},it="ties",add="4ac94a87"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Moonhorn guides new Horde arrivals in the canyon toward safety and the fortified heights of Freewind Post.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may recognize Moonhorn's wariness of the Grimtotem as part of the distrust between Cairne Bloodhoof's traditional tribes and the secretive Grimtotem."},kw={"brave moonhorn","centaur","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","great lift","grimtotem","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:4542","subzone:great-lift","subzone:freewind-post","npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","zone:thousandneedles","topic:grimtotem-tribe","topic:centaur","topic:tauren"},src={"Brave Moonhorn"}}
E["npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn"] = {t="npc",n="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Cliffwatcher Longhorn watches over the Horde's isolated hold in Thousand Needles. He directs its defense against the Galak centaur and keeps an eye on the Grimtotem tribe's dealings.",h="At Freewind Post, Cliffwatcher Longhorn watches over the Horde's isolated hold in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Mesas",b="Cliffwatcher Longhorn guards Freewind Post, an isolated settlement atop the rock spires of Thousand Needles. He oversees its daily security and gathers reports from scouts on the canyon floor and nearby ridges. Hostile forces are gathering around the post, so his steady leadership guides its defenses.",sp=0},{t="Centaur Hostility and Grimtotem Intrigue",b="Galak centaur probe Freewind Post's perimeter from the canyon below. Cliffwatcher Longhorn sends adventurers to drive them back and reduce their numbers.\n\nHis concern for the Grimtotem tauren runs deeper still. Their secretive camp lies near the post, and Longhorn distrusts them. He arranges reconnaissance to seize their hidden notes, which reveal treachery within the tribe and Arnak Grimtotem's violent crimes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cliffwatcher Longhorn?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn commands Freewind Post, the Horde outpost in Thousand Needles. He organizes scouts, defense patrols, and responses to nearby threats.",al={"cliffwatcher longhorn info","who is longhorn","freewind post leader"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Cliffwatcher Longhorn?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn stands atop Freewind Post's main mesa in Thousand Needles. Take the lift from the canyon floor, then cross the wooden bridges.",al={"cliffwatcher longhorn location","where is longhorn"},gp=true},{q="Why is Longhorn concerned about the centaur?",a="Scouts such as Brave Moonhorn report a sharp rise in Galak centaur hostility. Longhorn orders strikes to pacify the clan and keep them from overwhelming the approaches to Freewind Post.",al={"why kill centaur","pacify the centaur lore","centaur threat thousand needles"},it="conflict"},{q="What is his interest in the Grimtotem tribe?",a="The Grimtotem live among the Horde, yet act in secret and with malice. Longhorn suspects foul play, so he commissions adventurers to take their hidden notes and learn what they are plotting.",al={"longhorn grimtotem","grimtotem spying reason"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem and why does Longhorn want him?",a="Arnak Grimtotem carried out a violent attack on Freewind Post's inhabitants. Longhorn places a bounty on him so Arnak faces justice for his treachery.",al={"wanted arnak grimtotem","arnak bounty lore"},it="target"},{q="Does Cliffwatcher Longhorn have any family?",a="Yes. Cliffwatcher Longhorn's brother, Nataka Longhorn, is stationed far to the west at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. Duty leaves Cliffwatcher little time to write to him.",al={"longhorn brother","nataka longhorn brother"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Cliffwatcher Longhorn on?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn stands firmly with the Horde and the tauren tribes answering to Thunder Bluff. Stationed atop Freewind Post, he coordinates defense for the settlement, relying on Horde champions to safeguard the canyon roadways below from aggressive centaur clans and the subversive Grimtotem tribe.",al={"cliffwatcher longhorn faction","longhorn horde alliance","who does longhorn serve"},it="side",add="8c33620b"},{q="What does Cliffwatcher Longhorn want?",a="Longhorn wants to maintain security and order throughout Thousand Needles. He seeks to retaliate against hostile Galak centaur bands harassing travelers, uncover whatever secretive plots the local Grimtotem are hatching, and bring rogue threats like Arnak Grimtotem to swift justice.",al={"what does longhorn want","longhorn goal","cliffwatcher longhorn motives"},it="wants",add="d26a5d43"},{q="Why is Cliffwatcher Longhorn here?",a="Longhorn is stationed at Freewind Post as one of its primary overseers and defenders. From this soaring mesa, he monitors reports across the canyon floor, directs Horde scouts, and organizes responses to the dangerous centaur tribes and deceitful Grimtotem who surround the outpost.",al={"why is longhorn in freewind post","why is cliffwatcher longhorn in thousand needles","longhorn freewind post role"},it="why_here",add="e12f4ee3"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see Longhorn's Shu'halo frontier spirit. He watches over contested sacred mesas while facing bitter, unresolved friction with the Grimtotem tribe.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on Freewind Post to help secure supply lines across southern Kalimdor. Longhorn works to hold the Horde's precarious foothold amid hostile centaur territory."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","brave moonhorn","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","galak","grimtotem","nataka longhorn","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:brave-moonhorn","quest:4542","quest:4841","quest:5064","quest:5147","zone:desolace"},src={"Cliffwatcher Longhorn"}}
E["npc:dorn-plainstalker"] = {t="npc",n="Dorn Plainstalker",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker tests travelers who seek to prove their character and fortitude. The tauren elder guides Horde adventurers through rites of faith, endurance, strength, and lore, judging whether they are worthy servants of the Earth Mother and their people.",h="At the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker tests travelers who seek to prove their character and fortitude.",sec={{t="Hermit of the High Cliffs",b="Dorn Plainstalker lives in a shallow cave high on the Weathered Nook’s canyon ridges, apart from Freewind Post. Follow the northern cliffs above the towering mesas to reach his shelter. From this quiet vantage, he keeps ancient customs and judges those who seek guidance in the harsh southern barrens.",sp=0},{t="The Four Trials",b="Dorn Plainstalker guides pilgrims through four tests of a tauren champion: faith, endurance, strength, and lore. The trials ask aspirants to face fear, leap into the unknown, outlast cunning wilderness predators, and reflect on Kalimdor’s sacred history. Only then can they claim their final passage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dorn Plainstalker?",a="Dorn Plainstalker is a tauren elder who lives as a hermit in the Weathered Nook, high above Thousand Needles. He leads traditional rites of passage for aspiring Horde champions.",al={"who is dorn","dorn lore","dorn plainstalker"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Dorn Plainstalker?",a="Dorn Plainstalker lives in a cave at the Weathered Nook. From Freewind Post, head north to the high cliffs bordering the canyon, then follow the ridge east to a ramp that climbs to his mountain sanctuary.",al={"where is dorn","how to reach dorn plainstalker","weathered nook location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are the trials Dorn administers?",a="Dorn Plainstalker oversees four sacred tests: the Test of Faith, Test of Endurance, Test of Strength, and Test of Lore. Completing them proves a traveler’s courage, physical resolve, combat skill, and respect for tradition.",al={"dorn plainstalker quests","test of faith","trials of passage thousand needles"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Test of Faith?",a="The Test of Faith asks a pilgrim to step from a cliff plank into the chasm below. They must trust completely and overcome primal fear.",al={"leap of faith thousand needles","test of faith dorn"}},{q="Why does Dorn live alone in a cave?",a="Dorn Plainstalker follows ascetic tauren spiritual traditions. He lives alone in the heights of the Weathered Nook, away from Freewind Post’s daily trade and defense, where he keeps a quiet place for contemplation and trials.",al={"why is dorn isolated","dorn plainstalker background"},it="why_here"},{q="Is Dorn affiliated with Freewind Post?",a="Dorn Plainstalker lives outside Freewind Post, yet remains loyal to the Horde and the tauren tribes. He aids brave travelers who cross the windswept canyons.",al={"freewind post elder","is dorn horde"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Dorn Plainstalker on?",a="Dorn Plainstalker is loyal to the Horde and his fellow tauren. He welcomes travelers of the Horde into his sanctuary at the Weathered Nook to prove their mettle, guiding them through traditional rites to ensure they possess the strength, faith, and wisdom required to serve the tribes and the broader Horde.",al={"is dorn horde","dorn plainstalker faction","who does dorn serve"},it="side",add="4250a0db"},{q="What does Dorn Plainstalker want?",a="Dorn Plainstalker wants to test the character, endurance, and spirit of champions who journey through Thousand Needles. By overseeing the trials of faith, endurance, strength, and lore, he seeks to prepare worthy adventurers for the harsh challenges of the world and ensure they honor the traditions of the earth.",al={"dorn goals","what does dorn want","dorn plainstalker purpose"},it="wants",add="a0eea52d"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren wandering through Thousand Needles, you can see Dorn Plainstalker continuing nomadic ancestral traditions. His spiritual rites test your balance with the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, you are welcome to face Dorn Plainstalker’s trials. Warriors, hunters, and shamans of every race prove their mettle in Kalimdor’s rugged wilds."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","freewind post","tauren trial","test of endurance","test of faith","test of lore","test of strength","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"subzone:weathered-nook","quest:1149","quest:1150","quest:1151","quest:1152","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren"},src={"Dorn Plainstalker"}}
E["npc:elder-morningdew"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Morningdew",z="thousandneedles",s="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Morningdew greets travelers in Thousand Needles. She offers ancestral wisdom and blessings to those who honor her.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Morningdew greets travelers in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="An Honored Spirit of the Festival",b="In Thousand Needles, Elder Morningdew greets pilgrims during the Lunar Festival as an honored ancestor. Across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms, revered spirits gather to celebrate wisdom, legacy, and peace. She belongs to neither faction and takes no part in mortal conflicts. Travelers who seek her counsel and show respect receive her blessing and a Coin of Ancestry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Morningdew?",a="Elder Morningdew is a night elf ancestral spirit who greets travelers in Thousand Needles during the Lunar Festival.",al={"elder morningdew lore","who is morningdew","morningdew identity"},it="identity"},{q="What is the purpose of seeking her out?",a="Travelers seek Elder Morningdew during the Lunar Festival to honor the ancestors. She gives them a Coin of Ancestry and a blessing of wisdom.",al={"why find elder morningdew","morningdew purpose","lunar festival elder"},it="purpose"},{q="Does she belong to the Alliance or Horde?",a="Elder Morningdew is neutral in mortal politics. Alliance and Horde travelers can approach her peacefully and pay their respects.",al={"is morningdew hostile","elder morningdew faction","can horde talk to morningdew"},it="side"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, honoring elders like Morningdew connects you with the spirits who came before your people.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, honoring ancestral spirits shows your deep respect for the wisdom of those who came before."},kw={"ancestor","elder","elder morningdew","ghost","lunar festival","morningdew","night elf","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:8724","zone:thousandneedles","topic:night-elf"},src={"Elder Morningdew"}}
E["npc:elder-skyseer"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Skyseer",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Elder Skyseer watches over travelers as an ancestor beyond the mortal world. His spirit remains tied to the resting grounds of his people.",h="At Freewind Post, Elder Skyseer watches over travelers as an ancestor beyond the mortal world.",sec={{t="A Spirit of Freewind Post",b="High above Thousand Needles, Elder Skyseer watches over Freewind Post from its mesa. Tauren cross perilous bridges and wooden platforms there, while he keeps watch beyond the mortal veil. Travelers who honor old traditions may receive his blessings and seek the wisdom of past generations.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Ancestral Lands",b="Elder Skyseer’s spirit often appears among the wind-carved needles. He belongs to the line of tauren ancestors honored on Mulgore’s sacred soil, where the ancestral spirits of Red Rocks watch over the tribes. Through remembrance and ritual, those ancestors guide future generations. His presence shows how thin the veil remains between the living and the dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Skyseer?",a="Elder Skyseer watches over Freewind Post in Thousand Needles as an ancestral tauren spirit. He offers guidance to travelers who seek him.",al={"elder skyseer lore","who is skyseer","skyseer npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Elder Skyseer a ghost?",a="Elder Skyseer passed from the mortal world and remains as an ancient ancestor. Tauren honor their forebears, and certain elders linger or return in spirit to guide the living.",al={"why is skyseer dead","is elder skyseer dead","ghost tauren freewind"},it="history"},{q="What is his connection to Mulgore?",a="Elder Skyseer belongs to the tauren people, whose homeland is Mulgore. There, the ancestral spirits of Red Rocks watch over the tribes. His spirit appears at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",al={"skyseer red rocks","skyseer mulgore connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where can I find Elder Skyseer?",a="Elder Skyseer watches over Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, atop its mesa settlement high above the canyon floor.",al={"elder skyseer location","find skyseer","where is skyseer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Skyseer on?",a="Elder Skyseer takes no side in the wars of the living. Lingering as an ancestral tauren spirit above the windswept mesas of Freewind Post, he offers ancestral guidance and wisdom from beyond the grave to any traveler, Horde or Alliance, who honors him.",al={"skyseer faction","is elder skyseer horde","skyseer allegiances"},it="side",add="e54499fb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, meeting Elder Skyseer brings you into communion with an ancestor. His presence reflects the reverence taught at Red Rocks and across Mulgore’s plains.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you speak with the elements and spirits. You recognize the wisdom of ancestors who continue to watch over the living."},kw={"ancestor","elder skyseer","freewind post","red rocks","tauren ghost","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:red-rocks","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren","quest:8682"},src={"Elder Skyseer"}}
E["npc:elu"] = {t="npc",n="Elu",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Elu tends the mounts and waits to begin wind rider training. He hopes to fly and asks Horde travelers to bring back wild wyvern eggs from nearby roosts.",h="At Freewind Post, Elu tends the mounts and waits to begin wind rider training.",sec={{t="An Eager Apprentice",b="At Freewind Post, Elu cares for the aerial mounts and dreams of flying. The young tauren hopes to join the master wind riders who patrol Kalimdor’s mesas. Before training begins, he must prove himself by bringing fresh wyvern stock to the roost. So he sends capable travelers to Highperch for intact eggs from the fierce wild wyverns nesting there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elu?",a="Elu is a tauren apprentice wind rider at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He helps secure and raise new mounts for the Horde’s aerial network.",al={"elu freewind post","who is elu","tauren apprentice elu"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Elu need wyvern eggs?",a="Elu needs wyvern eggs to replenish the master wind riders’ stable. The young wyverns can be trained and bonded as mounts for the Horde.",al={"why wyvern eggs","elu wyvern quest","elu quest goal"},it="wants"},{q="Where does Elu send adventurers to find eggs?",a="Elu sends travelers to Highperch, a mesa in western Thousand Needles where wild wyverns fiercely guard their nests.",al={"where are wyvern eggs","where is highperch","elu egg location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elu on?",a="Elu is loyal to the Horde and his fellow tauren. Stationed high atop the bluffs of Freewind Post, he works alongside the master wind riders of the Horde to train and supply the aerial steeds vital for traveling across Kalimdor.",al={"elu faction","is elu horde","who does elu serve"},it="side",add="74f15e75"},{q="Why is Elu at Freewind Post?",a="Elu serves as an apprentice wind rider at Freewind Post. He remains here to aid the flight masters and earn his place in the sky, tasked with securing fresh wyverns from the high perches of Thousand Needles so they can be trained for Horde riders.",al={"why is elu in thousand needles","elu freewind post","elu purpose"},it="why_here",add="3d25520c"},{q="Who is Elu tied to?",a="Elu is an apprentice to the master wind riders of the Horde. He answers to the trainers and beast handlers who raise Kalimdor's winged wyverns, working under their guidance in hopes of beginning his own formal training as a wind rider.",al={"elu master","who does elu work for","elu wind riders"},it="ties",add="c552be8c"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, helping Elu supports a fellow tribesman learning to handle wyverns above your ancestral canyon lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, gathering wyvern eggs for Elu strengthens the Horde’s courier and transport network. It keeps remote outposts across Kalimdor connected by air."},kw={"elu","freewind post","highperch","thousand needles","wind rider","wyvern","wyvern eggs"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","quest:4767","subzone:highperch","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Elu"}}
E["npc:fizzle-brassbolts"] = {t="npc",n="Fizzle Brassbolts",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Fizzle Brassbolts works on the salt flats of Thousand Needles. He and Pozzik founded the raceway to pit gnomish precision against goblin ingenuity in rocket car races. Fizzle seeks parts, fuel, and desert reagents for his team.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Fizzle Brassbolts works on the salt flats of Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Matter of Principle and Pistons",b="Fizzle Brassbolts came to the Shimmering Flats to prove gnomish craftsmanship superior to goblin tinkering. With the goblin engineer Pozzik, he laid out the Mirage Raceway. Race cars, pit crews, and spectators soon filled the basin.",sp=0},{t="Tinkering on the Flats",b="The dry salt beds keep Fizzle improvising. He tests mixtures made with local creature venom and contracts travelers to find replacement mechanical parts. His aim is to keep his driver's wheels turning faster than any goblin contraption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Fizzle Brassbolts?",a="Fizzle Brassbolts leads the gnomish racing crew at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles. He is a master gnomish engineer.",al={"who is fizzle","fizzle brassbolts lore","gnome at raceway"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Fizzle come to the Shimmering Flats?",a="Fizzle came to the Shimmering Flats to settle a technical debate with the goblin engineer Pozzik over whose racecars have superior engineering. Together they established the Mirage Raceway, where their rocket cars compete head-to-head on the flat salt basin.",al={"why is fizzle here","raceway purpose","why raceway built"},it="why_here"},{q="Who are the Brassbolts brothers?",a="Fizzle and his brother Wizzle Brassbolts run the gnomish racing team at the Mirage Raceway. Their new rocket car is so fast that its pilots keep crashing, so they asked their friend Pilot Longbeard in Ironforge for siege engine crash helmets.",al={"brassbolts brothers","wizzle brassbolts","fizzle brother"}},{q="Why does Fizzle need creature venom for race cars?",a="Fizzle tests local reagents to make engine fluids, additives, and accelerants that might give his rocket cars an edge over Pozzik's machines.",al={"salt flat venom quest","venom racing fuel","why does he need venom"},it="motive"},{q="Does Fizzle fight against the goblins?",a="Fizzle does not fight the goblins with weapons. He and Pozzik maintain an uneasy, neutral truce at the raceway so they can focus on high-speed competition.",al={"is fizzle hostile to goblins","fizzle pozzik fight"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Pilot Longbeard?",a="Pilot Longbeard is a dwarven siege engine pilot with the Ironforge Siege Brigade. He is a friend of the Brassbolts brothers and shares their fondness for dangerous machinery.",al={"pilot longbeard connection","fizzle pilot friend"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Fizzle Brassbolts on?",a="Fizzle Brassbolts represents the gnomes and their racing team at the Mirage Raceway. Neutral toward both Alliance and Horde travelers, here on the Shimmering Flats he maintains a functional working relationship with goblin engineers like Pozzik. While fiercely loyal to proving gnomish engineering superior to that of the goblins, their rivalry is focused on the Mirage Raceway rather than open warfare.",al={"is fizzle alliance","fizzle brassbolts faction","who does fizzle work for"},it="side",add="092966e5"},{q="What does Fizzle Brassbolts want?",a="Fizzle wants nothing more than to prove absolute gnomish engineering supremacy over goblin technology. To that end, he co-founded the Mirage Raceway alongside his goblin rival Pozzik. He focuses entirely on developing faster rocket cars, procuring exotic fuel ingredients like the salty venom of the Shimmering Flats scorpids, and beating the goblin team across the salt flats.",al={"what does fizzle want","fizzle brassbolts goal","why is fizzle racing"},it="wants",add="4ec804ad"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you carry Gnomeregan's honor into the desert, seeking to prove gnomish precision outperforms goblin recklessness.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate Fizzle's efforts to improve rocket propulsion and draw up advanced automotive designs in harsh desert conditions.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance wanderer, you can find a friendly face and mechanical work with Fizzle in the neutral speed zone as you travel south toward Tanaris."},kw={"brassbolts","fizzle","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","npc:pozzik","quest:1104","zone:thousandneedles","npc:pilot-longbeard","topic:gnome","topic:goblin","zone:tanaris"},src={"Fizzle Brassbolts"}}
E["npc:hagar-lightninghoof"] = {t="npc",n="Hagar Lightninghoof",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof investigates rumors of an unusual egg hidden deep in the canyon. Wind serpents guard it fiercely, and he wants to learn what lies within.",h="At Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof investigates rumors of an unusual egg hidden deep in the canyon.",sec={{t="The Strange Clutch",b="Hagar Lightninghoof hears reports of an unnatural egg in a cavern below Freewind Post. Wind serpents guard the nest with unusual ferocity, keeping curious scouts away. So Hagar seeks an adventurer bold enough to brave their den and bring back the egg. He hopes to study it firsthand and learn what creature inspires such fierce protection from the canyon’s natural predators.",sp=0},{t="A Myth Hatched",b="The egg reaches Freewind Post and hatches before Hagar Lightninghoof. A young wind serpent emerges, resembling Arikara, the revered spirit of vengeance in tauren folklore. Hagar recognizes the creature’s weight in tauren culture and spiritual life. Then he sends the traveler to consult the elder Motega Firemane.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Hagar Lightninghoof?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof is a tauren scout at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He investigates reports of unusual wildlife, including an egg deep in a nearby cavern.",al={"who is hagar","hagar lightninghoof role","hagar lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Hagar Lightninghoof be found?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof can be found atop Freewind Post, the central Horde outpost perched on the massive rock needles of central Thousand Needles.",al={"where is hagar","hagar lightninghoof location","freewind post hagar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the 'alien egg' Hagar is looking for?",a="The alien egg is an unusual egg guarded by wind serpents in a cavern below. Hagar asks an adventurer to retrieve it so he can study it.",al={"alien egg","what is the egg","wind serpent egg"},sp=1,it="wants"},{q="Who does Hagar consult about the egg?",a="Hagar sends the adventurer to speak with Motega Firemane, an elder at Freewind Post with deeper wisdom about tauren traditions.",al={"who do i turn serpent wild into","hagar follow up quest","where to go after hagar"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Hagar Lightninghoof on?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof is loyal to the Horde and his fellow tauren. Stationed atop the towering spires of Freewind Post, he entrusts his tasks solely to Horde champions who prove capable of braving the dangerous canyons below.",al={"hagar lightninghoof faction","is hagar horde"},it="side",add="d173f224"},{q="Why is Hagar Lightninghoof here in Freewind Post?",a="Hagar traveled to Thousand Needles after hearing rumors of a peculiar, alien egg spotted in the wind serpent nests. Intrigued by the strange find, he made his camp at Freewind Post to find someone bold enough to retrieve it past the serpent guards.",al={"why is hagar here","why did hagar come to thousand needles"},it="why_here",add="c809f2c7"},{q="Who is Hagar Lightninghoof tied to?",a="Hagar works alongside the tauren defenders of Freewind Post and consults closely with Motega Firemane. When his investigations reveal matters steeped in ancient tauren legends and sacred omens, it is Motega he turns to for guidance.",al={"hagar ties","who does hagar work with"},it="ties",add="a74332ba"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, helping Hagar brings an ancient legend into the present: Arikara, the winged embodiment of vengeance, lives in the canyons below.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior, you can help Hagar reach perilous dens that ordinary scouts cannot safely enter."},kw={"alien egg","arikara","freewind post","hagar","lightninghoof","motega firemane","thousand needles","wind serpent"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","quest:4821","quest:4865","npc:motega-firemane","quest:5088","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Hagar Lightninghoof"}}
E["npc:kanati-greycloud"] = {t="npc",n="Kanati Greycloud",z="thousandneedles",s="At Whitereach Post, Kanati Greycloud and his companions stand against the Galak centaur. The tauren hunters watch western Thousand Needles as the centaur threat continues.",h="At Whitereach Post, Kanati Greycloud and his companions stand against the Galak centaur.",sec={{t="A Precarious Perch",b="Kanati Greycloud keeps camp at Whitereach Post, high on the sandstone spires of western Thousand Needles. Game is plentiful there, and the view stretches across the canyon. Below, Galak warbands contest the arid flats. Kanati and the other tauren hunters watch the canyon floor and defend the post from nearby marauders.",sp=0},{t="Centaur Ambush",b="Orders pass between Galak camps, calling for Kanati Greycloud and his companions to be assassinated. The centaur mean to destroy Whitereach Post and its defenders. Travelers can intercept the messengers carrying those orders, then stand with Kanati when Galak raiders descend on the mesa to attack the hunters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kanati Greycloud?",a="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren hunter who keeps camp at Whitereach Post in western Thousand Needles. He defends the post against local threats.",al={"who is kanati","kanati greycloud lore","whitereach post tauren"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Kanati Greycloud?",a="Find Kanati at Whitereach Post, a tauren encampment on the northern bluffs in western Thousand Needles.",al={"kanati location","where is kanati","where is greycloud"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Galak centaur trying to kill him?",a="The Galak centaur seek dominance over the canyons and target Horde outposts. Orders between their camps call for Kanati's assassination and the breaking of Whitereach Post's defenses.",al={"why centaur attack kanati","galak assassination plot","protect kanati why"}},{q="Whose side is Kanati Greycloud on?",a="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren hunter loyal to the Horde. He welcomes travelers of the Horde who visit Whitereach Post and relies on them to help defend his camp from hostile threats in the canyon.",al={"kanati faction","is kanati horde","kanati alliance or horde"},it="side",add="35c73e38"},{q="What does Kanati Greycloud want?",a="Kanati simply wants to maintain his hunting camp in peace and ensure his companions survive. Because the local Galak centaur seek to drive out or slaughter all intruders, his primary concern is defending against their assassination attempts.",al={"what does kanati need","kanati greycloud goals","why help kanati"},it="wants",add="cf857b32"},{q="Why is Kanati Greycloud here?",a="Kanati established a hunting camp at Whitereach Post alongside his companions to hunt the game of Thousand Needles. Unfortunately, setting up camp in the canyon placed him squarely in the territory contested by the hostile Galak centaur.",al={"why is kanati at whitereach post","what is kanati doing here","kanati greycloud purpose"},it="why_here",add="10a1bee5"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren crossing Thousand Needles, you can help Kanati defend your kin at Whitereach Post against the centaur, their ancient enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you rely on Whitereach Post's view over the needle canyons. Keeping Kanati alive helps Horde scouts watch centaur troop movements."},kw={"assassination plot","centaur","galak","greycloud","kanati","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","quest:4881","quest:4966","topic:centaur","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Kanati Greycloud"}}
E["npc:kravel-koalbeard"] = {t="npc",n="Kravel Koalbeard",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, Kravel Koalbeard sees profit in the rivalry between gnome and goblin racers. He seeks coin through scavenged machine parts, blackmail, and schemes to sway race results.",h="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, Kravel Koalbeard sees profit in the rivalry between gnome and...",sec={{t="A Con Artist in the Flats",b="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard watches the crowds and crews for a chance to profit. He works among the raceway encampment, offering contracts and favors for motives rarely clean. The rivalry between gnome and goblin engineers gives him openings for extortion, sabotage, and theft.",sp=0},{t="Rigging the Track",b="Kravel Koalbeard’s schemes reach beyond salvage on the salt flats. He sends willing adventurers to spread rumors, carry out blackmail, and get pit crews drunk before a race.\n\nHe may ply goblin mechanics with strong spirits or serve strong drinks to gnomish pilots. On race day, any underhanded trick may help fill his purse.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kravel Koalbeard?",a="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, Kravel Koalbeard schemes to profit from the rivalry between gnomes and goblins. He makes coin through salvage, race-fixing, and extortion.",al={"who is kravel","kravel koalbeard identity","mirage raceway dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="What does Kravel Koalbeard do at the Mirage Raceway?",a="Kravel hires travelers at the Mirage Raceway for underhanded errands. They collect rocket car parts, seek blackmail material, and get mechanics or pilots drunk to sway race results.",al={"kravel purpose","what does kravel want","kravel schemes"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Kravel trying to get race crews drunk?",a="Kravel gets race crews drunk to influence races on which he wagers heavily. He targets gnomes or goblins according to which outcome promises the most profit.",al={"get the gnomes drunk quest","get the goblins drunk","kravel sabotage"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Kravel Koalbeard be found?",a="Kravel Koalbeard can be found around the pit camps at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles.",al={"kravel location","where is kravel","kravel thousand needles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Kravel have ties outside Thousand Needles?",a="Yes. Kravel’s dealings reach the goblin ports of Ratchet and Booty Bay. They include contacts tied to Ratchet’s Wharfmaster Dizzywig, rumormongers, and exotic brews from Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"kravel booty bay","kravel connections"},it="ties"},{q="Will Kravel work with both Alliance and Horde?",a="Kravel values gold above faction loyalty and employs both Alliance and Horde adventurers at the Mirage Raceway.",al={"is kravel alliance only","can horde talk to kravel"},it="side"},{q="What does Kravel Koalbeard want?",a="Kravel is entirely driven by profit and self-interest. He seeks to line his pockets through any scheme available out on the Shimmering Flats, from running parts and peddling favors to orchestrating blackmail. His most audacious ambition is manipulating the outcome of the Mirage Raceway itself, plotting to sabotage and rig the contests by keeping the pit crews and drivers thoroughly inebriated.",al={"what does kravel want","kravel koalbeard goals","kravel motives"},it="wants",add="33aea695"},{q="Why is Kravel Koalbeard out in Thousand Needles?",a="The Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats is a lawless hive of high-stakes gambling, fierce rivalry, and reckless engineering, making it prime hunting ground for a con artist. Kravel set up camp alongside the competing gnomes and goblins because their bitter obsession with beating one another leaves them blind to opportunists and easy marks for his schemes.",al={"why is kravel here","why is kravel at mirage raceway","kravel shimmer flats"},it="why_here",add="97572808"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Kravel is a rogue and swindler, unlike Ironforge’s honest miners, prospectors, and mountaineers. His conduct brings shame to traditional dwarven values.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, watch your drinks and blueprints around Kravel. He is as ready to drug gnomish pilots as to sabotage their machines.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you may recognize Kravel’s methods: theft, sabotage, blackmail, and manipulating greedy targets from the shadows."},kw={"blackmail","koalbeard","kravel","mirage raceway","rocket car","sabotage","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1110","quest:1492","subzone:booty-bay","topic:dwarf","topic:gnome","topic:goblin"},src={"Kravel Koalbeard"}}
E["npc:lakota-windsong"] = {t="npc",n="Lakota Windsong",z="thousandneedles",s="At Darkcloud Pinnacle, Lakota Windsong waits under Grimtotem guard. Arnak Grimtotem took her after she refused his proposal.",h="At Darkcloud Pinnacle, Lakota Windsong waits under Grimtotem guard.",sec={{t="A Deadly Courtship",b="Not long after the Third War, Arnak Grimtotem began courting Lakota Windsong. She refused him and would not join his clan, but Arnak would not accept her answer. Under cover of night, he returned and killed Lakota's brother when he tried to stop him. Then Arnak carried Lakota into the jagged heights of Thousand Needles. Now she is held high above the canyon floor at Darkcloud Pinnacle, under heavy guard. Arnak still insists she will be his bride.",sp=0},{t="Descent to Safety",b="Grimtotem bandits surround Lakota, and she cannot descend the cliffs alone. An escort must guide her across the suspension bridges and down the winding paths to the canyon basin. From the base of Darkcloud Pinnacle, Lakota flees toward Freewind Post. There she tells Thalia Amberhide and the defenders at the post of her rescue.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Lakota Windsong being held at Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="Lakota is held at Darkcloud Pinnacle because she refused Arnak Grimtotem's marriage proposal. He killed her brother and abducted her to the Grimtotem stronghold, hoping to force her hand.",al={"why is lakota captured","who kidnapped lakota","why is lakota in darkcloud pinnacle"},it="why_here"},{q="Where does Lakota go once she is rescued?",a="After reaching the base of Darkcloud Pinnacle, Lakota makes her way to Freewind Post. There she finds refuge among the Horde defenders and reports her ordeal to Thalia Amberhide.",al={"where does lakota run","where does she go after escort","lakota destination"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Arnak Grimtotem is a violent warrior of the treacherous Grimtotem clan. When Lakota refused to marry him, he murdered her brother and abducted her.",al={"who is arnak","who kidnapped her","arnak lore"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Lakota Windsong?",a="Lakota Windsong is a tauren woman held captive atop Darkcloud Pinnacle. When Arnak Grimtotem sought her hand in marriage, Lakota refused him. Enraged by her rejection, Arnak murdered her brother and dragged her away to the Grimtotem stronghold in Thousand Needles, intending to force the union upon her against her will.",al={"lakota windsong who","who is lakota","lakota identity"},it="identity",add="e2861ac8"},{q="Whose side is Lakota Windsong on?",a="Lakota is aligned with the peaceful tauren of the Horde and looks to the braves at Freewind Post for protection. She holds deep enmity toward the Grimtotem clan, who brutally took her brother's life and abducted her.",al={"lakota windsong faction","is lakota horde","lakota allegiance"},it="side",add="412850e2"},{q="What does Lakota Windsong want?",a="Lakota desires only to escape Darkcloud Pinnacle and reach safety away from the Grimtotem bandits. With her brother slain defending her, she relies on someone bold enough to fight past her captors and guide her safely down the winding paths toward Freewind Post.",al={"lakota windsong goal","what does lakota need","lakota desires"},it="wants",add="2c16a924"},{q="Who is Lakota Windsong tied to?",a="Lakota was fiercely protected by her brother, who lost his life attempting to defend her from Arnak Grimtotem. She also places her trust in Thalia Amberhide and the defenders stationed at Freewind Post.",al={"lakota family","lakota connections","who is lakota related to"},it="ties",add="3261173c"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the Grimtotem's treachery and their defiance of Cairne Bloodhoof's leadership, which often turns violent.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you strike a blow against Grimtotem dominance over Thousand Needles when you rescue Lakota. You also help keep the way safe for travelers resting at Freewind Post."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","darkcloud pinnacle","free at last","freewind post","lakota windsong","thalia amberhide","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:4904","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","npc:thalia-amberhide","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Lakota Windsong"}}
E["npc:mad-magus-tirth"] = {t="npc",n="Magus Tirth",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Magus Tirth tends chickens, serves drinks, and stakes books on the races. The human wizard lives on the Shimmering Flats, where he torments his apprentice and has wagered away valuable works.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Magus Tirth tends chickens, serves drinks, and stakes books on the races.",sec={{t="A Wizard in the Dust",b="Magus Tirth makes his home beside the roaring Shimmering Flats. Mages of his skill often study in Dalaran or Stormwind, but he sells chickens and drinks to passersby. He gambles and watches the rocket cars race.\n\nHis apprentice, 'Plucky' Johnson, lives under a curse that has turned him into a chicken. Beneath Tirth’s odd habits lies true arcane mastery. He wrote esoteric books on magical power, then lost them in reckless wagers at the speedway.",sp=0},{t="Rituals and Debts",b="Magus Tirth once owned a manual called 'Rituals of Power', sought by practicing mages. Gambling debts at the Mirage Raceway drove him to sell his own work to an agent of the Scarlet Crusade. The sale settled his losses.\n\nNow apprentices and seekers of knowledge must track the book into hostile territory.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Magus Tirth out in the desert?",a="Magus Tirth lives on the Shimmering Flats beside the Mirage Raceway, drawn by its spectacle and gambling. He watches the gnome and goblin racers, sells chickens, and indulges his vices instead of pursuing a scholarly life in a major city.",al={"why is tirth here","magus tirth shimmering flats","tirth location"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is the chicken next to him?",a="The chicken beside Magus Tirth is 'Plucky' Johnson, his apprentice. Tirth cursed Johnson into chicken form and can no longer remember why, though he is sure the little ingrate deserved it.",al={"who is plucky","plucky johnson","tirth chicken apprentice"},it="ties"},{q="What is the book Rituals of Power?",a="'Rituals of Power' is an advanced treatise on arcane energy written by Magus Tirth. Mages use it to advance their craft, but Tirth sold his copy to pay his racing debts.",al={"rituals of power","tirth book","mage quest book"}},{q="Why is his book difficult to obtain?",a="Magus Tirth no longer has his copy of 'Rituals of Power'. Mages seeking it must follow up on his account of how he parted with the tome.",al={"who has rituals of power","tirth debts","scarlet crusade book"}},{q="Who is Magus Tirth?",a="Magus Tirth is an eccentric human spellcaster residing at the Mirage Raceway out on the Shimmering Flats. Though clearly knowledgeable in esoteric arcane lore—having penned a notable magical tome titled Rituals of Power—he now spends his days peddling Ancona chickens, drinking and gambling on the races.",al={"who is mad magus tirth","who is tirth","magus tirth lore"},it="identity",add="8056ee12"},{q="Whose side is Magus Tirth on?",a="Magus Tirth remains strictly neutral. He makes his living out on the salt flats of the Shimmering Flats alongside goblin and gnome engineers, happily offering his wares and magical counsel to travelers of both the Alliance and the Horde without taking part in their wider war.",al={"is magus tirth alliance or horde","tirth faction","is magus tirth neutral"},it="side",add="f085518f"},{q="What does Magus Tirth want?",a="Beyond scraping together coin from race spectators by selling Ancona chickens, Tirth mostly wants a fresh mug of ale and hot tips on the next race. He once sought quick money to pay off his steep gambling debts, which led him to sell away his own scholarly research.",al={"what does tirth want","magus tirth motives","why is tirth selling chickens"},it="wants",add="3482f0bf"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can study Magus Tirth’s treatise 'Rituals of Power' to deepen your understanding of arcane power."},kw={"ancona chicken","magus tirth","mirage raceway","plucky","plucky johnson","rituals of power","shimmering flats","thousand needles","tirth"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1950","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Magus Tirth"}}
E["npc:motega-firemane"] = {t="npc",n="Motega Firemane",z="thousandneedles",s="At Whitereach Post, Motega Firemane studies the beasts of Thousand Needles. A serpent spirit’s vengeance and his young assistant’s mishaps keep drawing him from his work.",h="At Whitereach Post, Motega Firemane studies the beasts of Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="Scholar of the Canyons",b="Motega Firemane came south to Thousand Needles four years after the Third War. He studies the beasts that survive among its towering mesas. His young assistant, Pao'ka Swiftmountain, came with him, though Pao'ka’s protective father had been reluctant to let him leave Mulgore. Motega made camp at Whitereach Post with Kanati Greycloud. He hoped to observe nature in peace, but dangers on the canyon floor often force him to fight for survival.",sp=0},{t="The Wrath of Arikara",b="Word from Freewind Post brought news that Arikara had returned to the canyons. The fearsome winged serpent spirit sought vengeance against Cairne Bloodhoof. Motega could not understand the spirit’s grudge against the High Chieftain, but moved quickly to protect the Horde.\n\nHe sent scouts to gather Incendia agave from the canyon basin and carry it to Elder Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff. She enchanted the plant into sacred powder. Hunters used it to summon and slay Arikara, then brought the serpent’s hide back to Whitereach Post as proof that Cairne was safe.",sp=1},{t="Guardian of Whitereach",b="Galak centaur near Whitereach Post kept probing the camp. They even plotted to assassinate Kanati Greycloud and his followers. Then young Pao'ka wandered away from the campfire and disappeared into the wyvern-filled heights of Highperch. Motega was frustrated by the young brave’s carelessness, but relieved when Horde travelers brought him back alive.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Motega Firemane?",a="Motega Firemane studies the wildlife of Thousand Needles from Whitereach Post. He came to the canyons with other braves and his assistant, Pao'ka Swiftmountain.",al={"motega firemane lore","who is motega","whitereach motega"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Motega Firemane be found?",a="You can find Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post, a small Horde campsite on the road in northwestern Thousand Needles near Camp E'thok.",al={"motega location","where is motega firemane","motega firemane map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Motega concerned about Arikara?",a="Arikara is a vengeful serpent spirit who appeared in Thousand Needles to target Cairne Bloodhoof. Motega does not understand the spirit’s grudge, but takes the threat seriously and directs hunters to summon and slay it.",al={"who is arikara","why kill arikara","arikara cairne"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="What role does Magatha Grimtotem play in Motega's plans?",a="Motega sends scouts to gather Incendia agave and carry it to Magatha Grimtotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Magatha enchants the plant into sacred powder that can summon Arikara.",al={"magatha incendia powder","motega and magatha","sacred fire quest lore"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What happened to Motega's companion, Pao'ka?",a="Pao'ka Swiftmountain wandered into the dangerous wyvern roosts of Highperch and became lost. Motega feared for him, especially since Pao'ka’s father had been reluctant to let him make the journey. Travelers brought him safely back to Whitereach Post.",al={"pao'ka swiftmountain","missing tauren highperch","homeward bound quest"},sp=1},{q="What other dangers does Whitereach Post face?",a="The nearby Galak centaur threaten Whitereach Post with ambushes and plots to assassinate Kanati Greycloud and the other tauren there. Rogue spirits and predators also threaten the camp.",al={"whitereach post threats","centaur at whitereach","galak centaur plot"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Motega Firemane on?",a="Motega Firemane is loyal to the tauren and the Horde. Stationed at Whitereach Post alongside Kanati Greycloud, he cooperates closely with Horde travelers and looks out for the interests of Cairne Bloodhoof and the tribes under Thunder Bluff's banner.",al={"motega firemane faction","motega firemane horde or alliance","is motega horde"},it="side",add="ca68f68f"},{q="What does Motega Firemane want?",a="Motega is primarily focused on studying the unique wildlife of Thousand Needles while keeping an eye on his young companion, Pao'ka Swiftmountain. However, threats to Thunder Bluff quickly take priority. When warned of the vengeful wind serpent Arikara, he seeks to summon and destroy the beast before it can endanger Cairne Bloodhoof.",al={"what does motega want","motega firemane goals","what is motega trying to do"},it="wants",add="8b7dc2d8"},{q="Why is Motega Firemane here?",a="Motega traveled down into Thousand Needles to observe and study the exotic beasts native to the canyon floor and surrounding mesas. Whitereach Post serves as a base camp for his research, though local troubles—from lost companions to menacing mythical serpents—often pull him away from his scholarly pursuits.",al={"why is motega in thousand needles","what brought motega to whitereach post","motega firemane purpose"},it="why_here",add="12cba981"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see Motega’s work at a research camp in Kalimdor’s wilds. He also helps protect Cairne Bloodhoof from spiritual threats.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share Motega’s respect for nature and devotion to Cairne Bloodhoof. He studies the Earth Mother’s creatures and defends his tribe from ancient spirits.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you share Motega’s reliance on skilled trackers. They gather canyon plants, follow wyverns in Highperch, and track the mighty spirit Arikara."},kw={"arikara","cairne bloodhoof","kanati greycloud","magatha grimtotem","motega firemane","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain","npc:kanati-greycloud","npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","subzone:highperch","npc:hagar-lightninghoof"},src={"Motega Firemane"}}
E["npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain"] = {t="npc",n="Pao'ka Swiftmountain",z="thousandneedles",s="Among Highperch's cliffs, Pao'ka Swiftmountain is trapped by the wyverns he came to study. He traveled south with Motega Firemane, but curiosity brought him too near their nesting grounds.",h="Among Highperch's cliffs, Pao'ka Swiftmountain is trapped by the wyverns he came to study.",sec={{t="A Naturalist in Trouble",b="Pao'ka came to Thousand Needles with Motega Firemane to study the canyon beasts. His father feared the journey was too perilous, and now Pao'ka's plight has proved him right.\n\nThe young scholar followed a mountain trail behind a solitary tauren totem, drawn by Highperch's wyverns. The territorial beasts drove him into the crags. Now he is trapped and terrified, with swooping wyverns barring his way back to Whitereach Post.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pao'ka Swiftmountain?",a="Pao'ka is a young tauren scholar who came to Thousand Needles with Motega Firemane to study the region's wildlife. Territorial wyverns have trapped him on Highperch.",al={"who is pao'ka","paoka swiftmountain","who is the tauren at highperch"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Pao'ka Swiftmountain be found?",a="Pao'ka is stranded atop Highperch in Thousand Needles. A narrow path climbs the mountainside behind a towering tauren totem near the cliffs and leads to the wyvern roosts.",al={"where is paoka","highperch path","how to find paoka"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is he hiding in Highperch?",a="Pao'ka's fascination with wyverns brought him too close to one of their nests. The angry beasts drove him away and blocked his retreat, leaving him in hiding for several days.",al={"why is paoka trapped","why did wyverns attack paoka"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after you help him escape?",a="After you lead Pao'ka safely out of the nesting grounds, he flees to Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post. He hopes his mentor will keep the blunder from his father.",al={"homeward bound outcome","does paoka make it back"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Pao'ka Swiftmountain on?",a="Pao'ka belongs to the Horde. He is a young tauren naturalist who traveled into the canyon under the guidance of elders from his people, relying on Horde champions to help him navigate the dangers of Thousand Needles.",al={"paoka swiftmountain faction","is paoka horde","paoka swiftmountain side"},it="side",add="3733bdd0"},{q="What does Pao'ka Swiftmountain want?",a="Pao'ka wants safe escort out of Highperch and back to Whitereach Post without facing his mentor's wrath. He ventured up into the cliffs eager to study the wild wyverns, but after disturbing a nest and getting chased into hiding, his primary desire is simply to escape with his life and avoid being sent home to his father in disgrace.",al={"paoka goal","what does paoka want","paoka swiftmountain motive"},it="wants",add="ca840f79"},{q="Who is Pao'ka Swiftmountain tied to?",a="Pao'ka is under the mentorship of Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post, who convinced Pao'ka's hesitant father to allow the youth out into the wild to study native beasts. Pao'ka dreads disappointing Motega or proving his protective father right by failing his expedition.",al={"paoka swiftmountain connections","who does paoka know","paoka mentor"},it="ties",add="29fbd111"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep Pao'ka alive and preserve strong ties with the elders at Whitereach Post. He belongs to a new generation of tauren scholars exploring Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know wyverns are deeply revered as allies and faithful mounts. Pao'ka's poorly planned intrusion is embarrassing and dangerous."},kw={"highperch","homeward bound","motega firemane","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","whitereach post","wyverns"},rel={"subzone:highperch","quest:4770","npc:motega-firemane","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Pao'ka Swiftmountain"}}
E["npc:parqual-fintallas"] = {t="npc",n="Parqual Fintallas",z="thousandneedles",s="In the Undercity's Apothecarium, Parqual Fintallas keeps his love of Lordaeron's history. Though once human, he now lives among the Forsaken and greets travelers with courtesy, sharing his deep knowledge of ancient lore.",h="In the Undercity's Apothecarium, Parqual Fintallas keeps his love of Lordaeron's history.",sec={{t="Scholar of Lost Lordaeron",b="Parqual studied Lordaeron's history as a respected human scholar, surrounded by the kingdom's records. The plague of undeath killed him and raised him among its many victims. Under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, he eventually broke free. Many Forsaken embrace cold pragmatism and turn from their former lives. Parqual keeps his scholarly passion and pleasant manners, though the knowledge he seeks has changed since his human life.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of Ancient Lore",b="Parqual lives among the bubbling vats and alchemists of the Undercity's Apothecarium. Its grim surroundings do not lessen his knowledge of Azeroth's history. Travelers facing difficult trials of the mind, including the elusive Test of Lore, are sent to him. He directs them to the Scarlet Monastery's library to find a book, then puts a question of his own to them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Parqual Fintallas?",a="You can find Parqual Fintallas in the Apothecarium beneath the ruins of Lordaeron, in the Forsaken capital of the Undercity.",al={"parqual fintallas location","where is parqual","parqual undercity"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Parqual Fintallas known for?",a="In life, Parqual knew nearly all there was to know about Lordaeron's history. Even in undeath, he remains an authority on history and helps travelers find obscure texts and ancient knowledge.",al={"who is parqual","what does parqual do","parqual fintallas lore"},it="fame"},{q="Why is Parqual involved in the Test of Lore?",a="The Test of Lore asks adventurers to prove their knowledge as well as their strength. Parqual sends them to the Scarlet Monastery for Beginnings of the Undead Threat, then asks a question about the book.",al={"parqual test of lore","test of lore undercity","parqual fintallas quest"},it="motive"},{q="Does Parqual share the hostile demeanor of most Forsaken?",a="Parqual is friendly in everyday conversation and says he is glad when someone takes time to speak with him. Yet he can sharply doubt those who claim to have passed Braug Dimspirit's trials, and he scorns the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"is parqual friendly","parqual personality"}},{q="Who is Parqual Fintallas?",a="Parqual Fintallas was once a renowned human historian who knew everything there was to know about the kingdom of Lordaeron. Claimed by the Plague and risen into undeath, he now resides among the Forsaken in the Undercity's Apothecarium. Despite his condition, he retains his deep passion for historical lore, tomes, and quiet scholarship.",al={"who is parqual","parqual fintallas","who is fintallas"},it="identity",add="8cab13a3"},{q="Whose side is Parqual Fintallas on?",a="Parqual is aligned with the Forsaken and the Horde, dwelling peacefully within the Undercity. Unlike many of his embittered kin, he bears little malice toward travelers and willingly shares his historical expertise with Horde wanderers seeking knowledge.",al={"who does parqual serve","parqual faction","is parqual horde"},it="side",add="d8934933"},{q="What does Parqual Fintallas want?",a="Parqual seeks to preserve the history of Lordaeron and continue his scholarly pursuits in undeath, valuing knowledge far above strength. He readily assists those who come seeking forgotten records and historical wisdom, though he first sends them to recover rare books such as Beginnings of the Undead Threat from the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"what does parqual want","parqual fintallas goals","parqual motive"},it="wants",add="5af35229"},{q="Why is Parqual Fintallas here in the Apothecarium?",a="Parqual makes his home in the Undercity's Apothecarium, surrounded by researchers and scholars. Though surrounded by darker alchemical works, he uses the quiet corners of the city to study and preserve historical records, acting as a resource for those pursuing lost lore.",al={"why is parqual here","why is parqual in undercity","what is parqual doing in the apothecarium"},it="why_here",add="03c3b7bf"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, Parqual recalls Lordaeron's intellectual past through scholarship and civilized conversation, even amid the Apothecarium's bleakness.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer facing trials of mind and blade, you can turn to Parqual's deep knowledge of history to uncover Azeroth's ancient truths."},kw={"apothecarium","fintallas","historian","lordaeron","parqual","scholar","test of lore","undercity"},rel={"quest:1152","zone:undercity","subzone:apothecarium","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Parqual Fintallas"}}
E["npc:pilot-longbeard"] = {t="npc",n="Pilot Longbeard",z="thousandneedles",s="In Ironforge's Military Ward, Pilot Longbeard watches for word from mechanics far away. He is stationed in the Hall of Arms and keeps close to gnomish tinkerers and fellow racing enthusiasts in the Shimmering Flats.",h="In Ironforge's Military Ward, Pilot Longbeard watches for word from mechanics far away.",sec={{t="A Pilot of the Siege Brigade",b="Pilot Longbeard serves with the Ironforge Siege Brigade in the Military Ward. He listens eagerly for news from mechanics across the continent. Among them are the Brassbolts brothers, who tinker on Kalimdor's salt flats.",sp=0},{t="Connections Across Continents",b="Longbeard points travelers bound for Kalimdor toward the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. There, gnomish inventors push the bounds of machinery alongside their goblin rivals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Pilot Longbeard?",a="Pilot Longbeard is in the Hall of Arms in Ironforge's Military Ward, near the trainers and military displays.",al={"pilot longbeard location","where is longbeard ironforge","how to find pilot longbeard"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Pilot Longbeard's role?",a="Pilot Longbeard directs Alliance adventurers toward ventures abroad. He especially points them to his friends, the Brassbolts brothers, in Thousand Needles.",al={"what does longbeard do","pilot longbeard quest","why talk to longbeard"},it="identity"},{q="Who are the Brassbolts brothers to Longbeard?",a="The Brassbolts brothers are gnomish tinkerers and associates of Longbeard in the Shimmering Flats. They share his passion for engineering and experimental machinery.",al={"brassbolts connection","why does longbeard know brassbolts","longbeard shimmering deep"},it="ties"},{q="Is Pilot Longbeard related to Furen Longbeard?",a="Pilot Longbeard and Furen Longbeard share Ironforge's prominent Longbeard clan name, suggesting they may be kin. Pilot Longbeard is concerned with siege engines and engineering connections rather than smithing.",al={"furen longbeard brother","longbeard family dwarf","is he related to furen"}},{q="Whose side is Pilot Longbeard on?",a="Pilot Longbeard stands firmly with the Ironforge dwarves and the Alliance. A pilot of the Ironforge Siege Brigade stationed within the Hall of Arms in Ironforge's Military Ward, he takes pride in the brigade's siege engines and helps friends and fellow pilots across the Alliance.",al={"pilot longbeard faction","is pilot longbeard alliance","longbeard allegiance"},it="side",add="e17c59b9"},{q="What does Pilot Longbeard want?",a="Pilot Longbeard wants to help his friends and fellow pilots, though his duties keep him in Ironforge. He sends travelers to deliver Siege Engine helmets to his friends, the Brassbolts brothers, whose rocket car pilots keep crashing out in the Shimmering Flats, and to help Pilot Stonegear track down a rare ore.",al={"pilot longbeard goal","what does longbeard need","pilot longbeard quests"},it="wants",add="97d29847"},{q="Why is Pilot Longbeard here?",a="As a pilot of the Ironforge Siege Brigade, Longbeard is stationed at the Hall of Arms within Ironforge's Military Ward. His duties keep him in the city, so he relies on travelers to carry help to friends afield, such as the Brassbolts brothers and their gnomish racing team.",al={"why is pilot longbeard in ironforge","longbeard military ward reason","why is longbeard here"},it="why_here",add="5f9eba76"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see Pilot Longbeard link Ironforge's martial service with siege engines and gnomish mechanics.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the mechanical ingenuity Longbeard values as a siege engine pilot with contacts among gnome tinkerers."},kw={"brassbolts","hall of arms","ironforge","military ward","pilot longbeard","shimmering deep","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:military-ward","quest:1179","quest:467","zone:thousandneedles","npc:furen-longbeard","topic:dwarf"},src={"Pilot Longbeard"}}
E["npc:pozzik"] = {t="npc",n="Pozzik",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Pozzik tests goblin engineering against a gnome rival. Once among Undermine’s most respected engineers, he now builds experimental rocket cars on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Pozzik tests goblin engineering against a gnome rival.",sec={{t="A Master of Undermine",b="Pozzik made his name among goblin tinkerers before settling in Thousand Needles. He was one of Undermine’s most respected engineers, mastering complex internal combustion, propulsion, and dangerous chassis construction. He left that reputation behind for the salt flats, where he pushes high-speed machines to their limits.",sp=0},{t="The Duel on the Salt Flats",b="At the Mirage Raceway, Pozzik works with Fizzle Brassbolts, his longtime gnome counterpart. Goblin explosives and gnomish calibration have long stood as rivals, yet the two built a sprawling track across a dried lakebed. Now their racing outfits test prototype rocket cars to prove whose engineering rules the track. Pozzik seeks resourceful adventurers to find parts and lighten his designs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pozzik?",a="Pozzik is a veteran goblin engineer from Undermine who now leads one side of the rocket car competition at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles.",al={"pozzik","who is pozzik","pozzik lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Pozzik out in Thousand Needles?",a="Pozzik left formal work in Undermine and came to the Shimmering Flats to build and race experimental rocket cars across the salt flats.",al={"why is pozzik here","pozzik shimmering flats"},it="why_here"},{q="What is his relationship with Fizzle Brassbolts?",a="Fizzle Brassbolts is Pozzik’s longtime gnomish rival and co-founder of the Mirage Raceway. They maintain the track together and compete to prove goblin engineering superior to gnomish craftsmanship.",al={"pozzik and fizzle","pozzik gnome rival"},it="ties"},{q="Does Pozzik work for the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Pozzik works independently at the raceway and does business with both Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"is pozzik neutral","pozzik faction"},it="side"},{q="What kind of projects is Pozzik working on right now?",a="Pozzik works to make his rocket cars faster. He develops multi-engine racing chassis, gathers rare lightweight ores, and sends explorers to recover salvaged parts and components.",al={"pozzik quests","what does pozzik build"},it="wants"},{q="Why is Pozzik famous?",a="Before settling in the Shimmering Flats, Pozzik earned a reputation as one of the most respected tinkerers in Undermine. His legendary engineering prowess carried over into his rocket car designs, where he revolutionized the sport by developing powerful two-engine racer models.",al={"pozzik fame","is pozzik famous","why is pozzik well known"},it="fame",add="186dfe38"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For goblin and gnomish engineers, Pozzik shows how far high-risk, high-speed mechanics can go.",["race:Gnome"]="At the track, gnomes meet their favorite foil in Pozzik, a loud goblin engineer who believes brute thrust beats careful precision."},kw={"fizzle brassbolts","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","tinker","undermine"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","npc:fizzle-brassbolts","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1176","topic:goblin","zone:tanaris"},src={"Pozzik"}}
E["npc:rau-cliffrunner"] = {t="npc",n="Rau Cliffrunner",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Rau Cliffrunner keeps watch over Thousand Needles and studies the Galak centaur. He works with allies in Thunder Bluff to guard his people from threats across the canyon.",h="At Freewind Post, Rau Cliffrunner keeps watch over Thousand Needles and studies the Galak centaur.",sec={{t="Watcher of the Canyons",b="From Freewind Post, Rau Cliffrunner watches the broad reaches of Thousand Needles. Predators, quilboar, and hostile centaur clans surround the tauren outpost. Rau helps organize the post and investigates dangers before they can threaten the mesa settlements.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Galak",b="Rau Cliffrunner studies the centaur, who have fought the tauren for generations. The Galak guard a sacred relic tied to their beginnings, and Rau seeks a way past its mystical protections.\n\nWith Zangen Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff, Rau obtains sacred moonwell water from Ashenvale. It can extinguish the eternal flame at Splithoof Hold and clear the way to retrieve the Cloven Hoof for his study.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Rau Cliffrunner?",a="Rau Cliffrunner is atop Freewind Post, a mesa outpost in the middle of Thousand Needles.",al={"rau cliffrunner location","where is rau","where is rau cliffrunner"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Rau Cliffrunner investigating?",a="Rau Cliffrunner studies the centaur's origins and mystical traditions. He seeks the Cloven Hoof, an ancient Galak relic kept within Splithoof Crag, whose strange energies may shed light on the tauren's historic enemies.",al={"rau cliffrunner purpose","what does rau want","why does rau want the hoof"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Rau need moonwell water?",a="Rau Cliffrunner needs moonwell water to extinguish the eternal mystical fire guarding the Galak relic. Pure water from a night elven moonwell in Ashenvale carries sacred power to quench the brazier's flame and breach its ward.",al={"rau moonwell water","sacred flame moonwell","why moonwell water"},it="motive"},{q="Who is working with Rau Cliffrunner in Thunder Bluff?",a="Zangen Stonehoof works with Rau Cliffrunner from the High Rise of Thunder Bluff. Zangen arranges to retrieve moonwell water from Ashenvale, then directs trusted Horde travelers to Rau at Freewind Post.",al={"rau ally","zangen and rau","who sent me to rau"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Cloven Hoof?",a="The Cloven Hoof is an ancient centaur artifact kept by the Galak clan in Splithoof Hold. It dates to the creation of the centaur race and radiates unusual energy Rau hopes to decipher.",al={"cloven hoof relic","what is the hoof","centaur relic thousand needles"},it="item"},{q="Does Rau Cliffrunner belong to a specific tauren tribe?",a="No specific tribe is recorded for Rau Cliffrunner. He is a tauren warrior of Thunder Bluff stationed at Freewind Post, and his surname is not tied to a named tribe.",al={"rau cliffrunner tribe","what tribe is rau"},it="people"},{q="Who is Rau Cliffrunner?",a="Rau Cliffrunner is a tauren scholar and scout stationed at Freewind Post high above the canyon floor of Thousand Needles. Deeply invested in unraveling the history of the local Galak centaur, he works alongside fellow researchers in Thunder Bluff to recover and study ancient artifacts tied to the origins of Kalimdor's centaur tribes.",al={"rau cliffrunner who","who rau cliffrunner","rau cliffrunner lore"},it="identity",add="c4ebc959"},{q="Whose side is Rau Cliffrunner on?",a="Rau stands firmly with the tauren of Thunder Bluff and the Horde. Stationed at Freewind Post, he coordinates with Horde travelers to safeguard the mesa and secure relics that might reveal crucial knowledge about the Horde's bitter enemies, the centaur.",al={"rau cliffrunner faction","is rau horde","rau cliffrunner allegiance"},it="side",add="dfeb320c"},{q="What does Rau Cliffrunner want?",a="Rau seeks to unlock the secrets behind an ancient centaur relic known as the Cloven Hoof, preserved since the race's creation. To claim it, he needs moonwell water to extinguish the sacred flame guarding it in Splithoof Hold, hoping its strange energies will grant profound insight into centaur history.",al={"rau cliffrunner goal","what does rau want","rau motives"},it="wants",add="3af393e1"},{q="Why is Rau Cliffrunner at Freewind Post?",a="Freewind Post serves as the central Horde bastion in Thousand Needles, towering directly over the canyon and neighboring the Galak centaur settlements. Rau remains here to oversee investigations into Splithoof Crag and decipher the mysteries of the ancient relics sheltered within the bluffs.",al={"why is rau cliffrunner here","why is rau in thousand needles","rau freewind post why"},it="why_here",add="66929801"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren, understanding the centaur is a matter of cultural survival. Rau Cliffrunner studies their beginnings for insight into the ancestral conflict that nearly drove the Shu'halo to extinction.",["faction:Horde"]="Rau Cliffrunner's work helps secure Freewind Post, an isolated Horde stronghold that supports supply lines between the Barrens and Tanaris."},kw={"cloven hoof","freewind post","galak","rau cliffrunner","sacred flame","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles","zangen stonehoof"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:zangen-stonehoof","quest:1195","subzone:splithoof-hold","subzone:splithoof-crag","topic:centaur","topic:tauren"},src={"Rau Cliffrunner"}}
E["npc:thalia-amberhide"] = {t="npc",n="Thalia Amberhide",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Thalia Amberhide waits for Lakota Windsong to return safely. Her friend was taken by the Grimtotem clan in Thousand Needles.",h="At Freewind Post, Thalia Amberhide waits for Lakota Windsong to return safely.",sec={{t="A Friend at the Post",b="At Freewind Post, Thalia Amberhide waits for word of Lakota Windsong. Arnak Grimtotem and his kin captured her close companion. Thalia needs passing Horde travelers to search the canyon depths, free Lakota, and guide her back up the lifts to the mesa settlement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thalia Amberhide?",a="Thalia Amberhide lives at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. She is a loyal friend to Lakota Windsong, a tauren caught up with the Grimtotem clan.",al={"thalia amberhide","who is thalia"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Thalia Amberhide be found?",a="Thalia Amberhide can be found on the high mesa at Freewind Post, in the middle of Thousand Needles. Wooden elevators carry travelers up from the canyon floor.",al={"thalia location","where is thalia amberhide"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Thalia's connection to Lakota Windsong?",a="Thalia Amberhide is a close friend of Lakota Windsong. After Arnak Grimtotem captures Lakota, Thalia welcomes travelers at Freewind Post who help Lakota escape her captors.",al={"thalia and lakota","who is lakota windsong"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Thalia Amberhide on?",a="Thalia Amberhide is loyal to the Horde and her tauren kin. Residing at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles, she welcomes Horde adventurers traveling across the windswept mesas and stands firm against hostile factions threatening the local tribes.",al={"thalia amberhide faction","is thalia amberhide horde","thalia horde or alliance"},it="side",add="29deb6ad"},{q="Why is Thalia Amberhide here?",a="Thalia makes her home atop Freewind Post, serving as a peaceful resident of the tauren mesa settlement. While she lives quietly among her people, her heart remains troubled by the threats facing her friends in the canyons below.",al={"why is thalia at freewind post","thalia amberhide location why","what brought thalia to thousand needles"},it="why_here",add="80c269cc"},{q="What does Thalia Amberhide want?",a="Thalia cares deeply about the well-being of her close companion, Lakota Windsong. Her chief concern is the safety of those she holds dear against the predations of aggressive rival clans like the Grimtotem.",al={"what does thalia want","thalia amberhide motive","thalia amberhide goals"},it="wants",add="211f0475"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can help Thalia rescue Lakota and stand against the Grimtotem tribe's treachery. Their actions threaten your kin amid clan discord.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help protect Freewind Post from Grimtotem aggression. It is a key Horde waypoint in Thousand Needles."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","freewind post","grimtotem","lakota windsong","thalia amberhide","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:lakota-windsong","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","quest:4904","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Thalia Amberhide"}}
E["npc:wizlo-bearingshiner"] = {t="npc",n="Wizlo Bearingshiner",z="thousandneedles",s="At Whitereach Post, Wizlo Bearingshiner waits for help after centaur attacked his caravan. The goblin tinkerer survived alone, while his clients still await their wares. He asks travelers to recover a valuable Hypercapacitor Gizmo from the wreckage.",h="At Whitereach Post, Wizlo Bearingshiner waits for help after centaur attacked his caravan.",sec={{t="An Engineer at the Post",b="Wizlo Bearingshiner waits with the tauren at Whitereach Post, along the canyon road. Centaur attacked his caravan and left him as its only survivor. His clients still await their wares, and he fears he will not deliver them in time.",sp=0},{t="A Stranded Shipment",b="Wizlo's best gizmo hangs around the neck of a fierce panther caged beside his ruined caravan, north of Whitereach Post. Even the centaur avoid the beast. Wizlo offers travelers the cage key and a reward for recovering the hypercapacitor. He does not know what the device does.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner, a goblin tinkerer, waits at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles after centaur attacked his caravan. He seeks help recovering a Hypercapacitor Gizmo from a caged panther.",al={"wizlo bearingshiner","who is wizlo","whitereach goblin"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="You can find Wizlo Bearingshiner at Whitereach Post, a Horde camp along the road near Camp E'thok in Thousand Needles.",al={"wizlo location","where is wizlo","find wizlo"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of experiments does he run?",a="Wizlo is trying to recover his Hypercapacitor Gizmo. He does not know what it does, so its exact function is unknown.",al={"wizlo quests","what does wizlo do","wizlo gadgets"}},{q="Why is a goblin working with the Horde at Whitereach Post?",a="Wizlo did not mean to stop at Whitereach Post. Centaur attacked his caravan nearby, leaving him stranded while his clients await their shipments.",al={"why is wizlo here","is wizlo horde","goblin at whitereach"},it="side"},{q="Does Wizlo belong to the Steamwheedle Cartel?",a="No Steamwheedle affiliation is established for Wizlo. At Whitereach Post with the Horde, he is focused on recovering his goods and delivering them to his clients.",al={"wizlo faction","steamwheedle wizlo","wizlo cartel"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Hypercapacitor Gizmo?",a="The Hypercapacitor Gizmo is a valuable device around the neck of a caged panther beside Wizlo's wrecked caravan. Even Wizlo does not know its purpose.",al={"hypercapacitor gizmo","wizlo device","gizmo quest"},it="item"},{q="What does Wizlo Bearingshiner want?",a="Wizlo wants his Hypercapacitor Gizmo recovered from the panther guarding his wrecked caravan north of Whitereach Post. Centaur attacked the caravan, leaving him stranded while his clients wait for their goods.",al={"what does wizlo want","wizlo bearingshiner goal","wizlo experiments"},it="wants",add="7d59faba"},{q="Why is Wizlo Bearingshiner here in Thousand Needles?",a="Whitereach Post is an unintended stop after centaur attacked Wizlo's caravan nearby. He is the only survivor and is anxious about the deliveries his clients are expecting.",al={"why is wizlo here","why is wizlo in thousand needles","wizlo whitereach post why"},it="why_here",add="1b304945"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may understand Wizlo's wish to recover the mysterious Hypercapacitor Gizmo and learn what it does.",["faction:Horde"]="At Whitereach Post, you can make camp alongside the local tauren and draw on Wizlo's mechanical expertise to secure useful gadgets."},kw={"goblin engineer","hypercapacitor gizmo","thousand needles","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","quest:5151","topic:goblin"},src={"Wizlo Bearingshiner"}}
E["npc:wizzle-brassbolts"] = {t="npc",n="Wizzle Brassbolts",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Wizzle Brassbolts gathers local materials for the gnomish team's experimental rocket cars. He works with fellow tinkerers on the salt flats of Thousand Needles.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Wizzle Brassbolts gathers local materials for the gnomish team's experimental rocket...",sec={{t="Tinkering on the Salt Flats",b="On the Shimmering Flats, gnomish and goblin engineers race rocket cars at high speed. Wizzle Brassbolts works with the gnomish crew to keep their machines whole against speed and abrasive salt. He asks travelers to hunt local wildlife, including sturdy turtles in the basin. Their hard shells may make fuel tanks strong enough to hold his brother's corrosive new rocket fuel.",sp=0},{t="Friends in Distant Places",b="Wizzle keeps in touch with friends across the continents. Pilot Longbeard sends couriers with racing helmets for the brothers. Their help keeps the gnomish team supplied at its remote testing ground on the Shimmering Flats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Wizzle Brassbolts?",a="Wizzle Brassbolts works at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats, in southeastern Thousand Needles. He can be found among the gnomish pit crew and their machinery.",al={"wizzle location","where is wizzle brassbolts","wizzle brassbolts map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Wizzle collecting turtle shells?",a="Wizzle collects turtle shells to make tanks for his brother's new rocket fuel, which can eat through a car's chassis. The hard shells of the Shimmering Flats tortoises can hold it.",al={"hardened shells quest","why does wizzle want shells","turtle shells raceway"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the Brassbolts brothers?",a="Wizzle, Fizzle, and Rizzle Brassbolts are gnomish brothers who run the rocket car team at the Mirage Raceway and race against the goblins. Pilot Longbeard is their friend.",al={"brassbolts family","the brassbolts brothers","wizzle brothers"},it="ties"},{q="Is Wizzle friendly to Horde players?",a="Yes. The Mirage Raceway is neutral ground, and Wizzle's work gathering hardened tortoise shells welcomes Horde and Alliance adventurers alike.",al={"can horde talk to wizzle","wizzle brassbolts horde"},it="side"},{q="Who is Wizzle Brassbolts?",a="Wizzle Brassbolts is an intrepid gnomish engineer stationed out on the shimmering flats of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. Alongside his kin, he works diligently on cutting-edge engineering projects and mechanical innovations, representing the ingenuity of Gnomeregan amid the relentless heat of the salt flats.",al={"who is wizzle","wizzle brassbolts lore","who is wizzle brassbolts"},it="identity",add="ae9cecf8"},{q="What does Wizzle Brassbolts want?",a="Wizzle seeks rare and durable materials from across the region to reinforce and perfect his engineering creations. Whether it is gathering hardened turtle shells or procuring formidable beast parts like tail fins, he relies on adventurous travelers to bring him the exotic components needed for his mechanical tests.",al={"what does wizzle want","wizzle brassbolts goal","wizzle brassbolts quest"},it="wants",add="704bc566"},{q="Why is Wizzle Brassbolts here?",a="Wizzle is stationed at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats to support gnomish engineering efforts and the ongoing vehicle races against their goblin rivals. The vast, flat salt basin offers the perfect testing ground for high-speed machinery and experimental contraptions.",al={"why is wizzle here","why is wizzle at mirage raceway","wizzle thousand needles why"},it="why_here",add="96d92e19"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizzle shows the gnomish way of engineering: push fast machines to their limits, and use unusual reinforcements when metal sheets fail.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome visiting the Shimmering Flats, you may recognize Wizzle's resolve to beat the Steamwheedle goblins' reckless machines through superior craft."},kw={"brassbolts","mirage raceway","pilot longbeard","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","wizzle"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","quest:1105","quest:1179","npc:pilot-longbeard","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},src={"Wizzle Brassbolts"}}
E["quest:1099"] = {t="quest",n="Goblins Win!",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, the goblin race decides who wins a goblin prize box. Goblins Win! names the result for whoever holds the winning ticket.",h="In Thousand Needles, the goblin race decides who wins a goblin prize box.",sec={{t="The Goblin Ticket",b="You hold the goblin race ticket while the goblins' side is decided. If they win, the ticket earns you a goblin prize box. The gnome ticket counts for the other side.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Goblin Race Ticket?",a="The Goblin Race Ticket counts for the goblin side of the race in Thousand Needles. If the goblins win, it is the winning ticket.",al={"race ticket","what is goblin race ticket"}},{q="What do you get when the goblins win?",a="Whoever holds the goblin race ticket when the goblins win receives a goblin prize box.",al={"goblin prize box","goblins win prize"}},{q="What happens if the gnomes win instead?",a="If the gnomes win, the gnome ticket counts. That result is called Gnomes Win!, the counterpart to Goblins Win!.",al={"gnomes win","gnome race ticket"}}},kw={"goblin","goblin prize box","race ticket","thousand needles"},rel={"topic:goblin","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Automatic",level="1",faction="Neutral",id=1099},src={"Wowpedia: Goblins Win!"}}
E["quest:1100"] = {t="quest",n="Lonebrow's Journal",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Great Lift in Thousand Needles, Henrig Lonebrow lies dead with Lonebrow's Journal in his hand. Its pages trace his last journey and ask you to carry the book west to a night elf druid at the Feralas border.",h="At the Great Lift in Thousand Needles, Henrig Lonebrow lies dead with Lonebrow's Journal in his hand.",sec={{t="A Fallen Explorer",b="Henrig Lonebrow lies near the Great Lift, the huge machine that carries travelers from the Barrens to the floor of Thousand Needles. His journal remains in his hand, filled with notes from his travels through the canyon. Centaur and tauren hold this harsh country. His death shows the peril of traveling here alone.",sp=0},{t="A Dying Request",b="Henrig's journal records the route he meant to take and his final wish. He hoped his records would reach friendly hands instead of decaying in the canyon. Follow the road west across Thousand Needles and out of its dry gullies toward Thalanaar. The night elf outpost guards the Feralas border, where its druid, Falfindel Waywarder, awaits news from you.",sp=0},{t="Uncovering the Kraul",b="Falfindel Waywarder finds signs of a wider menace in Southern Kalimdor among Lonebrow's notes. Henrig's observations point north to the bramble-choked warrens of Razorfen Kraul. A dangerous crone leads the quilboar who dwell there.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find Henrig Lonebrow's body?",a="Henrig Lonebrow's body lies at the foot of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles. From the bottom of the western elevator ramp, go about twenty-five feet toward a low rock ledge. His body rests there with the journal in hand.",al={"henrig lonebrow location","where is lonebrow journal","lonebrow body","find lonebrow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who do I deliver the journal to?",a="Take the journal to Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf druid stationed at Thalanaar. The outpost lies along the main road west, on the border between Thousand Needles and Feralas.",al={"who gets lonebrow journal","where to turn in lonebrow","lonebrow turn in","falfindel location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who was Henrig Lonebrow?",a="Henrig Lonebrow was a dwarven traveler crossing central Kalimdor. He died near the base of the Great Lift, leaving a weathered journal with observations of the surrounding lands and dangerous quilboar movements.",al={"who is henrig lonebrow","lonebrow backstory","who is lonebrow"},it="identity"},{q="What does this quest lead to?",a="Deliver the journal to Falfindel Waywarder, and the path opens to The Crone of the Kraul. It sends Alliance adventurers into Razorfen Kraul.",al={"lonebrow follow up","quest after lonebrow journal","lonebrow quest chain"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can Horde players pick up the journal?",a="No. Only Alliance players can take the journal and follow the chain it begins. The chain leads to the Alliance border post at Thalanaar.",al={"is lonebrow journal alliance only","can horde do lonebrow journal","horde lonebrow"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why was Lonebrow heading toward Thalanaar?",a="Lonebrow was heading to Thalanaar, the nearest Alliance outpost in the region and a sanctuary between Thousand Needles and the wilds of Feralas. He meant to share his observations of the region with the night elves stationed there.",al={"why thalanaar","why send book to druid","lonebrow purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the journal ask to be taken to Thalanaar?",a="Henrig Lonebrow knew his journey was ending in tragedy beneath the Great Lift. His final wish recorded in the weathered pages was for his findings to reach Falfindel Waywarder at the border post of Thalanaar. By seeing the journal delivered, you ensure that whatever critical intelligence or discoveries cost the dwarf his life are not lost to the sands of Thousand Needles.",al={"why deliver journal","journal purpose","henrig lonebrow journal motive"},it="purpose",add="0173d93a"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Henrig Lonebrow's death reminds you of the dangers dwarven explorers face far from Ironforge, in Kalimdor's wild corners.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know there are few outposts between Theramore and Thalanaar. Recover Lonebrow's journal to carry vital intelligence to Alliance allies before the canyon claims it.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see why Falfindel Waywarder in Thalanaar watches for unnatural shifts in the local ecosystem. Lonebrow's notes about the quilboar in Razorfen matter to the Cenarion Circle."},kw={"falfindel","feralas","great lift","henrig","journal","lonebrow","razorfen kraul","thalanaar","thousand needles","waywarder"},rel={"quest:1101","npc:falfindel-waywarder","subzone:great-lift","subzone:thalanaar","zone:thousandneedles","zone:razorfenkraul","zone:feralas","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Henrig Lonebrow's Journal",["end"]="Falfindel Waywarder",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1100},src={"Lonebrow's Journal (quest)"}}
E["quest:1104"] = {t="quest",n="Salt Flat Venom",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Fizzle Brassbolts seeks hotter fuel for his rocket car. He believes scorpid venom from the Shimmering Flats can give it the fierce burn he needs.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Fizzle Brassbolts seeks hotter fuel for his rocket car.",sec={{t="A Volatile Recipe",b="At the Mirage Raceway, gnomish precision meets goblin audacity in contests of speed and invention. Fizzle Brassbolts wants more from fuel and clockwork parts. He seeks a mixture that burns hotter than common propellants and sends rocket cars racing across the dry salt lake at blistering speed.",sp=0},{t="Saline Venom of the Salt Flats",b="Scorpids in the Shimmering Flats may hold the key to Fizzle's new fuel. They endure an arid wasteland crusted with salt, and their venom carries an unusual amount of it. Fizzle sees a useful chemical payload in their deadly sting. He believes boiling and refining the venom, then treating it with exotic catalysts, can create the fierce combustion needed to leave the goblin pit crews behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Fizzle Brassbolts want scorpid venom?",a="Fizzle Brassbolts wants scorpid venom for rocket car fuel that burns extremely hot. He believes the unusual salt content in Shimmering Flats scorpids' venom is vital to his explosive mixture.",al={"why scorpid venom","what is venom for","fizzle fuel recipe"},it="motive"},{q="Where can the necessary scorpids be found?",a="Scorpids roam the open Shimmering Flats, especially the western flats and desert sands away from the central racetrack.",al={"scorpid location","where are scorpids","salt flat venom mobs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What will Fizzle do with the venom once collected?",a="Fizzle plans to boil down the venom, treat it with a skipper-otomer, and mix it with a nega-catalyst for rocket propellant. He has misplaced his notes.",al={"how is venom turned to fuel","fuel process"},it="item"},{q="Can members of both the Alliance and Horde help Fizzle?",a="Yes. Gnomes and goblins manage the Mirage Raceway under a neutral truce, so adventurers from either faction can help the pit crews without political interference.",al={"is this quest neutral","horde or alliance"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Why are gnomes and goblins racing in Thousand Needles?",a="The Shimmering Flats offer a vast, flat stretch of hard-packed salt without obstructions. That makes them a proving ground for experimental, high-speed rocket cars and dragsters.",al={"why raceway here","why mirage raceway"},it="conflict"},{q="Does the fuel actually make the car fly?",a="Fizzle eagerly says the car will “fly,” but gnomish rocket vehicles on the salt flats are built to skim the ground at breakneck speed. Catastrophic liftoffs and crashes remain possible.",al={"does car fly","fizzle rocket car result"},it="power"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may recognize Fizzle's familiar ambition: relentless tinkering, risky chemistry, misplaced notes, and the urge to outshine goblin mechanics.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how organic toxins and catalysts like skipper-otomers fuel the creative, volatile experiments of competitive vehicle craft."},kw={"fizzle brassbolts","fuel","mirage raceway","rocket car","salty scorpid venom","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:fizzle-brassbolts","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},m={start="Fizzle Brassbolts",level="30",id=1104,ri={"Salty Scorpid Venom"}},src={"Salt Flat Venom"}}
E["quest:1105"] = {t="quest",n="Hardened Shells",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Wizzle Brassbolts fears his brother’s fuel will eat through their racer. He seeks tortoise shells to shield the tanks.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Wizzle Brassbolts fears his brother’s fuel will eat through their racer.",sec={{t="Volatile Innovations",b="At the Mirage Raceway, Wizzle Brassbolts and his brother race to outdo goblin engineers. Their custom rocket car runs on an experimental fuel mixture his brother has made. The mixture is so potent that Wizzle fears it will eat through the car’s usual chassis and tanks. He needs a container sturdy enough to hold it across the Shimmering Flats.",sp=0},{t="Desert Armored Solutions",b="Wizzle turns to the tortoises native to Thousand Needles. Their shells resist harsh elements and mechanical wear, so they may hold where refined metal fails. He hopes to gather the hardened shells and shape them into fuel tanks. They must contain the volatile mixture and keep the rocket car from blowing to pieces.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Wizzle need tortoise shells instead of metal?",a="Wizzle’s brother is brewing experimental rocket fuel that can dissolve metal. Wizzle hopes local tortoise shells will endure the chemical strain better than standard tanks.",al={"why turtle shells","why tortoise shells","fuel tank shell"},it="item"},{q="Who is Wizzle Brassbolts?",a="Wizzle Brassbolts is a gnome engineer at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. He and his brother build and fine-tune a rocket car to outrun their goblin competitors.",al={"wizzle","who is wizzle"},it="identity"},{q="Where can the tortoises be found?",a="Tortoises roam the Shimmering Flats salt pan, with dense gatherings near the old shipwreck in the northeast.",al={"tortoise location","where are the turtles","where to get hardened shells"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this an Alliance or Horde quest?",a="The Mirage Raceway operates outside faction warfare and focuses on engineering competitions. Adventurers of either faction can help Wizzle.",al={"is hardened shells neutral","alliance or horde"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What happens once the shells are delivered?",a="Once the shells arrive, Wizzle begins shaping them into reinforced fuel tanks. They are so durable that he expects to ruin a toolbox carving them.",al={"wizzle shell result","what does wizzle do with shells"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is fuel tank failure such a concern on the flats?",a="Rocket cars race at terrifying speeds across the salt. Wizzle fears his brother’s fuel could eat through the car’s chassis, so he wants reinforced tanks before that happens.",al={"rocket car danger","why worried about fuel"}},{q="Why does Wizzle Brassbolts want this done?",a="Wizzle's brother is designing an extremely volatile new fuel for their rocket car on the Mirage Raceway. While Wizzle admires his brother's brilliance, he is terrified that the concoction is corrosive enough to melt straight through the car's existing chassis during testing. To prevent a catastrophic disaster on the salt flats, Wizzle needs to craft sturdier replacement fuel tanks before his brother finishes the mixture.",al={"wizzle motive","why help wizzle","why does wizzle want shells"},it="motive",add="201b3417"},{q="What are the tortoises of the Shimmering Flats?",a="Sparkleshell tortoises wander the sun-baked expanses of the Shimmering Flats. Over generations in the harsh, arid basin, their carapaces have hardened into remarkably tough, resilient shells. They generally keep to themselves amidst the salt crust, making them an ideal, durable natural material for gnomish tinkerers in dire need of non-reactive, heat-resistant plating.",al={"salt flat tortoises","shimmering flats turtles","why are there tortoises here"},it="target",add="5a3ddfa8"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Using organic armor plates to contain volatile compounds is an unorthodox choice. It shows the trial and error gnomish tinkerers rely on under pressure.",["race:Gnome"]="Brotherly ingenuity and reckless scientific ambition meet here. The work captures the gnomish drive to out-innovate goblin rivals despite every logistical hurdle."},kw={"hardened shells","mirage raceway","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","tortoise","wizzle brassbolts"},rel={"npc:wizzle-brassbolts","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},m={start="Wizzle Brassbolts",level="30",id=1105,ri={"Hardened Tortoise Shell"}},src={"Hardened Shells"}}
E["quest:1106"] = {t="quest",n="Martek the Exiled",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Fizzle Brassbolts seeks pistons strong enough for the engine he hopes will carry his car into the air. He sends you with a letter to Martek the Exiled, camped in the Badlands.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Fizzle Brassbolts seeks pistons strong enough for the engine he hopes will carry his...",sec={{t="A Letter for the Smith",b="After Salt Flat Venom, Fizzle tells you his new engine should make his car so fast it could fly. His trials have failed because he cannot forge pistons strong enough for the strain. He knows one smith who may help: Martek the Exiled, who knows more about metal than anyone. Martek camps far away in the Badlands with a goblin, and you carry Fizzle's letter to him.",sp=0},{t="At the Camp",b="At the camp, Martek greets you with suspicion. He asks if you have come over an axe made for Gath'Ilzogg or to reclaim Duchess Pamay's honor. If you have come for a fight, he says, it may as well begin now.",sp=1},{t="Martek's Reply",b="When Martek learns Fizzle sent you, his manner changes. Fizzle and his brother are among the few who do not want Martek dead. So Martek agrees to help make pistons strong enough for the strain Fizzle has planned. To Martek, the new car sounds like a volcano on wheels.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Fizzle Brassbolts need Martek's help?",a="Fizzle's new engine should make his car fast enough to fly, but his trials have failed because he cannot make pistons strong enough for the strain. Martek knows more about metal than anyone and may be able to help.",al={"why visit martek","fizzle brassbolts piston problem","why martek the exiled"}},{q="Where is Martek the Exiled located?",a="Martek is camped in the Badlands with a goblin.",al={"where is martek","martek the exiled location","how to find martek"}},{q="What came before this journey?",a="Salt Flat Venom comes before this journey in the chain, and Indurium follows it.",al={"prerequisites for martek the exiled","what quest comes before martek the exiled"}}},kw={"badlands","fizzle brassbolts","gath'ilzogg","martek the exiled","mirage raceway","pistons","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:fizzle-brassbolts","quest:1104","quest:1108","zone:badlands","subzone:mirage-raceway","npc:gath-ilzogg"},m={start="Fizzle Brassbolts",["end"]="Martek the Exiled",level="35",id=1106},src={"Martek the Exiled (quest)"}}
E["quest:1107"] = {t="quest",n="Encrusted Tail Fins",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Wizzle Brassbolts fears the rocket car’s speed will tear it apart. Saltscale murloc tail fins from the Vile Reef off Stranglethorn Vale may protect it.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Wizzle Brassbolts fears the rocket car’s speed will tear it apart.",sec={{t="A Coating for the Car",b="Wizzle calls the rocket car the fastest thing on the Shimmering Flats. Yet friction may tear it apart. Its moving parts need a coating that is hard without being brittle and can resist salt corrosion. Otherwise, the flats will eat away at the car. The key ingredient is ten tail fins from the Saltscale murlocs at the Vile Reef off Stranglethorn Vale.",sp=0},{t="The Finished Composite",b="Wizzle grinds the fins to powder and mixes them with a few other ingredients. The finished composite should protect the car from its own speed, as long as it does not hit anything.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Wizzle Brassbolts need encrusted tail fins?",a="Wizzle fears the rocket car is so fast that friction will tear it apart. The fins are a key ingredient in a composite for its moving parts, hard without being brittle and resistant to salt corrosion.",al={"why tail fins","wizzle tail fins purpose","why murloc fins"}},{q="Where can the Saltscale murlocs be found?",a="The Saltscale murlocs live at the Vile Reef off the coast of Stranglethorn Vale, almost due west of Grom'gol Base Camp.",al={"vile reef location","where are saltscale murlocs","where to find encrusted fins"}},{q="What came before this for Wizzle?",a="Hardened Shells comes before Encrusted Tail Fins in the chain.",al={"what quest comes first","wizzle chain previous quest","prerequisite for encrusted tail fins"}},{q="Who is Wizzle Brassbolts?",a="Wizzle Brassbolts is at the Mirage Raceway. Worried that friction will tear the rocket car apart, he asks you to bring him the fins.",al={"who is wizzle","who gives encrusted tail fins"}}},kw={"encrusted tail fins","mirage raceway","rocket car","saltscale murlocs","shimmering flats","stranglethorn vale","vile reef","wizzle brassbolts"},rel={"quest:1105","npc:wizzle-brassbolts","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:vile-reef","zone:stranglethorn","zone:thousandneedles","topic:murloc"},m={start="Wizzle Brassbolts",["end"]="Wizzle Brassbolts",level="35",id=1107},src={"Encrusted Tail Fins"}}
E["quest:1108"] = {t="quest",n="Indurium",z="thousandneedles",s="In the Badlands, Martek the Exiled seeks metal samples for Fizzle's car. Indurium is said to endure heat and stress, and Stonevault troggs sometimes carry flakes.",h="In the Badlands, Martek the Exiled seeks metal samples for Fizzle's car.",sec={{t="A Metal Worth Testing",b="Martek the Exiled stays in the Badlands for more than solitude. He thinks indurium might suit Fizzle's car because it is said to endure heat and stress. He wants samples for a test, with the forge ready.",sp=0},{t="Flakes from the Troggs",b="True indurium ore lies deep in Uldaman, but Stonevault troggs in the Badlands sometimes carry flakes. Martek asks for ten. The troggs roam the south-east slope of a rocky clump at Agmond's End, just south of the Valley of Fangs.",sp=0},{t="The Forge Test",b="Martek heats the flakes in his forge, raising the heat in stages. They hold firm, and he swears by Orgrim that indurium can withstand massive heat. The test succeeds. Martek calls the metal amazing stuff.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you after the indurium?",a="Martek the Exiled, in the central Badlands, asks for indurium samples. The chain to him begins with Fizzle Brassbolts at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles.",al={"who gives indurium quest","where to get indurium"}},{q="Why does Martek need indurium?",a="Martek thinks indurium might suit Fizzle's car because it is said to endure heat and stress. He wants samples to test in his forge.",al={"what is indurium used for","why indurium"}},{q="Where can the indurium flakes be found?",a="Stonevault troggs in the Badlands sometimes carry indurium flakes. They roam the south-east slope of a rocky clump at Agmond's End, just south of the Valley of Fangs.",al={"where are indurium flakes","how to get flakes","who drops indurium flakes"}},{q="Where does true indurium ore come from?",a="Martek says true indurium ore lies deep in Uldaman.",al={"where is indurium ore","where is indurium mined"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="Martek the Exiled comes first in the chain, which begins with Fizzle Brassbolts at the Mirage Raceway.",al={"previous quest indurium","how to start indurium"}},{q="What comes after the flakes are delivered?",a="The chain continues with News for Fizzle.",al={"next quest after indurium","what happens next"}}},kw={"agmond's end","badlands","fizzle brassbolts","indurium","indurium flakes","martek the exiled","mirage raceway","stonevault troggs","uldaman"},rel={"quest:1106","quest:1137","npc:fizzle-brassbolts","zone:badlands","subzone:agmond-s-end","subzone:uldaman","topic:trogg"},m={start="Martek the Exiled",["end"]="Martek the Exiled",level="39",faction="Neutral",id=1108},src={"Indurium"}}
E["quest:1110"] = {t="quest",n="Rocket Car Parts",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Rocket Car Parts lie scattered across the Shimmering Flats after racers crash. Kravel Koalbeard pays travelers to gather the wreckage and sell it back to rival crews.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Rocket Car Parts lie scattered across the Shimmering Flats after racers crash.",sec={{t="Debris on the Salt Flats",b="Goblin and gnomish engineers race to outdo one another across the Shimmering Flats. Their experimental rocket cars often fail at speed. Twisted gears, cylinders, and jagged metal scatter over the white desert. As pit crews build and tune their next machines, the salt flats gather what the racers leave behind.",sp=0},{t="Koalbeard's Salvage Enterprise",b="Kravel Koalbeard makes his profit as a middleman at the Mirage Raceway instead of competing on the track. Gnome and goblin mechanics use parts quickly and are always short of spare mechanisms for their vehicles. So Koalbeard pays travelers to gather thirty bundles of shattered debris. He turns each crash into stock he can sell back to the crews.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kravel Koalbeard?",a="Kravel Koalbeard is a dwarf merchant at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. He pursues several schemes around the track, scavenging and taking odd jobs while profiting from gnome and goblin rivalries.",al={"kravel koalbeard","who gives rocket car parts","raceway dwarf"},it="identity"},{q="Why are there so many rocket car parts scattered on the ground?",a="Goblin and gnomish engineers push experimental rocket vehicles hard at the Mirage Raceway. Their crashes and sudden explosions scatter structural fragments, gears, and cylinders across the salt pans.",al={"why are there car parts in the desert","shimmering flats debris","broken rocket cars"},it="origin"},{q="What does Kravel do with the wrecked parts?",a="Koalbeard gathers the scrap and sells it back to the gnome and goblin race teams. Their crews use materials quickly and are eager to buy parts for their next prototypes.",al={"what does kravel want with parts","why collect car parts"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these parts located?",a="The parts lie across the open desert floor of the Shimmering Flats, around the central racing camp. Among the heaps are mechanical scrap, twisted gears, cylinders, and flattened metal plates.",al={"where to find rocket car parts","parts locations","car parts shimmering flats"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does this quest tie into other tasks around the raceway?",a="Yes. Travelers can gather parts while culling local wildlife for other raceway patrons. That work includes collecting venom from scorpid stingers and turtle shells, and thinning out buzzards and basilisks across the salt pans.",al={"raceway quests","shimmering flats hunting quests","quests to do with rocket car parts"},gp=true},{q="What happens to the drivers involved in these wrecks?",a="Rocket car racing is lethal, and many pilots die on their test runs. While sorting scrap, Koalbeard finds a severed ear crushed between metal plates.",al={"do drivers survive crashes","squashed ear","pilot deaths raceway"}},{q="What are the rocket car parts used for?",a="They are twisted salvage—gears, cylinders, and scrap metal thrown from high-speed collisions across the salt flats. Rather than letting them rust in the brine, Kravel Koalbeard gathers them to resell straight back to the frantic gnome and goblin pit crews. Desperate to rebuild their shattered racers and out-tinker their rivals, both sides will gladly buy back scavenged metal to weld onto their next reckless contraption.",al={"rocket car parts use","what are rocket car parts for","why collect rocket car parts"},it="item",add="16d6be49"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The salt flats show the reckless ingenuity of goblin and gnomish designs. Unstable rocket boosters and improvised chassis often fail with a crash.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may see a mercenary streak in Kravel Koalbeard. Many Ironforge dwarves look to the raceway for mechanical innovation or excavation, but he cares only for the coin salvage brings.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see the relentless drive to outpace and out-innovate goblin competitors on the open track. Sometimes that effort ends in disaster."},kw={"crashes","gnome","goblin","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","rocket car parts","salvage","scrap","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","npc:kravel-koalbeard","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1104","quest:1105","quest:1176","topic:goblin"},m={level="31",id=1110,ri={"Rocket Car Parts"}},src={"Rocket Car Parts (quest)"}}
E["quest:1111"] = {t="quest",n="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard sends you to Ratchet for parts the gnomes are waiting on.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard sends you to Ratchet for parts the gnomes are waiting on.",sec={{t="Legwork for Kravel",b="Kravel Koalbeard tends to the needs of the Mirage Raceway. A batch of parts reached Ratchet a week ago, and the gnomes are waiting. Since Kravel cannot make the journey himself, he asks you to carry his order. If you do, he promises more work with serious profit potential.",sp=0},{t="The Docks of Ratchet",b="Ratchet lies in the Barrens, where Kravel expects Wharfmaster Dizzywig to be at the docks. The goblin is the one you need to see. You carry Kravel's Parts Order there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="Kravel Koalbeard, a dwarf at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles, gives you his parts order and sends you to Ratchet.",al={"who gives wharfmaster dizzywig","kravel koalbeard quest"}},{q="Where can Wharfmaster Dizzywig be found?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig, a goblin, will probably be at the docks of Ratchet in the Barrens.",al={"dizzywig location","where is dizzywig","where to find dizzywig"}},{q="What is the purpose of Kravel's order?",a="The gnomes of the Mirage Raceway are waiting for parts that reached Ratchet a week ago. Kravel cannot go himself, so he asks you to carry his order to the docks there.",al={"what are the parts for","why go to ratchet"}},{q="What comes after Wharfmaster Dizzywig?",a="The next step in the chain is Parts for Kravel.",al={"next quest after dizzywig","what comes next"}}},kw={"kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","parts order","ratchet","thousand needles","wharfmaster dizzywig"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","quest:1112","subzone:ratchet","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens","topic:goblin","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",level="36",id=1111},src={"Wharfmaster Dizzywig (quest)"}}
E["quest:1112"] = {t="quest",n="Parts for Kravel",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard awaits the package you carry from Wharfmaster Dizzywig. Dizzywig sends a warning with it: Kravel must pay his tab before he can receive more special orders.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard awaits the package you carry from Wharfmaster Dizzywig.",sec={{t="A Package and a Tab",b="Wharfmaster Dizzywig gives you a package for Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway. The Raceway lies in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles. Dizzywig asks you to carry a warning with the package: Kravel must pay what he owes before he can receive more special orders.",sp=0},{t="Kravel's Welcome",b="Kravel welcomes the package and says it still needs to reach the gnomes. Before it travels any farther, he sets down the crate, removes one small item, and slips it into his pocket.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives you the package for Kravel?",a="Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet gives you Kravel's package and asks you to carry it to Kravel Koalbeard.",al={"who starts parts for kravel","where do the parts come from","parts for kravel quest giver"}},{q="Where does Kravel Koalbeard await the delivery?",a="Kravel Koalbeard awaits the delivery at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",al={"kravel koalbeard location","where is kravel","where to turn in parts for kravel"}},{q="What message does Dizzywig want delivered alongside the parts?",a="Dizzywig asks you to tell Kravel that he must pay his tab before he can receive more special orders.",al={"what does dizzywig say","dizzywig message to kravel","kravel tab"}},{q="What came before this delivery?",a="Before bringing this package back, you carried Kravel's parts order to Wharfmaster Dizzywig in Ratchet.",al={"parts for kravel prerequisite","previous quest parts for kravel"}}},kw={"kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","parts for kravel","shimmering flats","thousand needles","wharfmaster dizzywig"},rel={"quest:1111","quest:1114","npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","topic:dwarf","topic:gnome"},m={start="Wharfmaster Dizzywig",["end"]="Kravel Koalbeard",level="36",id=1112},src={"Parts for Kravel"}}
E["quest:1114"] = {t="quest",n="Delivery to the Gnomes",z="thousandneedles",s="Kravel Koalbeard sends Delicate Car Parts from the Mirage Raceway to Fizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats. Fizzle has waited a long time for them, and Kravel asks you to keep quiet about one small piece he removed.",h="Kravel Koalbeard sends Delicate Car Parts from the Mirage Raceway to Fizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering...",sec={{t="A Piece Left Out",b="Kravel Koalbeard sends the parts to Fizzle Brassbolts, who has waited a long time for them. Kravel admits he removed one little piece from Fizzle's order. He says it is small and worthless, and that Fizzle will not miss it. Then he asks you to trust him and leave it unmentioned.",sp=0},{t="Fizzle's Verdict",b="Fizzle Brassbolts welcomes the parcel. His hydro ratchets and repeater bolts have arrived at last. They will do well enough.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the parts to Fizzle Brassbolts?",a="Kravel Koalbeard sends the parts from the Mirage Raceway and asks you to carry them to Fizzle Brassbolts.",al={"who gives delivery to the gnomes","quest giver delivery to the gnomes","who sends the parts"}},{q="What did Kravel Koalbeard take from the package?",a="Kravel says he removed one little piece from Fizzle's order. He calls it small and worthless, then asks you not to mention it to Fizzle.",al={"what did kravel take","what is missing from the parts","kravel stole parts"}},{q="Where does this delivery go?",a="The parts go to Fizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats. The Mirage Raceway is also on those flats, where Kravel Koalbeard is found.",al={"delivery to the gnomes location","where is fizzle brassbolts","shimmering flats delivery"}},{q="What came before this delivery?",a="Before this delivery, you brought Kravel's package back from Ratchet in Parts for Kravel.",al={"previous quest delivery to the gnomes","what leads to delivery to the gnomes"}}},kw={"delicate car parts","delivery to the gnomes","fizzle brassbolts","hydro ratchets","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","repeater bolts","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","npc:fizzle-brassbolts","quest:1112","quest:1115","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Fizzle Brassbolts",level="36",faction="Neutral",id=1114},src={"Delivery to the Gnomes"}}
E["quest:1115"] = {t="quest",n="The Rumormonger",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard now has a question about Nazz Steamboil. The goblin racer pilot once used another name, and Kravel wonders whether the secret could bring profit. He sends you to Krazek in Booty Bay, who may know.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard now has a question about Nazz Steamboil.",sec={{t="A Name Worth Asking About",b="Kravel Koalbeard says the goblins are next in line for a favor. He has heard that Nazz Steamboil, the goblin racer pilot, once used another name. Why did it change? Might Nazz be keeping a secret? Kravel believes Krazek knows the truth. You can find Krazek at the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay, at Stranglethorn's southern tip. Useful information might turn a profit.",sp=0},{t="Krazek's Answer",b="Krazek knows Nazz Steamboil as a racer pilot on the Shimmering Flats. He says the truth may be uncovered, but it will take effort, time, and money.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Krazek?",a="Kravel Koalbeard, a dwarf at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats, sends you to Krazek.",al={"who gives the rumormonger","rumormonger questgiver","who starts the quest"}},{q="Why is Kravel interested in Nazz Steamboil?",a="Kravel heard that Nazz Steamboil, the goblin racer pilot, once used another name. He wonders whether it hides a secret Nazz wants kept, and whether that secret could bring profit.",al={"why nazz steamboil","kravel motive nazz","what is the rumor"}},{q="Where can Krazek be found?",a="Krazek is at the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay, at the southern tip of Stranglethorn.",al={"krazek location","where is krazek","how to find krazek"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows Delivery to the Gnomes, after you have done a service for the gnomes.",al={"prereq for the rumormonger","rumormonger previous quest","what quest comes first"}}},kw={"booty bay","kravel koalbeard","krazek","mirage raceway","nazz steamboil","salty sailor tavern","shimmering flats","stranglethorn vale","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:salty-sailor-tavern","quest:1114","quest:1116","zone:thousandneedles","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Krazek",level="36",id=1115},src={"The Rumormonger"}}
E["quest:1116"] = {t="quest",n="Dream Dust in the Swamp",z="thousandneedles",s="In the Swamp of Sorrows, Krazek asks you to gather ten specks of dream dust from dragon whelps. He contacts sources about Nazz while seeking dust for his snuff pouch. Bring it back to him for the information you seek.",h="In the Swamp of Sorrows, Krazek asks you to gather ten specks of dream dust from dragon whelps.",sec={{t="A Favor for a Favor",b="Krazek says that learning about Nazz is a considerable favor, and you have traveled a long way from the Shimmering Flats to ask. While he contacts sources, he asks you to gather ten specks of dream dust from dragon whelps in the Swamp of Sorrows. The dust is for his snuff pouch. Bring it back, and Krazek will give you the information you seek.",sp=0},{t="Where the Dust Is Found",b="Green dragons in the Swamp of Sorrows carry dream dust. Adolescent whelps and dreaming whelps can be found in the swamp’s south-western corner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for the dream dust?",a="Krazek of Booty Bay asks you for dream dust in exchange for information about Nazz.",al={"who gives dream dust quest","who sends me to swamp of sorrows","dream dust quest giver"}},{q="Why does Krazek want dream dust?",a="Krazek wants the dust for a snuff pouch. He asks for it while he contacts sources about Nazz.",al={"what is dream dust for","why krazek wants dust","dream dust snuff"}},{q="Where is the dream dust found?",a="You can take dream dust from dragon whelps in the Swamp of Sorrows. Adolescent and dreaming whelps live in the swamp’s south-western corner.",al={"where to find dream dust","where is dream dust swamp of sorrows","dream dust location"}},{q="How does this connect back to Kravel Koalbeard?",a="Kravel Koalbeard of the Mirage Raceway sent you to Krazek to ask about the goblin racer pilot Nazz Steamboil. You came from the Shimmering Flats seeking an answer.",al={"why am i in booty bay","how does this relate to kravel","shimmering flats connection"}},{q="What comes next?",a="Rumors for Kravel comes next.",al={"what after dream dust in the swamp","next quest dream dust","rumors for kravel next"}}},kw={"booty bay","dream dust","kravel koalbeard","krazek","mirage raceway","nazz","swamp of sorrows","whelps"},rel={"quest:1115","quest:1117","npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:booty-bay","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","topic:goblin"},m={start="Krazek",["end"]="Krazek",level="36",id=1116},src={"Dream Dust in the Swamp"}}
E["quest:1117"] = {t="quest",n="Rumors for Kravel",z="thousandneedles",s="At last, Krazek has a letter about Nazz Steamboil for you to carry to Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats. Keep its origin secret.",h="At last, Krazek has a letter about Nazz Steamboil for you to carry to Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway...",sec={{t="A Letter From Krazek",b="Krazek spent favors, a rare bottle of elven wine, and hours of deducing to learn about Nazz Steamboil. His letter holds very interesting bits about the goblin racer pilot. Krazek considers the letter too dangerous to use and leaves it to you, provided nobody learns where it came from. Carry it to Kravel Koalbeard on the Shimmering Flats.",sp=0},{t="Kravel's Verdict",b="Kravel Koalbeard finds the letter very interesting. He wonders if he should bow to the goblin pilot the next time they meet. He expects Nazz Steamboil to pay a small fortune to keep the secret buried.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this begin?",a="Krazek gives you the letter in Booty Bay after you bring him the dream dust.",al={"who gives rumors for kravel","rumors for kravel starter","where do i get the rumors"}},{q="To whom should the letter be brought?",a="Bring the letter to Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles.",al={"where to turn in rumors for kravel","who gets the goblin rumors","where is kravel koalbeard"}},{q="Who is the subject of Krazek's findings?",a="Krazek's findings concern Nazz Steamboil, the goblin racer pilot. His letter holds very interesting bits about Nazz.",al={"who is nazz steamboil","what is the rumor about","who are the rumors on"}},{q="How did Krazek uncover the information?",a="Krazek spent favors, hours deducing, and a rare bottle of elven wine to uncover the information.",al={"how did krazek get the info","krazek favors"}},{q="What comes next?",a="Next, you return to Booty Bay.",al={"next quest after rumors for kravel","rumors for kravel follow up"}}},kw={"booty bay","goblin rumors","kravel koalbeard","krazek","mirage raceway","nazz steamboil","rumors for kravel","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:booty-bay","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1116","quest:1118","topic:goblin"},m={start="Krazek",["end"]="Kravel Koalbeard",level="36",id=1117},src={"Rumors for Kravel"}}
E["quest:1118"] = {t="quest",n="Back to Booty Bay",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard sends you back to Booty Bay with a letter and asks you to keep his scheme quiet. It is risky, but success could bring you both a bundle. This follows Rumors for Kravel.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard sends you back to Booty Bay with a letter and asks you to keep his...",sec={{t="A Letter for Booty Bay",b="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard trusts you to finish a job and keep silent. His new scheme is risky, but success could bring you both a bundle. He sends you back to Booty Bay, where his last job took you, to find Crank Fizzlebub and deliver a letter. If Crank needs help, do your best. Kravel says the effort will be worth it.",sp=0},{t="Crank Reads the Scheme",b="Crank Fizzlebub reads Kravel's letter and learns of the scheme. He admires Kravel's sinister mind. The plan needs something powerful to addle wits, and Crank wonders whether Zanzil's mixture for his zombies could serve.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this journey begin and end?",a="You begin with Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles. Then you carry his letter to Crank Fizzlebub at the Salty Sailor Tavern in Booty Bay, Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where do i go","who gives back to booty bay","where is crank fizzlebub"}},{q="What came before this?",a="Rumors for Kravel came before this and took you to Booty Bay.",al={"prerequisites","previous quest","what quest comes first"}},{q="What is Kravel's Scheme?",a="Kravel's scheme is the plan in the letter you carry to Crank Fizzlebub. Kravel calls it risky and says you could both make a bundle if it pays off.",al={"what is kravel's scheme","kravel scheme letter"}},{q="What should you do if Crank Fizzlebub needs help?",a="Kravel asks you to do your best to help Crank Fizzlebub, saying the effort will be worth it.",al={"help crank","does crank need aid"}},{q="What comes after this?",a="The chain continues with Zanzil's Mixture and a Fool's Stout.",al={"next quest","what follows back to booty bay"}}},kw={"booty bay","crank fizzlebub","kravel koalbeard","kravel's scheme","mirage raceway","salty sailor tavern","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","quest:1117","quest:1119","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:salty-sailor-tavern","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Crank Fizzlebub",level="43",id=1118},src={"Back to Booty Bay"}}
E["quest:1119"] = {t="quest",n="Zanzil's Mixture and a Fool's Stout",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard awaits a stout blended with Zanzil's Mixture. Crank Fizzlebub calls it Fool's Stout and believes Kravel needs it, so you carry it to him on the Shimmering Flats before it spoils.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard awaits a stout blended with Zanzil's Mixture.",sec={{t="A Libation for Kravel",b="Crank Fizzlebub has blended Zanzil's Mixture into stout, making a potent drink he calls Fool's Stout. He believes Kravel needs it and wants to hear how it works. So you carry the drink to Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats.",sp=0},{t="Do Not Let It Sit",b="Crank warns you not to keep the stout long. The mixture drives the yeast into high gear, and the drink will not stay fresh forever.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this delivery?",a="Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay gives you Fool's Stout to carry.",al={"who starts zanzil's mixture and a fool's stout","quest giver"}},{q="Who receives the Fool's Stout?",a="Kravel Koalbeard receives Fool's Stout at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",al={"who gets the stout","where do i turn this in","kravel location"}},{q="Why does the drink need to be delivered quickly?",a="The mixture drives the yeast hard, so stout that sits too long goes off.",al={"does fool's stout expire","why is it timed","fermentation effect"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows Back to Booty Bay and Zanzil's Secret.",al={"prerequisite quests","previous step"}},{q="What comes after delivering the stout?",a="The chain continues with Fool's Stout, Get the Gnomes Drunk and Get the Goblins Drunk.",al={"next quest","what happens next"}}},kw={"booty bay","fizzlebub","kravel","mixture","raceway","shimmering flats","stout","zanzil"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:booty-bay","quest:621","quest:1127","zone:thousandneedles","zone:stranglethorn"},m={start="Crank Fizzlebub",["end"]="Kravel Koalbeard",level="44",id=1119},src={"Zanzil's Mixture and a Fool's Stout"}}
E["quest:1120"] = {t="quest",n="Get the Gnomes Drunk",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Get the Gnomes Drunk begins with a test of Fool's Stout on a pit crew. Kravel Koalbeard gives you the stout for the Gnome Pit Boss nearby and warns that it will go bad eventually.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Get the Gnomes Drunk begins with a test of Fool's Stout on a pit crew.",sec={{t="A Test on the Pit Crews",b="Kravel Koalbeard asks you to test Fool's Stout on one of the pit crews. Choose the gnomes, and he gives you the stout for the Gnome Pit Boss nearby at the Mirage Raceway. That choice tips the races toward the goblins. Kravel warns you not to wait too long, since the stout will go bad eventually.",sp=0},{t="A Little Drink Before the Race",b="The Gnome Pit Boss welcomes your gift and calls it considerate. A race is coming up, so drinking may not be wise. Still, the crew can probably manage a little. The stout cannot be that strong.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who asks you to deliver the stout?",a="Kravel Koalbeard, the dwarf at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles, gives you the stout to deliver.",al={"who gives get the gnomes drunk","quest giver get the gnomes drunk","kravel koalbeard quest"}},{q="To whom should the Fool's Stout be delivered?",a="Take the Fool's Stout to the Gnome Pit Boss, nearby at the Mirage Raceway.",al={"where do i take the stout","who gets the fools stout","gnome pit boss location"}},{q="What happens if you take too long to deliver the stout?",a="The stout will go bad eventually, so Kravel tells you not to wait too long.",al={"does fools stout spoil","stout timer","fools stout goes bad"}},{q="Can you choose to target the goblins instead?",a="Yes. Kravel lets you choose which pit crew to test the stout on. The other choice is Get the Goblins Drunk.",al={"get the goblins drunk choice","can i get goblins drunk instead","gnomes or goblins raceway"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows Zanzil's Mixture and a Fool's Stout.",al={"previous quest","prereq for get the gnomes drunk"}},{q="What comes after the stout is delivered?",a="After you deliver the stout, the chain continues with Report Back to Fizzlebub.",al={"next quest","what comes after get the gnomes drunk"}}},kw={"fool's stout","gnome pit boss","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","thousand needles","zanzil"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1119","quest:1121","quest:1122","topic:gnome","topic:goblin"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Gnome Pit Boss",level="44",id=1120},src={"Get the Gnomes Drunk"}}
E["quest:1121"] = {t="quest",n="Get the Goblins Drunk",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard asks you to test Fool's Stout on a pit crew. Choose the goblins and carry the stout to the nearby Goblin Pit Boss before it goes bad.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard asks you to test Fool's Stout on a pit crew.",sec={{t="A Test on the Pit Crews",b="Kravel Koalbeard gives you Fool's Stout to test on one of the pit crews. If you choose the goblins, take it to the nearby Goblin Pit Boss at the Mirage Raceway. That choice tips the races toward the gnomes. The stout will go bad eventually, so Kravel warns you not to dawdle.",sp=0},{t="A Little Won't Hurt",b="The Goblin Pit Boss sees the booze you offer and agrees to have a little.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers this?",a="Kravel Koalbeard, a dwarf at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles, offers you the stout.",al={"quest giver","who gives get the goblins drunk","kravel koalbeard"}},{q="Where must the stout be taken?",a="Take the stout to the Goblin Pit Boss, who is nearby at the Mirage Raceway.",al={"where to bring stout","goblin pit boss location"}},{q="What happens if you wait too long?",a="The stout will go bad eventually, so Kravel warns you not to wait too long.",al={"does the stout spoil","fool's stout duration","stout goes bad"}},{q="What is the alternative to this?",a="Kravel lets you choose which pit crew to test the stout on. The alternative is Get the Gnomes Drunk, with the gnome crew.",al={"get the gnomes drunk choice","gnomes or goblins raceway"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows Zanzil's Mixture and a Fool's Stout.",al={"previous quest","prereq for get the goblins drunk"}},{q="What comes after the stout is delivered?",a="The chain continues with Report Back to Fizzlebub.",al={"next quest","what comes after get the goblins drunk"}}},kw={"fools stout","gnome","goblin","goblin pit boss","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1119","quest:1120","quest:1122","topic:goblin"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Goblin Pit Boss",level="44",id=1121},src={"Get the Goblins Drunk"}}
E["quest:1122"] = {t="quest",n="Report Back to Fizzlebub",z="thousandneedles",s="Kravel Koalbeard reports that the Fool's Stout worked and sends you to Booty Bay with news for Crank Fizzlebub. He has bet on the next race and hopes the pit crew you made drunk wrecked their own car. This follows your choice to make one pit crew drunk.",h="Kravel Koalbeard reports that the Fool's Stout worked and sends you to Booty Bay with news for Crank...",sec={{t="A Note for Crank",b="Kravel Koalbeard says the Fool's Stout worked well. He's bet on the next race and hopes the pit crew you made drunk wrecked their own car. Take his note about the successful test to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay. Crank will want the news, and Kravel hopes to get more stout for future races.",sp=0},{t="Crank's Answer",b="Crank Fizzlebub reads Kravel's note and calls the test a success. Glad to hear it, Crank says to ask whenever you want more stout. Then you'll be set to collect more of Zanzil's Mixture.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who starts this?",a="Kravel Koalbeard, the dwarf at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles, gives you the note.",al={"quest giver","who gives report back to fizzlebub"}},{q="Where is Crank Fizzlebub located?",a="Crank Fizzlebub is in Booty Bay.",al={"fizzlebub location","where is crank fizzlebub","turn in location"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="Before this, you completed Get the Gnomes Drunk or, if you chose the other crew, Get the Goblins Drunk.",al={"prerequisites","previous quest"}},{q="What does Kravel Koalbeard want Fizzlebub to know?",a="Kravel Koalbeard wants Fizzlebub to know the test succeeded.",al={"what is the report","report contents"}}},kw={"booty bay","crank fizzlebub","fool's stout","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:booty-bay","quest:1120","quest:1121","quest:1127","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Crank Fizzlebub",level="44",id=1122},src={"Report Back to Fizzlebub"}}
E["quest:1137"] = {t="quest",n="News for Fizzle",z="thousandneedles",s="In the Badlands, Martek the Exiled has news for Fizzle Brassbolts about indurium. You carry his message to the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",h="In the Badlands, Martek the Exiled has news for Fizzle Brassbolts about indurium.",sec={{t="Martek's Word on Indurium",b="Martek says indurium withstands heat remarkably well, so it may suit Fizzle's pistons. Flakes will not do; Fizzle needs real indurium ore, dug from deep within Uldaman at the Badlands' northern edge. Martek names Uldaman as indurium's true source. He sends his regards and asks you to repeat all he has told you to Fizzle Brassbolts.",sp=0},{t="Fizzle Hears the News",b="Fizzle Brassbolts is eager to hear Martek's words and learn whether he can help. When you tell Fizzle of your travels in the Badlands, he declares indurium the key.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this journey begin and end?",a="Martek the Exiled in the Badlands gives you a message for Fizzle Brassbolts at the Mirage Raceway on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",al={"who gives news for fizzle","where to turn in news for fizzle","martek to fizzle"}},{q="What news does Martek send to Fizzle?",a="Martek says indurium withstands heat remarkably well and may suit Fizzle's pistons. Fizzle needs real ore, not flakes, mined from deep within Uldaman.",al={"what does martek say","indurium news","martek message"}},{q="Where does indurium ore come from?",a="Martek says indurium ore is dug from deep within Uldaman at the northern edge of the Badlands. He calls Uldaman indurium's true source.",al={"where is indurium ore","indurium ore source"}},{q="Where in the storyline does this step fit?",a="This follows Indurium in the chain that began when Fizzle Brassbolts sent you to Martek the Exiled.",al={"news for fizzle chain","previous quest news for fizzle"}}},kw={"badlands","fizzle brassbolts","indurium","indurium ore","martek the exiled","mirage raceway","shimmering flats","thousand needles","uldaman"},rel={"npc:fizzle-brassbolts","quest:1108","quest:1106","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:uldaman"},m={start="Martek the Exiled",["end"]="Fizzle Brassbolts",level="38",faction="Neutral",id=1137},src={"News for Fizzle"}}
E["quest:1147"] = {t="quest",n="The Swarm Grows",z="thousandneedles",s="At Ironstone Camp, Moktar Krin says Belgrom wants the silithid driven back underground. His war party is too weakened to fight, so you are sent to the dig site south of camp to face them.",h="At Ironstone Camp, Moktar Krin says Belgrom wants the silithid driven back underground.",sec={{t="A Half-Dead War Party",b="Moktar Krin says Belgrom considers the silithid a threat and wants them driven back into the depths they came from. Moktar's war party has already killed the dwarves sent by the Explorers' League, but the fighters are in no state for another battle.\n\nThe dig site lies south of Ironstone Camp, and Moktar expects no more dwarves there. You are to kill the silithid Searchers, hive drones and invaders. Moktar's party cannot leave until the work is done.",sp=0},{t="Moktar's Thanks",b="Moktar jokes that the ichor covering you improves your looks, though you reek of it. He warns you to keep away from the kodo. The smell alone proves you have done your part against the silithid.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the silithid infestation located?",a="The infestation is at the Rustmaul Dig Site, south of Ironstone Camp.",al={"silithid location","where are the bugs","where is the dig site"}},{q="Why can't Moktar Krin's party handle the insects themselves?",a="Moktar's war party is half-dead after killing the dwarves sent by the Explorers' League, and cannot fight another battle in that condition.",al={"why help moktar","why is the war party hurt","moktar party condition"}},{q="Who wants the silithid driven back?",a="Belgrom, who sees the silithid as a threat and wants them pushed back into the depths they came from.",al={"who wants the silithid dead","belgrom silithid order"}},{q="What kinds of silithid must be defeated?",a="You must defeat Silithid Searchers, Silithid Hive Drones and Silithid Invaders, five of each.",al={"which silithid to kill","silithid targets"}},{q="Are there still dwarves at the dig site?",a="Moktar expects no more dwarves at the dig site.",al={"are dwarves at rustmaul","explorers league at dig site"}}},kw={"belgrom","explorers' league","ironstone camp","moktar krin","rustmaul dig site","shimmering flats","silithid","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:rustmaul-dig-site","subzone:ironstone-camp","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:explorers-league","topic:horde"},m={start="Moktar Krin",["end"]="Moktar Krin",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1147},src={"The Swarm Grows (3)"}}
E["quest:1148"] = {t="quest",n="Parts of the Swarm",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, you find a cracked silithid carapace and see how tightly its plating is woven. Korran at the Crossroads wants to study more of these creatures.",h="In Thousand Needles, you find a cracked silithid carapace and see how tightly its plating is woven.",sec={{t="A Curious Carapace",b="You find silithid chitin woven tighter than anything you have seen. The creature's body shows great strength and advanced development. Korran at the Crossroads wants to learn more about the creatures and their origins. He asks for one silithid heart, five silithid talons and three intact silithid carapaces.",sp=0},{t="Specimens for Korran",b="Korran welcomes the specimens. Along with the eggs found in the Field of Giants, they give him a beginning in learning what manner of creatures the insects are and what they seek.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wants these silithid parts?",a="Korran at the Crossroads wants the silithid parts so he can study more of these creatures.",al={"who is korran","turn in parts of the swarm","who studies the silithid"}},{q="Where does this begin?",a="It begins when you inspect a cracked silithid carapace in Thousand Needles.",al={"how to start parts of the swarm","cracked silithid carapace start","where to find the carapace"}},{q="What specimens does Korran want?",a="Korran wants one silithid heart, five silithid talons and three intact silithid carapaces.",al={"what items needed","silithid parts list","what do i gather"}},{q="Why would Korran want to study silithid?",a="Studying more silithid might reveal the creatures' nature and origins.",al={"why study silithid","what korran learns"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you bring the specimens to Korran at the Crossroads."},kw={"carapace","crossroads","field of giants","heart","korran","silithid","talons","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:korran","subzone:crossroads","subzone:field-of-giants","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},m={start="Cracked Silithid Carapace",["end"]="Korran",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1148},src={"Classic quest text: Parts of the Swarm"}}
E["quest:1149"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Faith",z="thousandneedles",s="At Dorn Plainstalker's camp above Thousand Needles, Horde adventurers face a test of faith. The hermit asks them to step from a wooden plank into the chasm and trust their resolve.",h="At Dorn Plainstalker's camp above Thousand Needles, Horde adventurers face a test of faith.",sec={{t="A Measure of the Spirit",b="Above Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker reflects on the mind, body, and spirit. He sets trials to measure what lies within an adventurer instead of relying on simple tribal traditions. Conviction takes many forms, he believes. At its heart is faith strong enough to risk one's life.",sp=0},{t="The Leap into the Void",b="On a stone needle, you stand on weathered planks above empty air. To pass, you step into the abyss without a sure promise of survival. Arcane or spiritual forces break your fall and carry you back to safety. Then you are ready for trials yet to come.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dorn Plainstalker?",a="Dorn Plainstalker is a tauren hermit at a remote cliffside camp above Thousand Needles. He tests Horde adventurers in faith, endurance, and strength.",al={"dorn plainstalker lore","who gives test of faith","quest giver thousand needles"},it="identity"},{q="Will jumping off the plank kill me?",a="No. Though the fall from the needle spire looks fatal, magical warding catches you and teleports you unharmed to Dorn Plainstalker's cave.",al={"do i die jumping","will fall damage kill me test of faith","is test of faith dangerous"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="What happens after passing the Test of Faith?",a="Once Dorn judges your spirit receptive, he challenges your physical resilience in the Test of Endurance.",al={"what comes after test of faith","test of faith chain","dorn plainstalker next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dorn say failure means realizing the vastness of the Nether?",a="Dorn's words are a grim reminder of mortality. He believes those without the inner fire to commit fully risk losing their lives and souls to the endless void beyond the living world.",al={"vastness of the nether meaning","dorn plainstalker nether quote"}},{q="Can Alliance adventurers take this test?",a="No. Dorn Plainstalker offers wisdom and spiritual guidance only to Horde champions traveling through the dangerous canyons of southern Kalimdor.",al={"is test of faith horde only","can alliance do test of faith"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Where does the Test of Faith take place?",a="The trial begins at Dorn's camp in the Thousand Needles canyon walls. Magic connects the camp to an isolated stone spire above the gorge floor.",al={"test of faith location","where is the plank thousand needles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Dorn Plainstalker test your faith?",a="Dorn Plainstalker believes every being is shaped by the spirit, the body, and the mind. While some qualities are shaped by cultural tradition, others can only be discovered deep within yourself. By offering these trials, Dorn aims to measure your inner strength and prepare your spirit for hardship. He demands a blind leap into the canyon winds to prove that you possess belief and trust without guarantee of survival, ensuring your mind is open to the greater challenges ahead.",al={"why does dorn want this done","dorn plainstalker motive","why leap of faith test"},it="motive",add="f9bf32d9"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the Shu'halo, rites of passage across Kalimdor's sacred places are an ancient tradition. Dorn's trial asks you to show trust in the unseen.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you cultivate faith in higher powers. Dorn's trial asks you to put those convictions into action.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face trials of conviction, resilience against hostile lands, and unyielding will. These values bind the fledgling Horde together in Kalimdor."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","horde","leap of faith","planks","test of endurance","test of faith","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","quest:1150","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",level="26",faction="Horde",id=1149},src={"Test of Faith (quest)"}}
E["quest:1150"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Endurance",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, challengers face the second rite in Dorn Plainstalker's spiritual trials. After proving their courage of spirit, they enter Roguefeather Den to test their physical endurance and draw out its fierce leader, Grenka Bloodscreech.",h="In Thousand Needles, challengers face the second rite in Dorn Plainstalker's spiritual trials.",sec={{t="Testing the Body",b="At the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker prepares young warriors for a wider, harsher world. This trial tests the body's strength. Dorn believes readiness calls for spiritual devotion, mental discipline, and the stamina to endure sustained brutality.",sp=0},{t="Incursion into Roguefeather Den",b="Roguefeather Den lies within Screeching Canyon, west of Freewind Post. Hostile harpies fill the cavern, making it perilous to wander in alone. Challengers fight deep into the roost and vandalize the harpies' gathered provisions. Then they endure the flock's fierce retaliation until its matriarch, Grenka Bloodscreech, enters the fight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Test of Endurance?",a="Dorn Plainstalker, an elder tauren, gives the Test of Endurance from the Weathered Nook in Thousand Needles' canyon bluffs.",al={"quest giver test of endurance","who starts test of endurance","dorn plainstalker quest"},gp=true},{q="Where is Roguefeather Den located?",a="Roguefeather Den lies high along Thousand Needles' southern canyon walls, west of Freewind Post. A winding path through Screeching Canyon climbs to the ramp leading to the cave entrance.",al={"roguefeather den location","where is harpy cave","screeching canyon ramp"},gp=true},{q="How do you summon Grenka Bloodscreech?",a="You draw Grenka Bloodscreech out by fighting to Roguefeather Den's deepest chambers and vandalizing the harpies' stored food and supplies. She appears to defend her roost.",al={"summon grenka","how to spawn grenka bloodscreech","find grenka"},gp=true},{q="What comes after the Test of Endurance?",a="When you return Grenka's severed claw to Dorn Plainstalker, he accepts it as proof of your physical stamina and sends you to the Test of Strength.",al={"next quest after endurance","what follows test of endurance","dorn plainstalker next test"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dorn test adventurers who aren't tauren?",a="Dorn believes his calling is to mentor all Horde youth, whatever their race or tribe. He sees untested pride as a death sentence in the wider world and insists every warrior prove readiness in body, mind, and spirit.",al={"why does dorn help horde","dorn plainstalker philosophy","tauren trials for other races"},it="why_me"},{q="What was the trial before this one?",a="The Test of Faith comes before the Test of Endurance. In that perilous leap of devotion, Dorn tests whether a challenger's spirit will falter in the face of fear.",al={"previous quest","test before endurance","first trial"}},{q="Why does Dorn Plainstalker want this done?",a="Dorn Plainstalker sees it as his sacred obligation to prepare young adventurers for the deadly perils of the wider world. After ensuring your spirit and faith were intact, he insists on testing your physical body. By forcing you to weather wave after wave of furious harpies deep inside their own territory, he ensures you possess the stamina and resolve required to survive beyond the safety of home.",al={"why dorn test endurance","dorn plainstalker motive","purpose of test of endurance"},it="motive",add="8999be4f"},{q="What is Grenka's Claw for?",a="The claw serves as undeniable proof that you stood your ground in the heart of Roguefeather Den, survived the harpies' sustained onslaught, and struck down their fierce matriarch, Grenka Bloodscreech. Dorn requires it to confirm that your endurance held up under relentless assault before he will present your next trial.",al={"grenkas claw use","why do i need grenkas claw","grenka claw purpose"},it="item",add="b2efd71b"},{q="Who is Grenka Bloodscreech?",a="Grenka Bloodscreech is a formidable leader among the Roguefeather harpies infesting the canyon caverns west of Freewind Post. Vicious and highly territorial, she rules the flock's inner sanctuary. When you storm deep into Roguefeather Den and smash their hoarded provisions, her fury draws her down from the roost to slay you herself.",al={"who is grenka","grenka bloodscreech lore","roguefeather harpy leader"},it="target",add="28ecd26a"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see Dorn Plainstalker's trials as rites of passage. They test whether your physical stamina matches the Earth Mother's spiritual guidance.",["faction:Horde"]="Dorn offers these challenges to every Horde race. He believes young warriors from every tribe must be tempered by hardship before facing Kalimdor's perils."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","freewind post","grenka bloodscreech","roguefeather den","screeching canyon","test of endurance","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","quest:1149","quest:1151","subzone:roguefeather-den","subzone:weathered-nook","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:harpy"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1150,ri={"Grenka's Claw"}},src={"Test of Endurance"}}
E["quest:1151"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Strength",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker asks you to prove your strength. Your trial brings you against Rok'Alim the Pounder, an ancient rock elemental, and calls for pieces of his shattered form.",h="In Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker asks you to prove your strength.",sec={{t="Remnants of the Old Gods' Age",b="Long ago, primordial elementals covered the world and served the Old Gods. When those powers were overthrown and sealed beneath the earth, the spirits lost their hold on this realm. Most faded from the physical world unless modern spellcraft bound and summoned them. A few were strong enough to remain on Azeroth without such magic. Rok'Alim the Pounder is one of them, wandering the arid canyons of Thousand Needles as an echo of that age.",sp=0},{t="The Pounder of Thousand Needles",b="The centaur clans named Rok'Alim for the deafening crashes of his stone fists against the canyon floor. Anyone who crosses his path risks being hammered into dust. Dorn Plainstalker sends initiates to face this force of raw might and prove their warrior spirit. They return with fragments of the elemental's stony heart as proof of victory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this quest begin and end?",a="Dorn Plainstalker offers and completes the trial at Weathered Nook, a secluded canyon camp high among the spires of Thousand Needles.",al={"quest giver","where to turn in","dorn location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Rok'Alim the Pounder?",a="Rok'Alim is an ancient rock elemental who has endured in Kalimdor since the age of the Old Gods. His innate power lets him remain physically present on Azeroth without being summoned.",al={"who is rokalim","what kind of mob is rokalim","elemental lore"},it="target"},{q="Why do the centaur call him 'the Pounder'?",a="The centaur tribes call Rok'Alim the Pounder for the thunderous shockwaves his stone fists unleash when they smash anything in his path.",al={"the pounder nickname","centaur name for rokalim"},it="name"},{q="Where can Rok'Alim be found in the canyon?",a="Rok'Alim wanders the northwestern stretches of Thousand Needles, usually patrolling open ground south of the main road across the canyon floor.",al={"rokalim spawn","where is rokalim"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What place does this quest hold in the overall trial chain?",a="This is the third trial in the chain, after the Test of Faith and the Test of Endurance. It comes before the final trial, the Test of Lore.",al={"quest chain order","what comes next","what comes before"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Dorn require an elemental to be slain instead of a beast or enemy?",a="Dorn chooses Rok'Alim because the elemental is living stone and an unyielding, primordial force. Overcoming him proves your physical strength against the raw, unbending earth itself.",al={"why kill an elemental","purpose of test of strength"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Dorn Plainstalker want this done?",a="Dorn Plainstalker is putting you through an ancient tauren rite to prove your mettle before advancing to the final trials. Facing a mere beast or soldier would not truly gauge your might, so he demands you challenge an enduring remnant of primordial stone. Slaying Rok'Alim proves that your inner and physical strength can overcome even ancient elemental forces.",al={"dorn plainstalker motive","why does dorn want rokalim killed","why take the test of strength"},it="motive",add="d3b1c16f"},{q="What are the Fragments of Rok'Alim for?",a="The fragments serve as incontrovertible proof that you stood before Rok'Alim the Pounder and reduced the ancient elemental to rubble. Dorn Plainstalker requires physical evidence of your victory to acknowledge that you have fulfilled the Test of Strength and earned passage to the next trial.",al={"fragments of rokalim use","what are the fragments for","why collect rokalim fragments"},it="item",add="67dd1d0a"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren pilgrim, you face an untamed spirit of stone in a traditional test of harmony and physical will. You show that you can endure and overcome the harshest forces of the Earth Mother.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you recognize Rok'Alim as a dangerous, unbound spirit of earth. His refusal to yield disturbs the local balance of spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you earn the respect of the Thunder Bluff elders by completing the Weathered Nook rites. You build your reputation across Kalimdor."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","old gods","rock elemental","rok'alim","test of strength","the pounder","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","subzone:weathered-nook","quest:1150","quest:1152","quest:1149","zone:thousandneedles","topic:old-god","topic:centaur"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1151,ri={"Fragments of Rok'Alim"}},src={"Test of Strength"}}
E["quest:1152"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker sends Horde champions north to face a trial of the world's history. Braug Dimspirit waits in Stonetalon Mountains to test what they know of Azeroth and its shared suffering.",h="In Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker sends Horde champions north to face a trial of the world's history.",sec={{t="From Faith to Lore",b="At the Weathered Nook, Dorn Plainstalker tests initiates in faith, endurance, and combat. Yet strength and faith alone do not make a true Horde champion. Dorn knows the bounds of what he can teach, so he sends those who have proved themselves to Stonetalon Mountains. There, an elder shaman will test their minds and knowledge of the world.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Stonetalon",b="The road runs north over the Barrens' dry scrub and into the crags of Stonetalon. High in the mountains, near the entrance to Talondeep Path, Braug Dimspirit keeps his hermitage. The cavern cuts through the rock toward Ashenvale. From there, Braug looks upon a frontier at war: goblin logging ventures despoil the forests, while hostile night elves fiercely defend their ancestral borders.",sp=0},{t="A Broader Perspective",b="Braug Dimspirit asks champions to look beyond factional pride. He speaks of Azeroth's tragic state and the blame laid on orcs and Forsaken for war and corruption. Yet almost every civilization shares responsibility for the land's plight. Goblins tear down ancient timber, and night elves distrust the younger races. To pass the trial, a champion must see beyond these enmities and understand the history of a wounded world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Test of Lore?",a="The Test of Lore is one trial in a rite of passage shaped by tauren elders. Initiates show physical might and faith, along with knowledge of history and Azeroth's shared past.",al={"test of lore meaning","what is this quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Braug Dimspirit?",a="Braug Dimspirit lives high in the Stonetalon Mountains, near Windshear Crag and the entrance to Talondeep Path. The cave links Stonetalon to Ashenvale.",al={"braug dimspirit location","where is braug"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Dorn Plainstalker send you away?",a="Dorn Plainstalker oversees the trials of faith, endurance, and strength in Thousand Needles. The world's lore lies beyond what he can teach, so he sends worthy initiates to Braug, a shaman wise enough to test their minds.",al={"why stonetalon","why dorn sends you"},it="motive"},{q="What threats should travelers look out for on the way?",a="Dorn warns that night elves prowl the borderlands near Ashenvale and Stonetalon, where they see the Horde as an intruder. Volatile goblin logging operations also fill the area around Windshear Crag.",al={"dangers to braug","talondeep path danger"},it="danger"},{q="What is Braug Dimspirit's view of the world's conflicts?",a="Braug Dimspirit believes all mortal races share blame for the world's suffering. Orcs and Forsaken often bear blame from their rivals, while goblin greed and night elven arrogance have also harmed Kalimdor and Lordaeron.",al={"braug dimspirit philosophy","what does braug believe"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Talondeep Path?",a="Talondeep Path is a mountain tunnel linking Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains with the ancient woodland borders of southern Ashenvale.",al={"what is talondeep path","talondeep cave"},it="place"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you face trials that prize spiritual harmony and knowledge of history above raw bloodlust.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can read the land's suffering in reckless deeds, from goblin exploitation to ancient elven isolation.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you must reckon with your allies' reputations. Orcs and Forsaken share responsibility with others for the land's troubles."},kw={"braug dimspirit","dorn plainstalker","stonetalon mountains","talondeep path","test of lore","thousand needles","weathered nook","windshear crag"},rel={"quest:1151","quest:1149","npc:dorn-plainstalker","subzone:weathered-nook","subzone:talondeep-path","subzone:windshear-crag","zone:stonetalon","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Dorn Plainstalker",["end"]="Braug Dimspirit",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1152},src={"Test of Lore"}}
E["quest:1154"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="At Talondeep Path, Horde seekers face the Test of Lore. Braug Dimspirit asks them to find and study a tome of dragon history before he tests what they remember.",h="At Talondeep Path, Horde seekers face the Test of Lore.",sec={{t="A Shift in the Trials",b="After trials across Thousand Needles' salt flats and plateaus, Dorn Plainstalker's candidates travel north to Braug Dimspirit in the Stonetalon Mountains. He waits near the mouth of Talondeep Path. Braug counts those earlier trials as tests of body and faith. Yet the Horde also needs disciplined minds and knowledge of ancient history, not only skill against beasts.",sp=0},{t="The Shadows of Dor'Danil",b="Braug sends seekers through Talondeep Path into southern Ashenvale. Beneath the trees south of Splintertree Post lies Dor'Danil Barrow Den, a dangerous ruin haunted by fallen night elf druids and the creatures that slaughtered them. Deep in its lower chambers, a stone podium holds 'Legacy of the Aspects'. The rare manuscript tells of the ancient creation and corruption of the great Dragon Aspects.",sp=0},{t="Study or Suffer",b="Braug's trial asks you to learn the tome's teachings before you hand it over. He takes the book and tests your memory of the Titan-empowered protectors and the betrayal that gave birth to Deathwing. Fail, or guess poorly, and you are banished across Kalimdor to Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens. Then you must journey back to Stonetalon in disgrace.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Braug Dimspirit?",a="Braug Dimspirit is an elder tauren shaman near Talondeep Path's entrance in the Stonetalon Mountains. After Dorn Plainstalker's earlier trials, Braug tests whether Horde champions match martial strength with knowledge and intellect.",al={"braug dimspirit","who gives test of lore","stonetalon quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the book Legacy of the Aspects located?",a="'Legacy of the Aspects' rests inside Dor'Danil Barrow Den in southern Ashenvale, almost directly south of Splintertree Post. Deep beneath the barrows, it lies on a stone podium atop a central platform.",al={"legacy of the aspects location","where is the book","dor danil book spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What lurks inside Dor'Danil Barrow Den?",a="Dor'Danil Barrow Den was once a sanctuary for night elf druids. Restless spirits of the dead druids and the lethal creatures that butchered them haunt its hollows, making the ruin dangerous to cross.",al={"dor danil enemies","who guards the book","ashenvale barrow den"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Braug make me read the book before turning it in?",a="Braug takes the book when you return and tests your memory. He expects you to study it first, for he measures what you know as well as whether you can retrieve the volume.",al={"why read legacy of aspects","quiz test of lore","what happens if i fail the question"},sp=1,it="motive"},{q="How does this quest fit into the broader trial series?",a="This trial follows the Test of Faith that Dorn Plainstalker began at the Weathered Nook in Thousand Needles. Dorn tested your nerve and survival against deadly odds. Braug tests your knowledge of lore and history.",al={"test of faith chain","what comes before test of lore","dorn plainstalker trials"},it="history"},{q="What is the subject matter of the Legacy of the Aspects?",a="'Legacy of the Aspects' tells how the Titans empowered the five great Dragon Aspects to safeguard Azeroth. It also tells of Neltharion the Earth-Warder's fall and his change into the destroyer known as Deathwing.",al={"legacy of the aspects story","book lore","what is the book about"},it="item"},{q="Why does Braug Dimspirit require me to find the Legacy of the Aspects?",a="Braug Dimspirit is testing your mind rather than your strength. Having already endured Dorn Plainstalker's physical trials, you are now being judged on your intellect, resourcefulness, and willingness to learn. By sending you alone into dangerous territory to recover and absorb ancient knowledge, Braug determines whether you possess the wisdom worthy of completing the trial series.",al={"why does braug test me","why the legacy of the aspects","why braug dimspirit test"},it="why_me",add="0efda427"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face a trial meant to prepare you for Kalimdor's deep history and Ashenvale's perilous elven ruins. Ignorance can leave you overcome there.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you encounter the tragedy of night elf kin slain and corrupted in Dor'Danil Barrow Den. They once slept there in communion with the Emerald Dream."},kw={"ashenvale","braug dimspirit","camp taurajo","deathwing","dor'danil barrow den","dorn plainstalker","legacy of the aspects","talondeep path","test of lore"},rel={"quest:1152","quest:1149","subzone:dor-danil-barrow-den","subzone:talondeep-path","npc:dorn-plainstalker","npc:deathwing","topic:titan","subzone:camp-taurajo"},m={start="Braug Dimspirit",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1154,ri={"Legacy of the Aspects"}},src={"Test of Lore (2)"}}
E["quest:1159"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="Across the Great Sea, Horde seekers now carry the Test of Lore to the ruins of Lordaeron. You have answered Braug Dimspirit's first riddle in the Stonetalon Mountains. Now he sends you to a former human scholar among the Forsaken in Undercity.",h="Across the Great Sea, Horde seekers now carry the Test of Lore to the ruins of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="A Scholarly Alliance",b="After you prove your mettle and learn the Dragon Aspects' history in the Legacy of the Aspects, Braug Dimspirit admits his knowledge has limits. The trial now reaches beyond Kalimdor and shows the Horde's far-reaching ties. So Braug sends you toward the undead capital beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="The Sceptical Historian",b="Parqual Fintallas lives in the damp corridors of the Apothecarium. Once a respected human chronicler of the northern kingdoms, he kept seeking knowledge through the Scourge and his transformation into one of the Forsaken. You arrive as an outsider, claiming to have completed the spiritual and physical trials of Thousand Needles. Parqual doubts you are more than an opportunistic mercenary, and expects you to prove your worth to him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does a tauren trial send me all the way to Undercity?",a="Braug Dimspirit knows mastering lore means learning more than Kalimdor's history. He sends you to Parqual Fintallas, a renowned human scholar whose knowledge survived Lordaeron's fall and his transformation into undeath. Parqual will test your understanding of world history.",al={"why go to undercity","why lordaeron","braug sending to undead"},it="purpose"},{q="Where exactly is Parqual Fintallas located?",a="Parqual Fintallas is in Undercity, along the southern bridge in the Apothecarium quarter.",al={"where is parqual","parqual location","find fintallas"},gp=true},{q="Who was Parqual Fintallas in life?",a="In life, Parqual Fintallas was an accomplished human historian in the kingdom of Lordaeron. The Plague of Undeath claimed him, and he joined Sylvanas's Forsaken. He kept studying, turning his intellect to darker inquiries.",al={"parqual fintallas lore","who is parqual","fintallas backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why doesn't Parqual believe Braug sent me?",a="Parqual distrusts outsiders. He cannot believe an ordinary adventurer could leap from Thousand Needles' spires, defeat primeval elementals, and retrieve ancient relics. He suspects you only overheard tavern rumors.",al={"why is parqual rude","parqual reaction","parqual doesn't believe me"},it="conflict"},{q="What larger trial is this quest part of?",a="The Test of Lore grew from the trial Dorn Plainstalker began at the Weathered Nook, and this is its midpoint. It tests combat prowess, courage, intellect, and historical knowledge worthy of a Horde champion.",al={"what chain is this","test of faith chain","what is test of lore"},it="history"},{q="What comes next after reaching Parqual?",a="Parqual will ask his own historical riddle only after you undertake an errand for him in the Eastern Kingdoms. He wants proof that you are the capable hero Braug claims you to be.",al={"what next after parqual","next quest after undercity","after talking to fintallas"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Braug Dimspirit send you to Undercity?",a="Braug Dimspirit has tested your initial knowledge, but his role is only to guide you through the first stage of the Test of Lore. To truly challenge your understanding of the world, he recognizes that the next question requires a perspective beyond his own. He sends you to Parqual Fintallas—a famed historian from Lordaeron now among the Forsaken—so your devotion to history and truth can be judged by a scholar who pursues enlightenment of an entirely different nature.",al={"why does braug send me","braug dimspirit motive","why go to undercity braug"},it="motive",add="670eb265"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Meeting Parqual shows how Forsaken scholars like him kept the academic traditions and records of fallen Lordaeron despite rot and undeath.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren initiate, you leave Kalimdor's open plains and high mesas for Undercity's poisonous, cramped sewers. The journey tests your understanding of another culture as well as history.",["faction:Horde"]="The Test of Lore reveals the ties between the newly forged Horde's peoples. It brings tauren seekers together with Lordaeron's grim archivists."},kw={"apothecarium","braug dimspirit","dorn plainstalker","lordaeron","parqual fintallas","test of lore","thousand needles","undercity","weathered nook"},rel={"quest:1152","npc:parqual-fintallas","zone:undercity","subzone:apothecarium","quest:1149","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:weathered-nook","npc:dorn-plainstalker"},m={start="Braug Dimspirit",["end"]="Parqual Fintallas",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1159},src={"Test of Lore (4)"}}
E["quest:1174"] = {t="quest",n="Gnomes Win!",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, the gnomes' victory decides which ticket pays out. The holder of the winning ticket gets a prize box.",h="In Thousand Needles, the gnomes' victory decides which ticket pays out.",sec={{t="The Gnome Ticket",b="When the gnomes win, the holder of the Gnome Race Ticket gets the prize box. The goblin ticket counts for the other side of the race.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Gnome Race Ticket?",a="The Gnome Race Ticket backs the gnome side of the race in Thousand Needles. It matters when the gnomes win.",al={"gnome ticket","what is gnome race ticket","race ticket purpose"}},{q="What do you get when the gnomes win?",a="Whoever holds the Gnome Race Ticket when the gnomes win gets a gnome prize box.",al={"gnome prize box","gnomes win prize"}},{q="Who can take part in this wager?",a="The wager belongs to neither faction. Alliance and Horde travelers stand on equal footing.",al={"can horde bet","can alliance bet","neutral ticket"}},{q="What happens if the goblins win instead?",a="If the goblins win, the goblin ticket matters. That result is called Goblins Win!, the counterpart to this one.",al={"goblins win","goblin race ticket"}}},kw={"gnome race ticket","gnome prize box","gnomes win","races","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Automatic",level="1",faction="Neutral",id=1174},src={"Wowpedia: Gnomes Win!"}}
E["quest:1175"] = {t="quest",n="A Bump in the Road",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Trackmaster Zherin needs the growing beasts kept from the track. You are asked to thin the Saltstone Basilisks, Crystalhides and Gazers before they wander onto it.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Trackmaster Zherin needs the growing beasts kept from the track.",sec={{t="Keeping the Track Clear",b="A basilisk once struck the goblins' racer, the Red Thunder. After the crash, Kronkrider hired Zherin to watch over the Mirage Raceway track. Zherin does not know what the beasts on the Shimmering Flats are eating. He knows only that they have grown too big.\n\nTheir numbers must be kept down before one strays onto the course during a race. Clearing wreckage is bad enough. Zherin would rather not pick burnt animal parts out of it as well.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Trackmaster Zherin?",a="Trackmaster Zherin looks after the Mirage Raceway track on the Shimmering Flats. Kronkrider hired him for the work.",al={"who is zherin","trackmaster zherin","zherin lore"}},{q="Why are the basilisks being hunted?",a="The beasts on the flats have grown big, and one straying onto the track during a race could cause a crash. A basilisk already collided with the goblins' Red Thunder.",al={"why kill basilisks","why basilisks must die","basilisk problem"}},{q="What is the Red Thunder?",a="The Red Thunder is a racer belonging to the goblins. A basilisk collision wrecked it.",al={"red thunder","red thunder crash","goblin red thunder"}},{q="Where are the basilisks usually found on the flats?",a="Basilisks roam all over the Shimmering Flats, but gather more thickly near Weazel's Crater and among the Tahonda Ruins.",al={"basilisk locations","where are the basilisks","where to find saltstone"}}},kw={"crystalhide","gazer","mirage raceway","red thunder","saltstone basilisk","shimmering flats","tahonda ruins","trackmaster zherin","weazel's crater"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:weazel-s-crater","subzone:tahonda-ruins"},m={start="Trackmaster Zherin",["end"]="Trackmaster Zherin",level="33",id=1175},src={"A Bump in the Road"}}
E["quest:1176"] = {t="quest",n="Load Lightening",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, Pozzik’s goblin crew seeks lighter parts for its racers. Hollow vulture bones may strengthen the steering and frame without adding heavy metal.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, Pozzik’s goblin crew seeks lighter parts for its racers.",sec={{t="Every Ounce Counts",b="Across the Shimmering Flats, goblin and gnome engineers race to win by fractions of a second. Raw engine thrust matters little if a car carries too much weight. Gnome teams favor intricate gears and brass fittings. Pozzik’s goblins strip away dense iron framing and replace it with lighter hollow parts wherever they can.",sp=0},{t="Desert Scavenging for Speed",b="Pozzik looks to the salt wastes around Thousand Needles instead of importing costly composites. Salt Flats vultures are plentiful, and their bones are hollow, honeycombed, strong under strain, and light. His mechanics work them into the racers’ steering rigs and smaller braces. They hope the machines can outmaneuver the gnomes without shaking apart at top speed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Pozzik want vulture bones for a race car?",a="Goblin engineers use vulture bones because they are hollow and light. Worked into delicate parts such as the steering rig, they add strength without weighing down the racer.",al={"vulture bones purpose","why bones","pozzik bones"},it="item"},{q="Who is Pozzik?",a="Pozzik leads the goblin racing crew at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats. He directs the goblin pits against their gnome rivals.",al={"pozzik","pozzik lore","who is the goblin engineer"},it="identity"},{q="Where are these vultures found?",a="Vultures circle the open Shimmering Flats, especially near the huge skeletal remains scattered across the northeastern salt basin.",al={"vulture location","where to find hollow bones","shimmering flats scavengers"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What is the Mirage Raceway?",a="The Mirage Raceway is a neutral racing ground on Thousand Needles’ dry salt lake. Goblins and gnomes race dangerous experimental rocket-cars there.",al={"raceway lore","what is mirage raceway","shimmering flats track"},it="place"},{q="Are the gnomes doing the same thing?",a="The gnomes also seek lighter racers, but their tradition favors precision clockwork and complex metals. Goblin mechanics rely more on salvage and improvised parts.",al={"gnome racers","gnome vs goblin","are gnomes using bones"},it="conflict"},{q="Does this work help with Pozzik's larger racing effort?",a="Yes. Lightening the racer earns Pozzik’s trust and leads to more work amid the rivalries and goblin sponsorship on the flats.",al={"quest continuation","what comes next","goblin sponsorship"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Pozzik so focused on lightening his racer?",a="At the Mirage Raceway, speed is everything, and races often come down to tiny fractions of an advantage. Pozzik is competing directly against gnome engineering, where any excess bulk can cost him a victory on the salt flats. Shaving every spare ounce off the frame and steering rig allows his rocket car to reach maximum acceleration without sacrificing structural integrity.",al={"pozzik motive","why lighten racer","why does pozzik need light parts"},it="motive",add="a8fc0189"},{q="Why are there so many vultures in the Shimmering Flats?",a="The Shimmering Flats are an unforgiving, sun-baked expanse littered with the remains of massive ancient beasts and fallen wanderers. Salt scavengers thrive out here by circling overhead and feeding on the carrion left behind by the harsh desert climate and the flats' violent basilisk and scorpid populations.",al={"why vultures shimmering flats","salt flats vultures lore","thousand needles vultures"},it="target",add="8208273d"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Pozzik’s use of bird bones shows goblin ingenuity: practical, improvised, and effective at reducing a racer’s weight.",["race:Gnome"]="A classically trained Tinker Town engineer might be scandalized to see goblins lash scavenged bird carcasses into steering rigs."},kw={"bones","load lightening","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","vulture"},rel={"npc:pozzik","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin"},m={start="Pozzik",level="30",faction="Neutral",id=1176,ri={"Hollow Vulture Bone"}},src={"Load Lightening"}}
E["quest:1178"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Sponsorship",z="thousandneedles",s="The goblin racers are waiting on a promised part as the gnomes gain ground. Pozzik sends you to Ratchet to ask Gazlowe what happened.",h="The goblin racers are waiting on a promised part as the gnomes gain ground.",sec={{t="A Promised Part",b="Pozzik calls the racing team the pride of goblins. Many people help it in one way or another. Gazlowe searches the world for parts and once came to work on one of its rigs.\n\nWeeks ago, Gazlowe promised a new prototype fuel regulator, but it has not arrived. He is usually prompt, so Pozzik asks you to go to Ratchet and learn what happened. The gnomes are gaining.",sp=0},{t="Words About Pozzik",b="Before retiring to work with the racers, Pozzik was one of Undermine's most respected tinkerers, Gazlowe recalls. His first act on joining the team was to design its two engine model racers.\n\nGazlowe admits the Tinkers' Union may suffer without Pozzik. Still, he says nothing beats the races.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Pozzik need you to go to Ratchet?",a="Weeks ago, Gazlowe promised a prototype fuel regulator, but it has not arrived. Pozzik asks you to go to Ratchet and ask what happened.",al={"why ratchet","pozzik errand","goblin sponsorship objective"}},{q="What does Gazlowe do for the racing team?",a="Gazlowe searches the world for parts for the team. He once came to work on one of its rigs.",al={"gazlowe involvement","gazlowe raceway sponsor","is gazlowe a sponsor"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows Load Lightening, also given by Pozzik.",al={"goblin sponsorship prequest","what quest comes before goblin sponsorship"}},{q="Why is the goblin team in a hurry?",a="Pozzik says the gnomes are gaining on the goblin team.",al={"why rush fuel regulator","goblin vs gnome race"}}},kw={"fuel regulator","gazlowe","mirage raceway","pozzik","ratchet","shimmering flats","tinkers union","undermine"},rel={"npc:pozzik","quest:1176","quest:1180","subzone:ratchet","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},m={start="Pozzik",["end"]="Gazlowe",level="37",id=1178},src={"Goblin Sponsorship"}}
E["quest:1179"] = {t="quest",n="The Brassbolts Brothers",z="thousandneedles",s="Pilot Longbeard in Ironforge needs a traveler to carry helmets to the Brassbolts Brothers. Their test drivers keep crashing rocket cars at the Shimmering Flats, so the gnomes need head protection.",h="Pilot Longbeard in Ironforge needs a traveler to carry helmets to the Brassbolts Brothers.",sec={{t="A Long-Distance Favor",b="Pilot Longbeard, a dwarven aviator in Ironforge, has an urgent request from the Shimmering Flats in southern Kalimdor. His friends, the inventive gnome Brassbolts brothers, have settled on its vast salt pans to race experimental machines. Longbeard's military and piloting duties keep him busy, so he cannot carry their supplies himself.",sp=0},{t="Safety at High Velocity",b="The Brassbolts' rocket car races across the salt beds at extraordinary speed. Yet its test drivers keep crashing and suffering severe concussions. Longbeard has gathered a crate of heavy-duty dwarven Siege Engine helmets to protect them. You carry the crate across the sea to Kalimdor, giving the gnomes the protection they need to bring reluctant pilots back behind the wheel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Pilot Longbeard?",a="Pilot Longbeard is a dwarven siege engine pilot in Ironforge. He is a friend and supply contact for the Brassbolts brothers in the Eastern Kingdoms, where he can obtain heavy dwarven gear they cannot easily make in the field.",al={"pilot longbeard","quest giver","who gives this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who are the Brassbolts brothers?",a="The Brassbolts brothers are ambitious gnomish engineers, including Wizzle Brassbolts. At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, they design and tune rocket cars to outrun goblin competitors.",al={"brassbolts brothers","wizzle brassbolts","gnome brothers"},it="people"},{q="Where is the Shimmering Flats?",a="The Shimmering Flats is a vast, sun-baked salt plain in southern Kalimdor, beyond the tall canyon pillars of Thousand Needles. Its broad, obstacle-free stretch suits the testing of fast experimental vehicles.",al={"shimmering flats location","where to deliver","where is race track"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the gnomes need Siege Engine helmets?",a="The Brassbolts need Siege Engine helmets because their rocket car is extremely fast, while its steering and stability are poor. Crashes and concussions became so common that no test pilots would drive without substantial dwarven head protection.",al={"why helmets","crash helmets","rocket car crashes"},it="motive"},{q="Why doesn't Longbeard deliver them himself?",a="Pilot Longbeard is occupied with military duties in Ironforge. The long voyage across the Great Sea to southern Kalimdor would mean abandoning his post, so he relies on travelers to carry the heavy crate.",al={"why not longbeard","longbeard duties"},it="why_me"},{q="Can Horde players complete this task?",a="No. Pilot Longbeard offers this work in Ironforge, the Alliance capital, so only Alliance couriers can take it. The Mirage Raceway itself welcomes both factions.",al={"is this alliance only","horde version","faction"},gp=true}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see the Brassbolts prize mechanical innovation above details like braking and their drivers' longevity.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know sturdy dwarven Siege Engine armor is thick enough to withstand a full-throttle collision on the salt flats.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate how this supply run joins dwarven heavy-armor craftsmanship with gnomish high-velocity experiments."},kw={"brassbolts","ironforge","mirage raceway","pilot longbeard","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles","wizzle brassbolts"},rel={"npc:wizzle-brassbolts","npc:pilot-longbeard","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},m={start="Pilot Longbeard",["end"]="Wizzle Brassbolts",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1179},src={"The Brassbolts Brothers"}}
E["quest:1180"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Sponsorship",z="thousandneedles",s="Gazlowe in Ratchet still waits for the fuel regulator he promised Pozzik. Revilgaz in Booty Bay said he would ship it, but it has not arrived. So Gazlowe sends you to Wharfmaster Lozgil at the far northwestern end of the Booty Bay docks to check the cargo records.",h="Gazlowe in Ratchet still waits for the fuel regulator he promised Pozzik.",sec={{t="A Part That Never Came",b="Gazlowe promised Pozzik a new fuel regulator, but it has not reached Ratchet. Revilgaz in Booty Bay said he would ship it over. Perhaps the part slipped through the cracks. If it never left, there may be little to do. Still, you can find out whether it departed Booty Bay. Wharfmaster Lozgil, at the far northwestern end of the docks, can search the cargo records.",sp=0},{t="The Wharfmaster's Records",b="Wharfmaster Lozgil checks the logbooks for shipments to Ratchet. The latest entry is boots from Drizzlik. Earlier shipments carried building supplies and tools. No race parts appear in the records.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What part is missing?",a="Gazlowe promised Pozzik a new fuel regulator, but it has not reached Gazlowe in Ratchet.",al={"pozzik part","why fuel regulator","pozzik shipment"}},{q="Who said they would send the regulator to Ratchet?",a="Revilgaz in Booty Bay said he would ship the regulator to Gazlowe in Ratchet.",al={"who sends the part","revilgaz part","who has the fuel regulator"}},{q="Who keeps the shipping records in Booty Bay?",a="Wharfmaster Lozgil keeps the shipping records in Booty Bay. He is at the far northwestern end of the Booty Bay docks.",al={"booty bay cargo master","who is wharfmaster lozgil","where is lozgil"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the chain?",a="This follows the first Goblin Sponsorship, when Pozzik sent you to Gazlowe. The next step is Goblin Sponsorship 3.",al={"goblin sponsorship chain","quest progression","what comes before this"}}},kw={"booty bay","fuel regulator","gazlowe","goblin sponsorship","mirage raceway","pozzik","ratchet","revilgaz","wharfmaster lozgil"},rel={"quest:1178","quest:1181","subzone:mirage-raceway","npc:pozzik","subzone:ratchet","subzone:booty-bay","topic:goblin","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Gazlowe",["end"]="Wharfmaster Lozgil",level="37",id=1180},src={"Goblin Sponsorship (2)"}}
E["quest:1181"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Sponsorship",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Mirage Raceway, the goblin racers still need their missing fuel regulator. Wharfmaster Lozgil sends you to Baron Revilgaz in Booty Bay for help.",h="At the Mirage Raceway, the goblin racers still need their missing fuel regulator.",sec={{t="Asking the Baron",b="Wharfmaster Lozgil can do little more to trace the missing shipment bound for Ratchet. He sends you to Baron Revilgaz, since the Baron knows his own business best. You will find him on the top floor of the tavern across the harbor in Booty Bay.",sp=0},{t="The Baron's Answer",b="Baron Revilgaz knows about the missing fuel regulator but cannot help. Some of his men went to find its blueprints and returned empty-handed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Baron Revilgaz?",a="Baron Revilgaz is on the top floor of the tavern across the harbor in Booty Bay.",al={"baron revilgaz location","where is revilgaz","find revilgaz booty bay"}},{q="Why does Wharfmaster Lozgil send you to Revilgaz?",a="Wharfmaster Lozgil can do little more to help, and says the Baron knows his own business best.",al={"why talk to revilgaz","lozgil sends to baron","why see baron revilgaz"}},{q="What shipment is being tracked down?",a="The shipment is a new fuel regulator bound for Ratchet, for the goblin racers of the Mirage Raceway.",al={"what shipment is missing","what are we looking for","missing ratchet cargo"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the chain?",a="This follows your talk with Wharfmaster Lozgil in Goblin Sponsorship two. The next step is Goblin Sponsorship four.",al={"what came before goblin sponsorship 3","chain progress goblin sponsorship"}}},kw={"baron revilgaz","booty bay","fuel regulator","goblin sponsorship","mirage raceway","ratchet","wharfmaster lozgil"},rel={"npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:ratchet","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin","quest:1180","quest:1182"},m={start="Wharfmaster Lozgil",["end"]="Baron Revilgaz",level="37",id=1181},src={"Goblin Sponsorship (3)"}}
E["quest:1182"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Sponsorship",z="thousandneedles",s="Baron Revilgaz is seeking the Venture Company’s new fuel regulator plans for Pozzik at Lake Nazferiti. Foreman Cozzle has outsmarted him, so the Baron sends you after the blueprints.",h="Baron Revilgaz is seeking the Venture Company’s new fuel regulator plans for Pozzik at Lake Nazferiti.",sec={{t="The Foreman's Blueprints",b="Baron Revilgaz says the Venture Company’s shredders at Lake Nazferiti in northern Stranglethorn carry a new model of fuel regulator. Pozzik could use its details, but Foreman Cozzle has proved cleverer than the Baron expected. So Revilgaz believes you may have better luck finding the plans.\n\nThe blueprints are kept in Cozzle’s house, almost certainly under lock and key. The Venture Company’s base lies around Lake Nazferiti, in the vale’s north-eastern corner. Cozzle keeps the key in his cabin atop the oil tower. The box of blueprints is in the small house near the tower’s base. Revilgaz admits the gnome team there is good, and his team needs every advantage it can find.",sp=0},{t="A Copy for the Baron",b="Revilgaz wants a copy of the blueprints for his own notes. Then he sends you to Pozzik, so the goblin does not think one of his sponsors has abandoned him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Baron Revilgaz want fuel regulator blueprints?",a="The Venture Company’s shredders at Lake Nazferiti carry a new model of fuel regulator. Revilgaz believes Pozzik could use the details.",al={"why steal blueprints","why fuel regulator","revilgaz motive"}},{q="Where are the blueprints kept?",a="The blueprints are in a box inside a small house at the foot of the oil tower, at the Venture Company’s base by Lake Nazferiti in northern Stranglethorn.",al={"where are blueprints","fuel regulator blueprints location","cozzle house"}},{q="Who holds the key?",a="Foreman Cozzle carries the key and works in the cabin atop the oil tower.",al={"cozzle key","where is key","how to open chest"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the chain?",a="Wharfmaster Lozgil sent you to Baron Revilgaz in the previous step, Goblin Sponsorship number three. Goblin Sponsorship number five comes next.",al={"what comes before this","what quest is next","goblin sponsorship chain"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a Rogue, you can pick the lock on the blueprints box without Cozzle’s key."},kw={"baron revilgaz","blueprints","foreman cozzle","fuel regulator","goblin sponsorship","lake nazferiti","mirage raceway","pozzik","venture company"},rel={"npc:baron-revilgaz","npc:pozzik","subzone:lake-nazferiti","topic:venture-company","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:stranglethorn","zone:thousandneedles","quest:1181","quest:1183"},m={start="Baron Revilgaz",["end"]="Baron Revilgaz",level="37",faction="Neutral",id=1182},src={"Goblin Sponsorship (4)"}}
E["quest:1183"] = {t="quest",n="Goblin Sponsorship",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Shimmering Flats, Baron Revilgaz's regards reach Pozzik with the Fuel Regulator Blueprints. The Baron invites Pozzik to ask for anything he needs.",h="At the Shimmering Flats, Baron Revilgaz's regards reach Pozzik with the Fuel Regulator Blueprints.",sec={{t="Regards for Pozzik",b="Baron Revilgaz sends you to the Shimmering Flats with the Fuel Regulator Blueprints and his regards for Pozzik. The Baron says Pozzik should ask if he ever needs anything. Revilgaz waits to hear that Pozzik breaks the track record.",sp=0},{t="Improving the Design",b="Pozzik had hoped the regulator would already be assembled. Instead, he sees a chance to improve its design from the ground up. He plans to sketch new schematics, build the part and have it installed soon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you with the blueprints?",a="Baron Revilgaz sends you from Booty Bay with his regards for Pozzik.",al={"who gives goblin sponsorship 5","quest giver","revilgaz quest"}},{q="Who receives the fuel regulator blueprints?",a="Pozzik receives the Fuel Regulator Blueprints on the Shimmering Flats.",al={"where do i take the blueprints","who gets the schematics","pozzik location"}},{q="What does Baron Revilgaz hope to hear?",a="Baron Revilgaz waits for news that Pozzik breaks the track record.",al={"revilgaz motivation","baron revilgaz sponsor"}},{q="What comes before this delivery?",a="Before this delivery, you fetched the blueprints for Revilgaz. The next step is The Eighteenth Pilot.",al={"previous quest","what led to this","goblin sponsorship chain"}}},kw={"baron revilgaz","fuel regulator blueprints","goblin sponsorship","mirage raceway","pozzik","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:pozzik","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:shimmering-flats","quest:1182","quest:1186","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin"},m={start="Baron Revilgaz",["end"]="Pozzik",level="37",faction="Neutral",id=1183},src={"Goblin Sponsorship (5)"}}
E["quest:1184"] = {t="quest",n="Parts of the Swarm",z="thousandneedles",s="From Thousand Needles, Korran sends word to Orgrimmar about Moktar and his studies.",h="From Thousand Needles, Korran sends word to Orgrimmar about Moktar and his studies.",sec={{t="Word for Orgrimmar",b="Korran sends you to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar with word from Thousand Needles. The cracked carapaces came from silithid at the Rustmaul Digsite. Tell Belgrom that Moktar is doing his bidding well and that Korran's studies are progressing. Korran hopes to learn more soon.",sp=0},{t="Belgrom's Reply",b="Belgrom Rockmaul thanks you and says the warchief will be glad to hear of your tenacity. He promises to mention your name. Thrall speaks with Belgrom often and values his opinions. Belgrom considers the silithid a serious threat and wants to hear if Korran learns more about them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Orgrimmar?",a="Korran, who studies the silithid, asks you to carry word to Belgrom Rockmaul in Orgrimmar.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","who gave parts of the swarm"}},{q="Who are you supposed to deliver the message to?",a="Belgrom Rockmaul, in Orgrimmar.",al={"who do i see","where does this go","belgrom rockmaul location"}},{q="What message does Korran want delivered?",a="Tell Belgrom that Moktar is doing his bidding well in Thousand Needles and that Korran's studies are progressing. Korran hopes to learn more soon.",al={"what is the message","korran report"}},{q="What are the creatures Korran is studying?",a="They are silithid. The cracked carapaces that began this work came from silithid at the Rustmaul Digsite in Thousand Needles.",al={"what are the creatures","why study the swarm"}}},kw={"belgrom rockmaul","korran","moktar","orgrimmar","parts of the swarm","rustmaul digsite","silithid","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:korran","zone:thousandneedles","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Korran",["end"]="Belgrom Rockmaul",level="35",faction="Horde",id=1184},src={"Parts of the Swarm (2)"}}
E["quest:1186"] = {t="quest",n="The Eighteenth Pilot",z="thousandneedles",s="On the Shimmering Flats, Pozzik sends you to find Razzeric while he works on the racers. Razzeric is the team's eighteenth pilot, and he enjoys modifying the racers.",h="On the Shimmering Flats, Pozzik sends you to find Razzeric while he works on the racers.",sec={{t="Meet the Pilot",b="Pozzik is fitting a new fuel regulator into the racer designs. He sends you to Razzeric on the Shimmering Flats, the team's eighteenth pilot. Razzeric likes to modify the racers. Pozzik says he is a little off his rocker, so try not to look too surprised.",sp=0},{t="A Pilot Remembers",b="Razzeric knows you have been helping Pozzik. He remembers running around the pit area and pitching in on any job the mechanics let him near. Now he is the goblin racing team's pilot extraordinaire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Razzeric?",a="Razzeric is a goblin who pilots the goblin racing team on the Shimmering Flats. Pozzik calls him the team's eighteenth pilot.",al={"who is the eighteenth pilot","razzeric lore","goblin pilot"}},{q="Why does Pozzik send you to Razzeric?",a="Pozzik is fitting a new fuel regulator into the racer designs, so he sends you to speak with Razzeric and help the team further.",al={"why talk to razzeric","pozzik eighteenth pilot"}},{q="What is Razzeric like?",a="Pozzik says Razzeric likes to make small changes to the racers and is a little off his rocker.",al={"razzeric personality","is razzeric crazy"}},{q="What came before this?",a="Before this, you delivered the Fuel Regulator Blueprints to Pozzik in Goblin Sponsorship.",al={"eighteenth pilot prerequisite","quest chain before razzeric"}}},kw={"goblin","pilot","pozzik","raceway","razzeric","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:pozzik","quest:1183","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin"},m={start="Pozzik",["end"]="Razzeric",level="37",faction="Neutral",id=1186},src={"The Eighteenth Pilot"}}
E["quest:1187"] = {t="quest",n="Razzeric's Tweaking",z="thousandneedles",s="On the Shimmering Flats, Razzeric's Tweaking gives racers more power once Pozzik is done with them. A seaforium booster ordered from Shreev in Gadgetzan traveled by zeppelin, which Razzeric says crashed in Dustwallow Marsh. He wants the booster brought back.",h="On the Shimmering Flats, Razzeric's Tweaking gives racers more power once Pozzik is done with them.",sec={{t="More Juice",b="Pozzik is a fine mechanic, Razzeric says, but too cautious with firepower and too ready to hold back. Once Pozzik finishes with a racer, Razzeric loosens its controls, removes parts of its frame, and adds power. He ordered a seaforium booster from Shreev at the Gizmorium in Gadgetzan. Razzeric says the zeppelin carrying it crashed in Dustwallow Marsh. The booster belongs back on the Shimmering Flats. Facing the track without that extra kick would be a travesty.",sp=0},{t="Strapped to the Racer",b="Razzeric praises the booster, which holds a full fifteen pounds of seaforium. Strapped to a racer's side, it should carry him through the circuit fast enough to beat the gnomes twice over.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Razzeric?",a="Razzeric races on the Shimmering Flats and changes racers himself after Pozzik finishes with them.",al={"razzeric","who gives razzerics tweaking","razzeric shimmering flats"}},{q="Where did the booster come from?",a="Razzeric ordered the booster from Shreev at the Gizmorium in Gadgetzan.",al={"where did booster come from","who made seaforium booster","gadgetzan gizmorium"}},{q="Where is the seaforium booster now?",a="Razzeric says the zeppelin carrying the booster crashed in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"where is seaforium booster","booster location","downed zeppelin location"}},{q="Why does Razzeric want the booster?",a="Razzeric wants more power than Pozzik is willing to load, and thinks facing the track without that extra kick would be a travesty.",al={"why does he want seaforium","why seaforium booster"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="The Eighteenth Pilot came first.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","what leads to razzerics tweaking"}}},kw={"dustwallow marsh","gadgetzan","gizmorium","pozzik","razzeric","seaforium booster","shimmering flats","shreev","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:pozzik","quest:1186","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:gadgetzan","zone:dustwallow","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Razzeric",["end"]="Razzeric",level="41",id=1187},src={"Classic quest text: Razzeric's Tweaking"}}
E["quest:1188"] = {t="quest",n="Safety First",z="thousandneedles",s="Razzeric sends you south with a seaforium booster, bound for Shreev in Gadgetzan. Its safety is still on, though Razzeric asked for it to be removed.",h="Razzeric sends you south with a seaforium booster, bound for Shreev in Gadgetzan.",sec={{t="A Safety Nobody Wanted",b="Razzeric finds the safety still on his seaforium booster. It limits the power the booster can deliver, though he had asked Shreev to remove it. So he gives you the booster and sends you south of the Shimmering Flats, into the Tanaris desert. Shreev can remove the safety at the Gadgetzan Gizmorium.",sp=0},{t="Shreev's Answer",b="At the Gizmorium, Shreev denies putting a safety lock on the booster. He says it is almost entirely seaforium explosive, already altered to deliver more of its payload when used. Razzeric, Shreev says, is never content unless he goes all the way to eleven.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Gadgetzan?",a="Razzeric, the goblin pilot, sends you to Gadgetzan with his seaforium booster.",al={"quest giver","who starts safety first","razzeric quest"}},{q="Why is Razzeric unhappy with the booster?",a="The safety Shreev left on the booster limits its power, though Razzeric asked for it to be removed.",al={"why does razzeric complain","booster problem","what is wrong with the booster"}},{q="Where can Shreev be found?",a="Shreev is at the Gizmorium in Gadgetzan, in the Tanaris desert south of the Shimmering Flats.",al={"shreev location","where is shreev","gadgetzan gizmorium location"}},{q="What item are you carrying to Gadgetzan?",a="You carry Razzeric's seaforium booster, which he gives you to bring to Shreev.",al={"what item","booster item","what do you bring to shreev"}},{q="What comes after this delivery?",a="A second part of the chain follows, also called Safety First.",al={"next quest","what follows safety first","safety first continuation"}}},kw={"gadgetzan gizmorium","razzeric","safety first","seaforium booster","shimmering flats","shreev","tanaris"},rel={"subzone:gadgetzan","zone:tanaris","subzone:shimmering-flats","topic:goblin","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Razzeric",["end"]="Shreev",level="41",id=1188},src={"Safety First (Thousand Needles)"}}
E["quest:1189"] = {t="quest",n="Safety First",z="thousandneedles",s="On the Shimmering Flats, you carry Shreev’s modified seaforium booster back to Razzeric. Shreev warns that one slip while setting it off could leave Razzeric a scorch mark on the track.",h="On the Shimmering Flats, you carry Shreev’s modified seaforium booster back to Razzeric.",sec={{t="A Warning from Shreev",b="Shreev hands you the modified booster, prepared as Razzeric asked. He warns that Razzeric must take care when setting it off. One slip, and Razzeric will be a scorch mark on the track instead of racing ahead. Shreev says that would be a shame. Then he wonders whether the nineteenth driver would have been any good.",sp=0},{t="Sand Under the Seat",b="Back on the Shimmering Flats, Razzeric grumbles that Pozzik loaded a bucket of sand onto his racer. How can he reach top speed with sand beneath the seat?",sp=0},{t="The Booster Returned",b="Razzeric is pleased with the modified booster. He wishes he could see the gnomes’ faces when he sets it off. Yet he expects to be too busy setting a new course record.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends the modified booster back to the flats?",a="In Gadgetzan, Shreev finishes modifying the seaforium booster as Razzeric wanted. Then he gives it to you to carry back to Razzeric on the Shimmering Flats.",al={"who gives safety first 2","shreev quest giver","who modifies the booster"}},{q="What does Shreev warn about?",a="Shreev warns Razzeric to take care when setting off the booster. One slip, and Razzeric will be a scorch mark on the track instead of racing ahead.",al={"is the booster dangerous","shreev warning","booster risk"}},{q="Why is Razzeric upset about his vehicle?",a="Pozzik loaded a bucket of sand onto Razzeric’s racer. Razzeric wonders how he can reach top speed with sand beneath the seat.",al={"why is razzeric mad","pozzik bucket of sand","razzeric complaint"}}},kw={"gadgetzan","pozzik","razzeric","safety first","seaforium booster","shimmering flats","shreev","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:1188","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:gadgetzan","zone:thousandneedles","npc:pozzik","topic:gnome"},m={start="Shreev",["end"]="Razzeric",level="41",id=1189},src={"Safety First (2)"}}
E["quest:1190"] = {t="quest",n="Keeping Pace",z="thousandneedles",s="Pozzik suspects the Brassbolts brothers have found a new material for their cars. Their designs and run data are unchanged, yet the cars go faster. Rizzle Brassbolts keeps close to his plans, and Zamek can distract him so you can take them. This follows News for Fizzle.",h="Pozzik suspects the Brassbolts brothers have found a new material for their cars.",sec={{t="Faster Than the Numbers Say",b="The Brassbolts brothers' cars have grown faster, and Pozzik can find only one explanation: a new building material. Their designs and the data from their runs remain unchanged. Rizzle Brassbolts has been absorbed in plans for this discovery almost constantly.",sp=0},{t="A Diversion from Zamek",b="Zamek can distract Rizzle while you take his plans. Pozzik is waiting for them on the Shimmering Flats.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Scroll",b="Rizzle's plans are a scroll of hurried notes and designs. They concern the refining of some raw material.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Pozzik want Rizzle's plans?",a="The Brassbolts brothers' cars run faster, though their designs and run data remain unchanged. Pozzik suspects they found a new building material and wants the plans Rizzle has been absorbed in.",al={"pozzik motivation","why steal brassbolts plans","keeping pace reason"}},{q="Who helps distract Rizzle Brassbolts?",a="Zamek can distract Rizzle Brassbolts, giving you a chance to take his plans.",al={"who creates the diversion","zamek role","how to distract rizzle"}},{q="Who are the plans stolen for?",a="Pozzik wants the plans. He is on the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles.",al={"where is keeping pace","keeping pace location"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="Keeping Pace comes right after News for Fizzle.",al={"keeping pace prerequisite","what quest precedes keeping pace"}},{q="What follows after securing the plans?",a="The chain continues with Rizzle's Schematics.",al={"what quest is next","after keeping pace"}}},kw={"brassbolts","diversion","pozzik","race car","rizzle brassbolts","schematics","shimmering flats","thousand needles","zamek"},rel={"npc:pozzik","quest:1194","quest:1137","quest:1192","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Pozzik",["end"]="Rizzle's Unguarded Plans",level="41",id=1190},src={"Keeping Pace"}}
E["quest:1191"] = {t="quest",n="Zamek's Distraction",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, Zamek's Distraction can draw Rizzle away while you work through Keeping Pace. You cannot finish Keeping Pace without it.",h="In Thousand Needles, Zamek's Distraction can draw Rizzle away while you work through Keeping Pace.",sec={{t="A Timely Diversion",b="While you work through Keeping Pace, Zamek draws Rizzle from his hut. The Indurium plans remain behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives Zamek's Distraction?",a="Zamek gives it in Thousand Needles.",al={"who starts zameks distraction","zamek quest giver","where do i get zameks distraction"}},{q="How does this relate to Keeping Pace?",a="It comes while you are in the middle of Keeping Pace, and you cannot finish that step without it.",al={"is this needed for keeping pace","keeping pace zamek","connection to keeping pace"}},{q="What does the diversion do?",a="Rizzle leaves his hut, and his plans are left behind.",al={"what happens when zamek distracts","rizzle leaves hut"}},{q="Can both Alliance and Horde adventurers work with Zamek?",a="Yes. Zamek is neutral and works with either faction.",al={"is zamek neutral","alliance or horde zamek","who can do zameks distraction"}}},kw={"distraction","keeping pace","thousand needles","zamek"},rel={"quest:1190","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Zamek",["end"]="Zamek",level="41",faction="Neutral",id=1191},src={"Zamek's Distraction"}}
E["quest:1192"] = {t="quest",n="Indurium Ore",z="thousandneedles",s="Pozzik needs Indurium Ore to build several parts for the racers. The ore lies at the Uldaman dig in the Badlands, across the sea in Khaz Modan. Gnomes are already gathering their own supply, and Pozzik wants to keep pace.",h="Pozzik needs Indurium Ore to build several parts for the racers.",sec={{t="Ore from Uldaman",b="Pozzik asks you to bring him four pieces of raw Indurium Ore. You can find it at the Uldaman dig in the Badlands, across the sea in Khaz Modan. Gnomes are already gathering their own supply, and Pozzik wants some too. This comes after Rizzle's Schematics.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Pozzik want indurium ore?",a="Pozzik needs a great deal of raw Indurium Ore for several parts of the racers.",al={"what is the indurium for","why indurium ore","pozzik indurium purpose"}},{q="Where is the indurium ore found?",a="Indurium Ore comes from the Uldaman dig site in the Badlands, over the sea in Khaz Modan.",al={"where to find indurium ore","indurium location","where do i get indurium ore"}},{q="Why does it matter to get the ore?",a="Gnomes are already gathering their own Indurium Ore, and Pozzik wants to keep pace.",al={"why hurry indurium","gnome rival indurium"}},{q="What came before this?",a="Rizzle's Schematics comes before this, and Keeping Pace comes before Rizzle's Schematics.",al={"prerequisite for indurium ore","indurium chain previous quest"}}},kw={"badlands","indurium","indurium ore","pozzik","racers","thousand needles","uldaman"},rel={"npc:pozzik","quest:1194","quest:1190","subzone:uldaman","zone:badlands","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome"},m={start="Pozzik",["end"]="Pozzik",level="42",id=1192},src={"Indurium Ore (quest)"}}
E["quest:1194"] = {t="quest",n="Rizzle's Schematics",z="thousandneedles",s="After Keeping Pace, you carry a raw indurium sample to Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats. Rizzle's plans lie beneath the ore, and his notes trace it to the dwarves' dig at Uldaman in the Badlands. They also describe how well indurium resists heat.",h="After Keeping Pace, you carry a raw indurium sample to Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.",sec={{t="Notes on Indurium",b="Rizzle's plans explain how to refine indurium ore. Scrawled notes trace its source to the dwarves' dig at Uldaman in the Badlands. Other notes describe the ore's resistance to heat. A lump of raw indurium holds the plans down, and you take the sample to Pozzik.",sp=0},{t="Pozzik's Verdict",b="Pozzik finds indurium interesting. If it resists heat as well as you say, that may explain how much the gnomes have improved of late. The sample will be invaluable for tests, though Pozzik needs more before it can be of real use.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Rizzle get his indurium ore?",a="Rizzle's scrawls point to the dwarves' dig at Uldaman in the Badlands as the source of his indurium ore.",al={"where is indurium from","source of indurium ore","rizzle indurium location"}},{q="What do Rizzle's notes say about indurium?",a="Rizzle's notes describe how to refine indurium, and many others concern its resistance to heat.",al={"what does indurium do","why indurium","indurium properties"}},{q="Who receives the indurium sample?",a="You bring the sample to Pozzik on the Shimmering Flats.",al={"who do i turn this in to","who wants the indurium sample","pozzik turn in"}},{q="Where did this sample come from?",a="A lump of raw indurium ore held Rizzle's plans down as a paperweight.",al={"where was the sample found","rizzle paperweight"}}},kw={"badlands","indurium","pozzik","rizzle","schematics","shimmering flats","uldaman"},rel={"npc:pozzik","quest:1190","quest:1192","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:uldaman","zone:badlands","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Rizzle's Unguarded Plans",["end"]="Pozzik",level="41",id=1194},src={"Rizzle's Schematics"}}
E["quest:1394"] = {t="quest",n="Final Passage",z="thousandneedles",s="You have passed Parqual Fintallas's test and all that came before it. Now he sends you to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles, who will judge whether your mind, body and spirit have grown strong enough to earn honour.",h="You have passed Parqual Fintallas's test and all that came before it.",sec={{t="Back to the Weathered Nook",b="Dorn Plainstalker began the Test of Faith, and its trials now reach their final step. He waits in the Weathered Nook, in a cave reached by a ramp north of Freewind Post. Parqual Fintallas urges you to keep the balance you have shown through the trials.",sp=0},{t="Dorn's Welcome",b="Dorn Plainstalker says many moons have passed since your first leap set you on this path. You have been away from his home for a long while. He finds you stronger and more enlightened than before, and is pleased. Dorn says you deserve honour for seeing his tests through to the end.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this final step?",a="Parqual Fintallas tells you that you have passed his test and all that came before it.",al={"quest giver","who starts final passage","parqual fintallas"}},{q="Where do I go next?",a="Return to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles. He waits in the Weathered Nook, in a cave reached by a ramp north of Freewind Post.",al={"where is dorn","where to turn in","dorn plainstalker location","weathered nook location"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="Test of Lore comes before this as an earlier trial in the same chain.",al={"previous quest","prereq","what leads to final passage"}},{q="What was the very first step of this journey?",a="Dorn Plainstalker gave you Test of Faith in the Weathered Nook. This is the chain's final step.",al={"first quest","where did this start","test of faith chain"}},{q="Why does Parqual send you back to Dorn?",a="Parqual says Dorn will notice how you have changed and judge whether your mind, body and spirit are strong enough for honour.",al={"why dorn","parqual reason"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face this chain of trials, which ends with Dorn Plainstalker."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","final passage","freewind post","parqual fintallas","test of faith","test of lore","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","npc:parqual-fintallas","quest:1149","subzone:weathered-nook","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post"},m={start="Parqual Fintallas",["end"]="Dorn Plainstalker",level="36",faction="Horde",id=1394},src={"Final Passage"}}
E["quest:1950"] = {t="quest",n="Get the Scoop",z="thousandneedles",s="Near the Mirage Raceway, Magus Tirth has forgotten the words to open his sealed strongbox. His apprentice, Johnson, is missing somewhere around the track, and Tirth needs the spellbook inside.",h="Near the Mirage Raceway, Magus Tirth has forgotten the words to open his sealed strongbox.",sec={{t="A Magus and His Memory",b="Magus Tirth lives on the cracked salt bed of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. He is an eccentric spellcaster whose arcane knowledge and books draw mages seeking to advance. Patience helps when dealing with him. Tirth relies on an assistant for everyday details, even the spoken passwords guarding his arcane stores. Now a book of power is locked away, and the magic words have slipped from his mind entirely.",sp=0},{t="Fowl Play",b="Goblins and gnomes who run the Mirage Raceway can tell you what happened to Johnson, Magus Tirth's apprentice. Tirth turned Johnson into a common chicken, and the apprentice now wanders the salt flats unable to speak. When you draw near, the spell's haze lifts for a moment. Johnson can squawk out the missing password.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Magus Tirth?",a="Magus Tirth is a reclusive human wizard near the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles. Mages seek his advanced arcane lore to hone their craft.",al={"tirth lore","who is magus tirth","tirth shimmer flats"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tirth need the password to his own box?",a="Tirth locked his strongbox with a spoken phrase and relied on his assistant to remember such everyday details. When his apprentice vanished, Tirth forgot the words.",al={"why tirth forgot","tirth strongbox password"},it="motive"},{q="Where did the apprentice go?",a="Johnson wanders near the racetrack east of Tirth's camp. Finding him is harder because Tirth turned him into a chicken.",al={"find tirth assistant","where is apprentice johnson","johnson location"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="Why was the apprentice turned into a chicken?",a="Tirth cursed Johnson, then forgot he had done so. When he learned what had become of his assistant, he vaguely assumed Johnson deserved it for being an ungrateful pupil.",al={"why johnson chicken","tirth polymorph apprentice"},sp=1},{q="What is inside Tirth's strongbox?",a="Tirth's strongbox holds a book of rituals, instructions essential to a mage's continuing education, and magical implements.",al={"tirth strongbox contents","what book is in the chest"},it="item"},{q="Who can undertake this task?",a="Only mages seeking specialized instruction and materials to craft a potent wand can undertake this trial.",al={"can non mages do get the scoop","is this quest mage only"},gp=true},{q="Why does Magus Tirth send you instead of finding the apprentice himself?",a="Magus Tirth has no intention of scouring the Shimmering Flats himself when you are the one begging for his knowledge. You came seeking his rare magical tome, and since he cannot recall the verbal incantation to open his own magically sealed strongbox without his missing assistant, he makes helping him the price of his aid.",al={"why send me","why doesn't tirth find johnson","why do i have to find the apprentice"},it="why_me",add="25c94f6f"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, dealing with Tirth shows the perils of polymorph curses and the absent-mindedness that can afflict powerful scholars."},kw={"get the scoop","johnson","magus tirth","mirage raceway","shimmering flats","strongbox","thousand needles","wand quest"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:drag"},m={start="Magus Tirth",level="30",faction="Neutral",id=1950},src={"Get the Scoop"}}
E["quest:4542"] = {t="quest",n="Message to Freewind Post",z="thousandneedles",s="At Thousand Needles' western approaches, Brave Moonhorn sends an urgent warning to Freewind Post. Centaur raids are rising, and he reports strange behavior among the Grimtotem.",h="At Thousand Needles' western approaches, Brave Moonhorn sends an urgent warning to Freewind Post.",sec={{t="A Warning Down the Canyon",b="Brave Moonhorn watches Thousand Needles' western approaches. Centaur attacks have risen sharply, and the border sentries need to alert their leaders. So Moonhorn asks you to carry a dispatch southeast to Cliffwatcher Longhorn, commander of the mesa settlement at Freewind Post.",sp=0},{t="Rising Perils and Uneasy Kin",b="Cliffwatcher Longhorn confirms that centaur recently intercepted and slaughtered a supply caravan. Freewind Post must defend itself and answer the attack. Moonhorn also warns you to avoid the nearby Grimtotem tauren. Their strange, hostile behavior points to growing divisions across the arid flats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the message to Freewind Post?",a="Brave Moonhorn, a tauren scout, watches Thousand Needles' western entrance and gives you the urgent message to deliver.",al={"quest giver","who starts message to freewind post","brave moonhorn"},it="identity"},{q="Who receives the urgent message?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn receives the message at Freewind Post, the mesa settlement southeast of the Great Lift.",al={"where to turn in","cliffwatcher longhorn location","freewind post leader"},it="identity"},{q="What does the urgent message report?",a="The message warns that centaur attacks and harassment of caravans along the trails below have risen sharply.",al={"message contents","what is the message about"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is Brave Moonhorn worried about the Grimtotem?",a="Moonhorn says the nearby Grimtotem have acted strangely and kept their distance from other tauren. He advises you to avoid them.",al={"grimtotem warning","why avoid grimtotem"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after Longhorn reads the message?",a="After learning that centaur slaughtered a supply caravan, Cliffwatcher Longhorn orders a counterattack against them in the follow-up, Pacify the Centaur.",al={"next quest","after message to freewind post"},it="next_step"},{q="How do you reach Freewind Post from the canyon floor?",a="From the canyon floor, follow the main road east to the base of the needle mesa. Then take the wooden platform lift up to the village.",al={"getting to freewind post","how to get up freewind post"},gp=true},{q="Why does Brave Moonhorn want the message delivered to Freewind Post?",a="Centaur attacks in the canyon have surged, putting travelers, caravans, and outposts in immediate danger. Stationed at the Great Lift, Brave Moonhorn witnesses the escalating violence firsthand and knows that Cliffwatcher Longhorn and the garrison atop Freewind Post need advance warning to organize defenses and protect vital supply routes.",al={"why send message to freewind post","brave moonhorn motive","why warn longhorn"},it="motive",add="65381134"},{q="Why does Brave Moonhorn need an adventurer to carry the message?",a="Brave Moonhorn is stationed as a guard holding the vital border at the Great Lift between the Barrens and Thousand Needles. With centaur raids escalating and the neighboring Grimtotem clan acting suspiciously, Moonhorn cannot abandon his sentry post without leaving the lift defenseless, making a capable traveler the best choice to run the dispatch.",al={"why can't moonhorn deliver it","why me message to freewind post","why does moonhorn need help"},it="why_me",add="c67c7dfd"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the centaur as bitter ancestral rivals. Moonhorn's warning shows they still hunt Kalimdor's trails, while tensions with the reclusive Grimtotem simmer.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Freewind Post links the routes across Thousand Needles. Open communication between the outpost watchers and settlement leaders helps secure the desert trade routes."},kw={"brave moonhorn","centaur","cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","grimtotem","message to freewind post","thousand needles","urgent message"},rel={"npc:brave-moonhorn","npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:freewind-post","quest:4841","quest:5064","topic:centaur","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Brave Moonhorn",["end"]="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="25",faction="Horde",id=4542},src={"Message to Freewind Post"}}
E["quest:4767"] = {t="quest",n="Wind Rider",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Elu hopes to join the Horde’s wind riders. He asks you to gather wild wyvern eggs at Highperch, where the Horde needs more mounts.",h="At Freewind Post, Elu hopes to join the Horde’s wind riders.",sec={{t="The Call of the Sky",b="Across Kalimdor, wind riders carry Horde couriers, scouts, and warriors over long distances. At Freewind Post, young tauren Elu hopes to join their ranks. The Horde needs more mounts, so Elu has been asked to help find new wyverns for its master wind riders. He asks travelers for help.",sp=0},{t="Ascending Highperch",b="Highperch rises above the Thousand Needles mesas and is a prime nesting ground for wild wyverns. To gather viable eggs, you climb the cliffs and face adults guarding their roosts. Elu hopes the eggs will prove his dedication. Then he can begin raising and training wyverns for the Horde’s flight masters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Elu gives you this work from atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He hopes to become a wind rider.",al={"wind rider quest giver","who starts wind rider","elu location"},it="identity"},{q="What does Elu need?",a="Elu asks you to bring him ten Highperch Wyvern Eggs from nests in Highperch.",al={"wind rider objectives","what do i collect","wyvern eggs"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where is Highperch located?",a="Highperch lies northwest of Freewind Post and just south of Whitereach Post. A natural ramp marked by a totem pole leads from the canyon floor to the nesting grounds.",al={"how to get to highperch","highperch entrance","where are wyvern eggs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Horde gathering wild wyvern eggs?",a="The Horde’s master wind riders face growing demand for aerial mounts across their outposts, and captive breeding cannot keep pace. Raising wyverns from wild clutches gives handlers new mounts to train for transport and scouting.",al={"why harvest wyvern eggs","lore behind wyvern eggs"},it="motive"},{q="Are the wild wyverns hostile?",a="Yes. Wild wyverns fiercely defend their broods and readily attack anyone who approaches their clutches on Highperch.",al={"will wyverns attack","wyvern danger"},it="danger"},{q="What does Elu intend to do with the eggs?",a="Elu hopes the eggs will let him begin formal wind rider training and raise wyverns to bond with and serve the Horde in the skies.",al={"elu wyverns","what happens to the eggs"},it="item"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Wyverns carry the Horde across Kalimdor. Replenishing their stables matters for communication and defense on the frontier.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can take pride in the wind riders of Freewind Post, who honor the care and training of wyverns.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you know the care and peril involved in taking wild clutches from a territorial predator’s nest."},kw={"elu","freewind post","highperch","thousand needles","wind rider","wyvern eggs"},rel={"npc:elu","subzone:highperch","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde","quest:92472"},m={start="Elu",level="29",faction="Horde",id=4767,ri={"Highperch Wyvern Egg"}},src={"Wind Rider (quest)"}}
E["quest:4770"] = {t="quest",n="Homeward Bound",z="thousandneedles",s="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is stranded among the wyverns of Highperch. You are helping the young tauren naturalist reach the canyon floor and return toward Whitereach Post after he wandered into their nesting grounds.",h="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is stranded among the wyverns of Highperch.",sec={{t="A Naturalist in Over His Head",b="Pao'ka Swiftmountain came to Thousand Needles with the elder Motega Firemane. They meant to study the canyon floor's wildlife and towering stone pillars. Curious and too sure of himself, Pao'ka went alone into Highperch to watch its wyverns up close. The territorial beasts drove him off. Now the young scholar has spent days frightened and stranded among the crags.",sp=0},{t="The Path Down the Crags",b="Aggressive wyverns guard their clutches and high roosts throughout Highperch. You clear a way through the nesting predators so Pao'ka can reach level ground. The panicked youth cannot defend himself in the open, and relies on passing Horde travelers to fend off the wyverns. He needs to reach the safer canyon path leading east.",sp=0},{t="Relief and Reckoning",b="Pao'ka reaches the base of the cliffs and can make his way home to Whitereach Post. Motega Firemane is stunned by what happened. He had promised Pao'ka's hesitant father that he would watch over the boy during their field studies. Relieved that Pao'ka survived his reckless expedition, Motega rewards those who saved him. In private, he wishes he had chained the apprentice to a totem.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Pao'ka Swiftmountain?",a="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is a young tauren apprentice who came to Thousand Needles with Motega Firemane to study and record wild creatures. His youthful enthusiasm led him alone into Highperch.",al={"paoka","pao'ka","who is the escort npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Pao'ka hiding in Highperch?",a="Pao'ka went alone into the roosts to observe the native wyverns and their nests up close. The aggressive beasts attacked him, forcing him into hiding and trapping him on the high mesa.",al={"why is paoka in highperch","what happened to paoka","why is he stuck"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Motega Firemane?",a="Motega Firemane is a tauren naturalist stationed at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. Pao'ka's father entrusted him with the youth's safety during their field studies.",al={"motega","who is motega firemane","quest turn in npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Highperch located?",a="Highperch is a raised mesa and wyvern nesting ground in western Thousand Needles. It lies just west of Whitereach Post and northwest of Freewind Post.",al={"highperch location","where is highperch","where do i escort him from"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where is Whitereach Post?",a="Whitereach Post is a small Horde encampment east of Highperch in Thousand Needles. Tauren naturalists use it as a field base while studying the canyon's wildlife.",al={"whitereach location","where is whitereach post"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does Motega know Pao'ka was missing?",a="No. Pao'ka slipped away to Highperch without telling Motega. Motega did not know his apprentice was in danger until you report the rescue.",al={"did motega know","why didn't motega search for him"},sp=1},{q="Why does Pao'ka Swiftmountain want this done?",a="Pao'ka snuck into Highperch alone to observe the wyverns and wound up cornered after venturing too close to their nests. Trapped and lost for days amidst aggressive predators, he cannot fight his way down on his own. Worse, he knows Motega Firemane will be furious if his reckless expedition is discovered, making an escorted escape his only hope of surviving and returning to Whitereach Post.",al={"why help paoka","paoka motive","why does paoka need escort"},it="motive",add="17b8918e"},{q="Why does Pao'ka need you to escort him rather than the guards?",a="Pao'ka snuck away from Whitereach Post in secret, and no one back at camp even knows he went missing. Calling for guards would expose his disobedience to Motega Firemane, but more urgently, he has been trapped in the aerie for days without seeing an ally. You are simply the first friendly traveler to stumble upon his hiding spot.",al={"why me paoka","why doesn't paoka call guards","why help paoka alone"},it="why_me",add="edb8f2eb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the duties shared by tribes and elders. Motega's promise to Pao'ka's father reflects the bonds that guide their field studies.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you may know wyverns as allies and mounts across Kalimdor. The wild wyverns of Highperch draw interest for their nature and strategic value."},kw={"escort","highperch","homeward bound","motega firemane","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","whitereach post","wyvern"},rel={"npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain","npc:motega-firemane","subzone:highperch","subzone:whitereach-post","quest:4767","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren"},m={start="Pao'ka Swiftmountain",["end"]="Motega Firemane",level="29",faction="Horde",id=4770},src={"Homeward Bound"}}
E["quest:4821"] = {t="quest",n="Alien Egg",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof sends you after an egg guarded by serpents beneath the stone needles. He wants it brought back before anything inside can break free.",h="At Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof sends you after an egg guarded by serpents beneath the stone needles.",sec={{t="A Strange Nest",b="Hagar Lightninghoof hears of an unusual egg in the serpent dens below the stone needles. The canyon serpents guard it as though it were their own brood, striking at travelers who draw near. Concerned for the hunting grounds, Hagar asks you to find the nest, pass its sentries, and bring the strange egg back for study.",sp=0},{t="The Hatchling Awakens",b="When Hagar Lightninghoof examines the egg, its shell cracks at once. A Young Arikara, a juvenile winged monstrosity, bursts out. The newborn does not attack. It takes to the sky and flees from Freewind Post's wooden platforms, while deeper primordial forces stir in the canyon winds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can the Alien Egg be found?",a="The egg lies in serpent nests along the cliff bases of Thousand Needles, especially south and northeast of Freewind Post. It rests on the canyon floor among hostile native serpents.",al={"alien egg location","where is alien egg","egg spawn thousand needles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the local serpents guarding it?",a="No one knows what laid the egg, but the canyon serpents guard it as though it belonged to their own clutch. They attack curious intruders who approach the nest.",al={"why do serpents protect the egg","serpent behavior alien egg"},sp=1,it="hostile"},{q="Who is Hagar Lightninghoof?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof is a tauren scout and warden stationed high above Thousand Needles at Freewind Post. He watches for unusual movement and threats to the canyon's wildlife, and coordinates Horde efforts to manage local beasts.",al={"hagar lightninghoof lore","who is quest giver hagar"},it="identity"},{q="What happens when you deliver the egg?",a="When you hand over the egg, Hagar examines it up close, revealing what it holds.",al={"what hatches from alien egg","what is inside the egg"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What does this quest lead to?",a="Delivering the egg immediately begins Serpent Wild, the first step in a longer chain. Hagar seeks to understand what the egg held.",al={"next quest after alien egg","arikara chain next step"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is the egg literally from outer space?",a="Here, “alien” means foreign and unfamiliar to Thousand Needles' local wildlife, not a creature from the stars. Hagar wants to learn what kind of creature the egg holds.",al={"is alien egg extraterrestrial","is egg alien"},sp=1,it="origin"},{q="Why does Hagar Lightninghoof want the Alien Egg?",a="Hagar has heard troubling rumors of an unfamiliar, foreign egg discovered within the serpent dens of Thousand Needles. Because none of the scouts have been able to get close enough to examine it past the serpents fiercely protecting it, he wants it recovered so he can study it firsthand. He is deeply concerned about what kind of unknown creature might hatch from it beneath Freewind Post.",al={"why hagar wants egg","hagar lightninghoof motive","why alien egg quest"},it="motive",add="7e0b1b71"},{q="What is the Alien Egg?",a="The Alien Egg is an unusual clutch found deep in the serpent dens across Thousand Needles. While it does not look like standard serpent brood, local wind serpents fiercely guard it as if it were their own. Hagar Lightninghoof seeks it out to inspect its origins, though upon closer inspection, it quickly hatches into a young winged serpent that takes flight.",al={"what is alien egg","alien egg purpose","alien egg lore"},sp=1,it="item",add="a4db3611"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you live above the canyon floor at Freewind Post and depend on understanding the wildlife below. An invasive or unnatural serpent brood could disrupt the balance around your home.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter familiar with Kalimdor's beasts, you may recognize that the nests in the canyon hold something far more primordial than common desert serpents.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Freewind Post is your main outpost in Thousand Needles. Containing emerging apex predators helps defend the supply lines."},kw={"alien egg","arikara","freewind post","hagar lightninghoof","serpent den","serpent wild","serpents","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:hagar-lightninghoof","quest:4865","quest:5088","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Hagar Lightninghoof",level="26",faction="Horde",id=4821,ri={"Alien Egg"}},src={"Alien Egg (quest)"}}
E["quest:4841"] = {t="quest",n="Pacify The Centaur",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, you face the Galak camp below. Cliffwatcher Longhorn wants the threat at Splithoof Crag cut down before it reaches the tauren post.",h="At Freewind Post, you face the Galak camp below.",sec={{t="A Threat on the Canyon Floor",b="Freewind Post stands on a desert mesa above Thousand Needles. From there, the tauren watch the canyon floor, where enemies gather beneath the ropes and lifts. The Galak centaur have built a war camp at Splithoof Crag, directly north along the canyon wall. Their camp threatens the supply lines and tauren movement through the needles.",sp=0},{t="Retaliation and Bloodshed",b="Cliffwatcher Longhorn sends Horde travelers to weaken the Galak ranks. The tauren believe Freewind Post will be safe only when the centaur vanguard is broken in its own camp. Galak Scouts, Galak Wranglers, and Galak Windchasers all face the fight. Their deaths may blunt an attack before it reaches the post.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Pacify the Centaur?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn gives the order from atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. He helps defend the post and watches the dangers across the surrounding salt flats and canyons.",al={"quest giver","who starts pacify the centaur","cliffwatcher longhorn"},gp=true},{q="Where are the Galak centaur located?",a="The Galak centaur camp lies directly north of Freewind Post, against the northern cliff wall of Thousand Needles. It is called Splithoof Crag.",al={"galak camp location","where is splithoof crag","centaur location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the tauren want the centaur killed?",a="The Galak have camped at the foot of Freewind Post, and Cliffwatcher Longhorn wants them killed to protect the Horde's desert stronghold. The centaur have also long waged a brutal war against nomadic tauren across central Kalimdor.",al={"why kill centaur","tauren centaur conflict","why revenge"},it="motive"},{q="What kinds of centaur need to be slain?",a="You hunt twelve Galak Scouts, ten Galak Wranglers, and six Galak Windchasers at Splithoof Crag.",al={"galak targets","which centaur to kill","quest objectives"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What comes after completing Pacify the Centaur?",a="Once the Galak ranks are thinned, Cliffwatcher Longhorn turns to other dangers nearby and sends you after Grimtotem Spying.",al={"next quest","what follows pacify the centaur","quest chain after centaur"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What pre-requisite leads into this mission?",a="Message to Freewind Post leads you here. It asks travelers to report directly to Cliffwatcher Longhorn.",al={"prereq","previous quest","how to unlock pacify the centaur"},gp=true},{q="Who are the Galak centaur camping north of Freewind Post?",a="The Galak tribe represents the local centaur threat in Thousand Needles, entrenched directly beneath the mesa cliffs at Splithoof Crag. Known for their fierce scouts, beast-tamers, and windchasers, they maintain an aggressive presence that constantly harasses travelers and tauren outposts throughout the canyon floor.",al={"who are galak centaur","galak centaur","centaur north of freewind post"},it="target",add="9375eea4"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As shu'halo, you know centaur camps near a settlement recall generations of slaughter. Thinning the Galak is a matter of survival for your people.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Freewind Post keeps the road open between the Great Lift and the Shimmering Flats. Aggressive centaur beneath its towers endanger every caravan crossing the zone."},kw={"cliffwatcher longhorn","freewind post","galak scout","galak windchaser","galak wrangler","pacify the centaur","splithoof crag","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:splithoof-crag","zone:thousandneedles","quest:4542","quest:5064","topic:centaur"},m={start="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="25",faction="Horde",id=4841},src={"Pacify the Centaur"}}
E["quest:4865"] = {t="quest",n="Serpent Wild",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof sends you northwest after signs of Arikara emerge in Thousand Needles. Strange eggs point to a vengeance spirit from tauren legend, and Hagar seeks Motega Firemane's counsel at Whitereach Post.",h="At Freewind Post, Hagar Lightninghoof sends you northwest after signs of Arikara emerge in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Legend Made Flesh",b="Strange eggs have appeared across Thousand Needles, and local tauren fear an ecological disaster. Their signs point beyond ordinary predators to Arikara, a vengeance spirit from old tauren tales. The evidence shakes Hagar Lightninghoof. A threat he knew only from fireside lore now faces the canyon.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Whitereach",b="Hagar Lightninghoof seeks Motega Firemane's counsel because this danger reaches beyond physical defense. Motega watches over the canyon floor from Whitereach Post, northwest of Freewind Post. As a spiritual guide versed in the Needles' traditional omens, he may help the Horde understand the rising spirit and decide whether to appease or destroy it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Serpent Wild?",a="Hagar Lightninghoof at Freewind Post starts it, right after you deliver the strange egg found in the canyon.",al={"who gives serpent wild","serpent wild questgiver","hagar lightninghoof quest"},gp=true},{q="Where is Motega Firemane located?",a="Motega Firemane is at Whitereach Post, a small tauren camp along the road northwest of Freewind Post, past the fork toward the Great Lift.",al={"where is motega firemane","motega firemane location","find motega"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who or what is Arikara?",a="Arikara is a legendary wind serpent spirit of vengeance in tauren mythology. Its rumored presence in Thousand Needles threatens the local tribes both spiritually and physically.",al={"what is arikara","arikara lore","legend of arikara"},it="threat"},{q="What prerequisite must be finished before taking this quest?",a="You must finish Alien Egg first. You recover an unusual egg from the canyon's wild beasts and deliver it to Hagar Lightninghoof for inspection.",al={"prereq for serpent wild","alien egg quest chain","serpent wild unlock"},gp=true},{q="What happens after reaching Motega Firemane?",a="Speaking with Motega opens Sacred Fire, which begins the ritual preparations to confront Arikara.",al={"what comes after serpent wild","serpent wild follow up","sacred fire quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Hagar Lightninghoof so alarmed?",a="Hagar believed the tales of Arikara were only stories. Evidence that the vengeance spirit has appeared in the canyon frightens him, so he seeks elder wisdom at once.",al={"why is hagar scared","hagar wiping brow","hagar reaction"},it="motive"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you face an urgent crisis as Arikara's awakening tests your people's spiritual stewardship of Thousand Needles.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see how Arikara's vengeful spirit unsettles the balance of elemental and spiritual forces on the canyon mesas.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep the Thousand Needles supply route open against mystical threats to the road between the Great Lift and Feralas."},kw={"arikara","freewind post","hagar lightninghoof","motega firemane","sacred fire","serpent wild","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"npc:hagar-lightninghoof","npc:motega-firemane","subzone:whitereach-post","subzone:freewind-post","quest:5062","quest:5088","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:great-lift"},m={start="Hagar Lightninghoof",["end"]="Motega Firemane",level="26",faction="Horde",id=4865},src={"Serpent Wild"}}
E["quest:4881"] = {t="quest",n="Assassination Plot",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, centaur move against Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post. Intercepted orders reveal their plan to attack the tauren hunter.",h="In Thousand Needles, centaur move against Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post.",sec={{t="A Hunter in Hostile Lands",b="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren hunter camped at Whitereach Post in contested Thousand Needles. The small post lies southwest of the Great Lift, amid warring centaur clans and dangerous wildlife. The local centaur see his camp as a bold intrusion into their territory. They mean to kill Greycloud and discourage further Horde expansion through the canyon.",sp=0},{t="The Intercepted Orders",b="Intercepted centaur orders name Kanati Greycloud as their target. The decree condemns his boldness and orders a strike force to converge on Whitereach Post, destroy the camp, and kill anyone who might follow him. With the orders in hand, you can warn Kanati in time to prepare for the raiders' attack.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the assassination plot?",a="Local centaur are planning a coordinated ambush against Kanati Greycloud, the tauren hunter camped at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. They want him dead to keep the Horde from gaining a foothold in the canyon.",al={"assassination plot overview","what is this quest about","centaur plot"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Kanati Greycloud?",a="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren hunter camped at Whitereach Post, southwest of the Great Lift in Thousand Needles. His camp lies near centaur territory, making him a target.",al={"who is kanati","kanati greycloud","whitereach post npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the centaur want to kill Kanati?",a="The centaur see Kanati's camp at Whitereach Post as an intolerable intrusion into Thousand Needles. They plan to kill him, destroy the camp, and deter future Horde scouts from settling in the region.",al={"why kill kanati","centaur motive","why do centaur attack"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Whitereach Post?",a="Whitereach Post is a small tauren camp on the canyon floor in Thousand Needles, southwest of the Great Lift.",al={"whitereach post location","where is kanati's camp","where is whitereach"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can Alliance players complete this quest?",a="Alliance travelers can recover the Assassination Note, but they cannot deliver the warning to Kanati Greycloud. He is a Horde tauren, so only the Horde can bring it to him.",al={"can alliance do this","alliance assassination note","alliance turn in"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What happens after Kanati is warned?",a="When Kanati receives the warning, he refuses to flee and prepares to fight off the attackers. The defense of Whitereach Post begins when the centaur war band arrives.",al={"what happens next","next quest","protect kanati"},sp=1,it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know centaur hatred runs deep in tauren memory. Defending Kanati Greycloud at Whitereach Post continues the struggle to protect Kalimdor's plains and canyons from centaur aggression.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can see Whitereach Post as a small outpost southwest of the Great Lift. Kanati's survival matters to the Horde's watch over Thousand Needles."},kw={"assassination note","assassination plot","centaur","great lift","horde","kanati greycloud","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"npc:kanati-greycloud","quest:4966","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:great-lift","topic:centaur","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},m={start="Assassination Note",["end"]="Kanati Greycloud",level="28",faction="Horde",id=4881},src={"Assassination Plot"}}
E["quest:4904"] = {t="quest",n="Free At Last",z="thousandneedles",s="Lakota Windsong is making her way back to Thalia Amberhide at Freewind Post. After refusing Arnak Grimtotem, she was taken to his stronghold above Thousand Needles and now needs protection on the journey home.",h="Lakota Windsong is making her way back to Thalia Amberhide at Freewind Post.",sec={{t="A Brutal Abduction",b="Arnak Grimtotem wanted Lakota Windsong for his bride. When she refused, he returned by night and attacked her home. Lakota's brother tried to defend her, but Arnak struck him down. Then he dragged Lakota to Darkcloud Pinnacle.",sp=0},{t="Escape from Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Darkcloud Pinnacle rises above Thousand Needles, with high wooden bridges linking its spires. Grimtotem warriors guard the heights. As Lakota makes her way down, you fight off bandits who mean to seize her before she reaches the canyon floor.",sp=0},{t="A Bitter Homecoming",b="Lakota reaches the canyon floor and makes her way to safety at Freewind Post. There, Thalia Amberhide welcomes her with relief, though she grieves for Lakota's brother. Thalia gives his remaining belongings to those who brought Lakota home alive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Lakota Windsong captured?",a="Arnak Grimtotem wanted Lakota Windsong for his bride. After she refused him, he attacked her home at night. He struck down her brother when he tried to defend her, then dragged Lakota to Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"why is lakota captured","who kidnapped lakota","why did arnak take lakota"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is Darkcloud Pinnacle located?",a="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a cluster of towering rock spires linked by bridges in northern Thousand Needles. It lies just southeast of the Great Lift and south of Razorfen Downs.",al={"darkcloud pinnacle location","how to get to darkcloud pinnacle","where is lakota"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Arnak Grimtotem is a ruthless member of the Grimtotem tribe stationed on Darkcloud Pinnacle. He kidnapped Lakota and killed her brother. Horde authorities at Freewind Post have marked him for death.",al={"arnak lore","who is arnak","wanted arnak"},it="identity"},{q="Who should you speak to after the rescue?",a="After Lakota reaches the canyon floor, return to Freewind Post atop the high bluffs and speak with Thalia Amberhide.",al={"where to turn in free at last","who is thalia amberhide","turn in free at last"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do the Grimtotem attack during the escape?",a="Arnak's Grimtotem bandits patrol the heights of Darkcloud Pinnacle. They ambush anyone trying to help Lakota, his intended captive, reach freedom.",al={"why do bandits spawn","grimtotem bandits escort"},it="hostile"},{q="What happens to Lakota's brother?",a="Lakota's brother was killed defending her from Arnak Grimtotem during the kidnapping. Thalia later gives his heirlooms to those who rescue Lakota.",al={"lakotas brother","who died saving lakota","what happened to lakota brother"},it="history"},{q="Why does Lakota Windsong need your help to escape?",a="Lakota was violently abducted by Arnak Grimtotem after she rejected his marriage proposal, and her brother was slain attempting to defend her. Trapped high on Darkcloud Pinnacle surrounded by hostile Grimtotem warriors, she cannot fight her way down alone. Desperate to flee Arnak's forced courtship and return to Thalia Amberhide at Freewind Post, she needs your armed escort to carve a path through the bandits guarding the mesas.",al={"why help lakota windsong","lakota motive","why does lakota need escort"},it="motive",add="aa9c9984"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The Grimtotem clan shows its disregard for peace and unity among the tauren through kidnapping and murder, even under the gaze of Freewind Post.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde holds Freewind Post as an essential fortress in southern Kalimdor. Grimtotem lawlessness and kidnappings at Darkcloud Pinnacle threaten the road."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","darkcloud pinnacle","escort","free at last","freewind post","lakota windsong","thalia amberhide","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:lakota-windsong","npc:thalia-amberhide","quest:5147","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","quest:5064","topic:tauren","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Lakota Windsong",["end"]="Thalia Amberhide",level="29",faction="Horde",id=4904},src={"Free at Last (Thousand Needles)"}}
E["quest:4966"] = {t="quest",n="Protect Kanati Greycloud",z="thousandneedles",s="At Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles, you join Kanati Greycloud as Galak assassins close in. Their orders name the tauren for death.",h="At Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles, you join Kanati Greycloud as Galak assassins close in.",sec={{t="An Ambush Revealed",b="At Whitereach Post, Kanati Greycloud finds centaur orders naming him as a target. The Galak centaur have long fought the nomadic tauren and their Horde allies. Raiding supply paths is not enough for them. They also seek to kill those who settle in their canyons.",sp=0},{t="Defending Whitereach Post",b="Kanati suspects the Galak will strike soon, and their numbers may be greater than he first thought. So he asks travelers at the post to stand with him. When the assassins attack, Kanati holds his ground beside his allies. Their blades and spells can break the ambush before the centaur kill him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kanati Greycloud?",a="Kanati Greycloud is a tauren with a hunting camp at Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles. The camp lies near canyons claimed by local centaur clans.",al={"who is kanati","kanati greycloud lore","who is the quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the centaur trying to assassinate him?",a="The Galak centaur see the tauren and their Horde encampments as enemies encroaching on their canyon territory. They aim to kill Kanati and drive out his hunting camp and anyone who might follow him.",al={"why do centaur attack kanati","centaur assassination reason","assassination plot why"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this defense take place?",a="The ambush takes place at Whitereach Post, a small Horde outpost along the canyon paths of Thousand Needles.",al={"where is this quest","protect kanati location","where does the ambush happen"},it="place"},{q="Which centaur clan attacks Kanati Greycloud?",a="The assassins belong to the Galak tribe, a centaur clan that inhabits the canyons and ravines of Thousand Needles.",al={"what tribe attacks","who are the assassins","which centaur"},it="hostile"},{q="What happens after the assassins are defeated?",a="After the Galak assassins are slain, Kanati lives and Whitereach Post remains secure. He thanks those who stood with him during the surprise assault.",al={"what happens next","quest follow up","after protecting kanati"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Does Kanati Greycloud fight in the battle?",a="Yes. Kanati fights beside those who answer his plea, helping repel the assassins who came to kill him.",al={"does kanati help","kanati fighting","is kanati passive"}},{q="Who are the centaur attacking Kanati Greycloud?",a="The attackers are assassins from the Galak centaur tribe, sent to strike deep into Whitereach Post. Angered that Kanati Greycloud dared to set up a hunting camp in their canyons, they dispatched a dedicated hit squad to kill the tauren hunter at his own camp and drive off anyone who might follow him.",al={"who are the assassins","protect kanati assassins","which centaur attack"},it="target",add="792f0095"},{q="Why does Kanati Greycloud need your help defending the post?",a="While Kanati is a capable tauren warrior who fights alongside you, he realizes the centaur have dispatched more assassins than he can handle alone. Whitereach Post is isolated with little immediate reinforcement, making your presence the deciding factor between repelling the ambush and being overwhelmed.",al={"why does kanati need help","why me protect kanati","can kanati fight alone"},it="why_me",add="e12a4220"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the feud with the centaur runs deep. Protecting a fellow tribesman from assassination is a matter of survival and honor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Whitereach Post offers a key vantage point in Thousand Needles. Keeping sentries like Kanati alive helps secure Horde operations throughout the canyon."},kw={"assassination plot","assassins","centaur","galak","kanati greycloud","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"npc:kanati-greycloud","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Kanati Greycloud",level="28",faction="Horde",id=4966},src={"Protect Kanati Greycloud"}}
E["quest:5064"] = {t="quest",n="Grimtotem Spying",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, Cliffwatcher Longhorn sends you to learn what the Grimtotem are planning. Three unknown couriers visited Darkcloud Pinnacle, and guarded notes lie scattered through their village. Their words may threaten the tauren settlements of Thousand Needles.",h="At Freewind Post, Cliffwatcher Longhorn sends you to learn what the Grimtotem are planning.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Wind",b="Freewind Post clings to high spires, where its defenders watch their hostile cousins. The Grimtotem have long resented the Horde and kept to strongholds atop Darkcloud Pinnacle. Then Cliffwatcher Longhorn noticed a change. Three unknown agents arrived over several weeks and met secretly with clan leaders. He suspects they brought orders or proposed alliances against Thunder Bluff's presence in the canyon.",sp=0},{t="Infiltration of Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a fortified village of sheer mesas joined by wooden rope bridges. Dense patrols of hostile Grimtotem warriors and shamans guard the way in. Longhorn's scouts found the agents' messages locked in separate chests among the central dwellings and outer bluffs. You cross the settlement to recover all three notes and take the clan's private words under its watchful eyes.",sp=0},{t="Dire Portents",b="Cliffwatcher Longhorn reads the three notes you bring back, and Freewind Post's fears deepen. The messages show that the Grimtotem are coordinating with outside agents for an impending move. Longhorn does not know the full scheme. He begins preparing to protect the canyon posts from sudden betrayal.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is sending agents to meet with the Grimtotem?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn knows only that three agents of unknown origin visited Darkcloud Pinnacle in recent weeks. Their backers remain unknown, their identity hidden in guarded notes.",al={"who visited grimtotem","grimtotem secret agents","who sent the notes"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Darkcloud Pinnacle located?",a="Darkcloud Pinnacle lies in western Thousand Needles, southeast of the Great Lift. A marked path with a blue totem climbs the mesa cliffs to the village, where wooden bridges join several high pinnacles.",al={"where is darkcloud pinnacle","how to get to darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Grimtotem hostile to other tauren?",a="The Grimtotem believe tauren are superior to all other races and reject Cairne Bloodhoof's alliance with the Horde. Some live under a fragile peace in Thunder Bluff, while clans on Darkcloud Pinnacle are openly hostile to both the Horde and the Alliance.",al={"why do grimtotem hate horde","grimtotem vs thunder bluff","are grimtotem evil"},it="hostile"},{q="Who gives the quest Grimtotem Spying?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn gives you this work at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles after you have proved reliable by completing earlier tasks for the post.",al={"who starts grimtotem spying","grimtotem spying quest giver"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What prerequisite quests are required before this one?",a="Before Longhorn trusts you with this work, you complete 'Message to Freewind Post' and 'Pacify the Centaur'.",al={"prereqs for grimtotem spying","how to unlock grimtotem spying","grimtotem spying chain"},gp=true},{q="What happens when you turn in the three secret notes?",a="When Cliffwatcher Longhorn reads the three notes, he is shocked and calls the news dire. He says Freewind Post must prepare defenses against the Grimtotem's scheme.",al={"grimtotem spying completion","what do the notes say"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Cliffwatcher Longhorn want this done?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn has watched three mysterious agents visit Darkcloud Pinnacle over recent weeks to confer secretly with the Grimtotem Clan. The Grimtotem are notoriously treacherous and untrustworthy, and their clandestine meetings signal that a quiet plot is brewing in the Needles. Longhorn needs those guarded messages retrieved before whatever scheme they are concocting can strike Freewind Post unprepared.",al={"why grimtotem spying","cliffwatcher longhorn motives","why spy on grimtotem"},it="motive",add="e48c00e3"},{q="Who are you sent against at Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="You are sent directly into the heart of Darkcloud Pinnacle, a fortified village inhabited by the Grimtotem Clan. Unlike the peaceful tribes under Cairne Bloodhoof, this aggressive and secretive tauren clan fiercely guards its territory across the spires of Thousand Needles. Infiltrating their settlement means braving their sentries and raiding their guarded chests to uncover what they are hiding.",al={"who is at darkcloud pinnacle","who are you infiltrating","grimtotem spying target"},it="target",add="219e0f02"},{q="Why does Cliffwatcher Longhorn entrust this mission to you?",a="You have already proven your loyalty and strength by assisting Freewind Post and dealing with the local centaur threat. Infiltrating a heavily fortified Grimtotem mesa is a delicate and deadly covert operation, not an open assault for the post's standard guards. Longhorn needs a proven, capable outsider who can slip in, secure the documents, and survive.",al={"why does longhorn send you","why me grimtotem spying"},it="why_me",add="c76c115b"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, the Grimtotem's betrayal strikes at a society built on harmony and family honor. Their secret meetings with unknown conspirators threaten what Cairne Bloodhoof has built.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you depend on Freewind Post as a vital route through southern Kalimdor. Grimtotem plotting at Darkcloud Pinnacle puts the fragile supply lines between the Barrens and Tanaris at risk.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can use stealth to recover the three chests from Darkcloud Pinnacle's suspended bridges and heavily patrolled buildings."},kw={"cliffwatcher longhorn","darkcloud pinnacle","freewind post","grimtotem","secret notes","spying","tauren","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","quest:4841","quest:4542","quest:5147","npc:lakota-windsong","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="28",faction="Horde",id=5064},src={"Grimtotem Spying"}}
E["quest:5147"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted - Arnak Grimtotem",z="thousandneedles",s="At Freewind Post, a Horde bounty calls for Arnak Grimtotem’s death. The authorities seek the violent Grimtotem exile for murder and kidnapping on the mesas above the canyon.",h="At Freewind Post, a Horde bounty calls for Arnak Grimtotem’s death.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Crime",b="Tauren of the Horde and the reclusive Grimtotem have long been at odds. Arnak worsened that strife by murdering a tauren and abducting the victim’s sister, Lakota Windsong. Branded an outcast, he drew the notice of Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post. Longhorn sanctioned an open bounty calling for Arnak’s death.",sp=0},{t="Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Arnak has taken refuge on the high northern cliff mesas of Darkcloud Pinnacle. Grimtotem encampments spread across the high crags near the entrance to Razorfen Downs, linked by rope bridges. Lakota Windsong is held captive there and waits for rescue. Anyone who reaches her must cross the Grimtotem bridges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Arnak Grimtotem is a tauren outcast who murdered a tauren and kidnapped Lakota Windsong. His crimes led Freewind Post to put a bounty on his head.",al={"who is arnak","arnak grimtotem lore","who is the wanted tauren"},it="target"},{q="Where can Arnak Grimtotem be found?",a="Arnak is high on the northern cliff mesas of Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles. Reach the winding path south of the Great Lift, then cross the high wooden bridges toward Razorfen Downs.",al={"where is arnak","arnak grimtotem location","how to find arnak"},gp=true},{q="Who is Lakota Windsong?",a="Lakota Windsong is a tauren captive held by Arnak on Darkcloud Pinnacle. Arnak murdered her brother during her abduction, and she remains stranded on the mesa until he is dealt with.",al={"who is lakota","lakota windsong story"}},{q="Who offers the bounty reward?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post manages the bounty. He rewards travelers who bring Arnak’s severed hoof as proof that the rogue tauren has been brought to justice.",al={"who turns in arnak","bounty turn in","cliffwatcher longhorn reward"}},{q="Is Arnak officially working for the Grimtotem tribe?",a="The bounty calls Arnak an outcast, showing he acted beyond tribal law. He has taken refuge within the Grimtotem stronghold of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"is arnak with grimtotem","arnak tribe status"}},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="Hunters must sever and return Arnak’s Hoof to Cliffwatcher Longhorn at Freewind Post to verify his death and receive the bounty.",al={"what do i bring cliffwatcher longhorn","arnak proof","arnaks hoof"},it="item"},{q="Why is Freewind Post offering a bounty on Arnak Grimtotem?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn and the defenders of Freewind Post posted the bounty to bring an end to Arnak's crimes across the canyon. Branded an outcast even among his own folk, Arnak committed the brutal murder of a fellow tauren and kidnapped the victim's sister, Lakota Windsong. With the safety of travelers and local tribes threatened by his unchecked violence, Freewind Post wants him permanently eliminated to restore justice to the Thousand Needles.",al={"arnak grimtotem bounty why","why kill arnak","why is arnak wanted"},it="motive",add="f1e95c6b"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren loyal to Cairne Bloodhoof, you can see tracking down Arnak as tribal justice. He is a kinslayer who dishonored tauren traditions by abducting Lakota Windsong.",["faction:Horde"]="Freewind Post is the Horde’s lifeline through Thousand Needles. By eliminating renegades on Darkcloud Pinnacle, you secure the heights along the canyon floor."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","bounty","cliffwatcher longhorn","darkcloud pinnacle","freewind post","lakota windsong","outcast","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","npc:lakota-windsong","quest:4904","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:freewind-post","quest:5064","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren"},m={start="Wanted Poster - Arnak Grimtotem",["end"]="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",level="29",faction="Horde",id=5147,ri={"Arnak's Hoof"}},src={"Wanted - Arnak Grimtotem"}}
E["quest:5151"] = {t="quest",n="Hypercapacitor Gizmo",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, Wizlo Bearingshiner waits at Whitereach Post after a centaur ambush. He needs his invention back from the wreckage, where a caged panther wears it around its neck.",h="In Thousand Needles, Wizlo Bearingshiner waits at Whitereach Post after a centaur ambush.",sec={{t="Ambush in the Needles",b="Beneath Thousand Needles' sandstone spires, centaur guard the canyon floor. Just north of Whitereach Post, they overran a trade caravan, killed its travelers and plundered the wagons. Only Wizlo Bearingshiner, a goblin tinkerer, escaped. He limped back to safety.",sp=0},{t="An Unlikely Guardian",b="The centaur left one ruined wagon untouched, though they looted nearly every other valuable scrap. Inside its transport cage, a ferocious, enraged panther remains bound with Wizlo's prized hypercapacitor gizmo fastened around its neck. The centaur feared the beast and left the cage closed. Now Wizlo entrusts its key to mercenaries willing to face the predator and reclaim his invention.",sp=0},{t="Tinkerer's Ambition",b="Wizlo Bearingshiner calls the hypercapacitor gizmo his finest creation, though he cannot yet say what it does. Even after lives are risked to recover it from a caged predator, he admits he still needs to tinker with the device to understand its purpose.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Wizlo Bearingshiner?",a="Wizlo Bearingshiner is a goblin tinkerer and merchant who took refuge at Whitereach Post after centaur ambushed and destroyed his caravan on Thousand Needles' canyon floor.",al={"who is wizlo","wizlo bearingshiner lore","quest giver wizlo"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the gizmo around the panther's neck?",a="The gizmo ended up fastened around the captive panther's neck during its transport or the centaur ambush. The centaur feared the beast and left the cage untouched, making the panther the device's guardian.",al={"why does the panther have the gizmo","panther necklace","collar gizmo"}},{q="Where is the wrecked caravan located?",a="The wrecked caravan lies just north of Whitereach Post in Thousand Needles, among shattered wagons and hostile centaur camps.",al={"caravan location","where to find panther cage","cage location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why didn't the centaur loot the cage?",a="Wizlo says the enraged panther was so ferocious that even the ruthless centaur marauders feared it. They left it locked in its cage rather than risk opening it.",al={"why centaur left panther","centaur afraid of panther","why is cage untouched"}},{q="What does the Hypercapacitor Gizmo actually do?",a="Wizlo calls the Hypercapacitor Gizmo his finest invention, but after its return he admits he still needs to study and tinker with it to discover what it does.",al={"what does gizmo do","hypercapacitor function","what is the gizmo"},sp=1,it="item"},{q="Who controls Whitereach Post?",a="Whitereach Post is a tauren settlement allied with the Horde. Set among the canyon mesas, it watches centaur activity and shelters Horde travelers.",al={"whitereach post faction","is whitereach horde"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Wizlo Bearingshiner want the Hypercapacitor Gizmo back?",a="Wizlo is the sole survivor of a caravan overrun by centaur in the canyon flats. He considers the hypercapacitor to be his finest invention, even admitting he still needs to figure out entirely what it does. Desperate to salvage the prized contraption from the wreckage of his expedition, he is willing to reward anyone brave enough to wrest it back.",al={"wizlo bearingshiner motive","why recover hypercapacitor","why does wizlo want gizmo"},it="motive",add="64badd6f"},{q="What beast is guarding the Hypercapacitor Gizmo?",a="The contraption hangs around the neck of an unusually ferocious, caged panther trapped inside the ruined caravan. The beast was so vicious that the raiding centaur dared not touch its iron cage when looting the rest of the supplies, leaving the predator stranded amid the debris just north of the post.",al={"who is guarding the gizmo","panther target","what is the panther"},it="target",add="01614ead"},{q="Why does Wizlo Bearingshiner need your help?",a="Wizlo barely escaped the centaur slaughter with his life and is an engineer, not a warrior. The tauren at Whitereach Post maintain their own vigil against the hostile tribes, leaving little interest or manpower to help an eccentric goblin reclaim abandoned tinkering projects from a caged monster surrounded by raiders.",al={"why does wizlo need me","why ask adventurer","why cant wizlo get gizmo"},it="why_me",add="6ff4273d"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Wizlo's frantic pursuit of an invention whose purpose he cannot quite recall shows the chaotic, trial-and-error ways of goblin engineering.",["faction:Horde"]="From Whitereach Post, Horde scouts and travelers battle the predatory centaur clans that menace routes through central Kalimdor.",["class:Hunter"]="The enraged panther in the wrecked caravan is a formidable beast, fierce enough to terrify a full warband of centaur marauders."},kw={"centaur caravan","enraged panther","goblin engineering","hypercapacitor gizmo","panther cage key","thousand needles","whitereach post","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Wizlo Bearingshiner",level="30",faction="Horde",id=5151,ri={"Hypercapacitor Gizmo"}},src={"Hypercapacitor Gizmo (quest)"}}
E["quest:5361"] = {t="quest",n="Family Tree",z="thousandneedles",s="Cliffwatcher Longhorn sends you to Ghost Walker Post with news of unusual centaur activity. His brother is there in Desolace.",h="Cliffwatcher Longhorn sends you to Ghost Walker Post with news of unusual centaur activity.",sec={{t="A Report for a Brother",b="Cliffwatcher Longhorn asks you to carry a report to his brother, Nataka, at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace. A year has passed since his last letter. Now the centaurs are acting unusually, and Nataka needs to hear what is happening.",sp=0},{t="The Way There",b="From Thousand Needles, travel to Stonetalon Mountain, north of the Crossroads. Go west into the Charred Vale, then south into Desolace. Follow the road south to Ghost Walker Post.",sp=0},{t="A Welcome at the Post",b="Nataka Longhorn welcomes you to Ghost Walker Post. He cannot say how you know Cliffwatcher, but his brother seems to trust you. The post has plenty of needs, so Nataka suggests speaking with the others there. One of them may need your help.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Cliffwatcher Longhorn trying to contact?",a="Cliffwatcher Longhorn is trying to contact his brother, Nataka Longhorn, at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace.",al={"who is nataka","longhorn brother","who receives the report"}},{q="Why is Cliffwatcher Longhorn sending a report now?",a="Cliffwatcher has not written for a year, and the centaurs have been acting unusually. Nataka needs to hear about it.",al={"why send report","centaur activity report","reason for message"}},{q="Where is Nataka Longhorn located?",a="Nataka Longhorn is at Ghost Walker Post in Desolace, reached by a road running south.",al={"nataka location","where is ghost walker post","where to deliver report"}},{q="What path leads to Ghost Walker Post from Thousand Needles?",a="From Thousand Needles, travel to Stonetalon Mountain, north of the Crossroads. Go west into the Charred Vale, then south into Desolace and follow the road to Ghost Walker Post.",al={"how to get to desolace","route to ghost walker post","travel path"}}},kw={"centaur","charred vale","cliffwatcher longhorn","desolace","family tree","ghost walker post","nataka longhorn","stonetalon","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:cliffwatcher-longhorn","subzone:ghost-walker-post","zone:desolace","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon","subzone:crossroads"},m={start="Cliffwatcher Longhorn",["end"]="Nataka Longhorn",level="35",faction="Horde",id=5361},src={"Family Tree (Thousand Needles)"}}
E["quest:5762"] = {t="quest",n="Hemet Nesingwary",z="thousandneedles",s="A crate delayed on the road from Kalimdor reaches the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale by sea. At the Mirage Raceway, Kravel Koalbeard sends special supplies to Hemet Nesingwary, the renowned big-game hunter.",h="A crate delayed on the road from Kalimdor reaches the jungles of Stranglethorn Vale by sea.",sec={{t="A Transcontinental Delivery",b="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, Kravel Koalbeard receives a long-overdue crate for one of his wealthy patrons. Hemet Nesingwary had already left Thousand Needles, but he paid to have the crate sent on to his hunting camp in Stranglethorn Vale. Kravel stays behind rather than face the arduous journey himself. So he hires passing adventurers to carry the crate across the sea.",sp=0},{t="Ammunition for the Hunt",b="North of Grom'gol Base Camp, Hemet Nesingwary's expedition receives the heavy crate. It holds specialized heavy-gauge ammunition for bringing down the jungle's dangerous predators. Hemet recognizes the white salt crust on the courier's gear. His old dealings with Kravel have brought the firepower his safari needed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this delivery begin and end?",a="The delivery starts with Kravel Koalbeard at the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, in southern Thousand Needles. It ends at Hemet Nesingwary's expedition camp in northern Stranglethorn Vale, just north of Grom'gol.",al={"quest start and end","where is hemet","where do i go"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is inside Kravel's Crate?",a="Kravel's crate holds special-gauge ammunition for big-game firearms. Hemet ordered the shot to pierce the thick hides of Stranglethorn's fiercest beasts.",al={"whats in the crate","crate contents","kravel package"},it="item"},{q="Why didn't Kravel deliver the crate himself?",a="Kravel stays busy overseeing his investments and schemes at the Mirage Raceway. He uses the coin Hemet paid in advance to hire passing adventurers rather than leave his post to cross the sea.",al={"why kravel hire someone","why does kravel need help"},it="why_me"},{q="How does Hemet know where the courier came from?",a="Hemet recognizes the salt crust on the courier's garments as a mark of the Shimmering Flats, not ordinary desert dust.",al={"desert salt","hemet dialogue salt"}},{q="What kind of relationship do Kravel and Hemet have?",a="Hemet is an old and lucrative customer of Kravel's. Kravel respects Hemet's deep pockets, while Hemet fondly calls Kravel a 'crusty old' rogue who's perpetually up to no good.",al={"kravel and hemet history","do they know each other"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Hemet Nesingwary?",a="Hemet Nesingwary is a celebrated dwarven marksman, author, and big-game hunter. He leads a safari through the perilous depths of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"who is hemet","nesingwary lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Kravel Koalbeard want this crate delivered to Hemet?",a="Kravel is maintaining a lucrative business connection. Hemet Nesingwary is a remarkably wealthy dwarf, and Kravel knows that keeping such rich clientele satisfied pays off. Hemet paid upfront for the crate to be forwarded to his hunting grounds once it arrived, so honoring the deal protects Kravel's reputation and guarantees future coin.",al={"why deliver kravel crate","kravel koalbeard motive","why send crate to hemet"},it="motive",add="4f3179a4"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you carry specialized ammunition to Hemet Nesingwary, who leads Azeroth's most famous big-game safari.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you see two roguish dwarven acquaintances scattered from Ironforge in pursuit of coin and quarry."},kw={"ammunition","hemet nesingwary","kravel koalbeard","kravel's crate","mirage raceway","shimmering flats","stranglethorn vale"},rel={"npc:kravel-koalbeard","subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Kravel Koalbeard",["end"]="Hemet Nesingwary",level="31",id=5762},src={"Hemet Nesingwary (quest)"}}
E["quest:6627"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="At Braug Dimspirit’s perch in Stonetalon, you face a test of ancient history. Having retrieved the tome Legacy of the Aspects, you must show what its lessons taught you. A wrong answer sends you far across Kalimdor.",h="At Braug Dimspirit’s perch in Stonetalon, you face a test of ancient history.",sec={{t="A Trial of Wisdom",b="Braug Dimspirit’s trial follows the tests Dorn Plainstalker began at the Weathered Nook. It calls for understanding, not martial survival or blind trust. Braug lives among the crags of the Stonetalon Mountains. He expects seekers to recover ancient texts and learn from their pages.",sp=0},{t="Legacy of the Aspects",b="The lesson concerns how the Dragon Aspects were created and divided, and the pact they made long before the Great Sundering. Braug asks what the tome says about the Earth Warder, Neltharion. His madness and betrayal reshaped Azeroth’s surface. You must understand this history before continuing along the path of wisdom.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Guesswork",b="Braug Dimspirit sends seekers who answer incorrectly away by mystic means. A wrong answer carries you to Camp Taurajo in the southern Barrens, far from the hermit. To face Braug’s scrutiny again, you must make the long trek back into Stonetalon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the answer to Braug Dimspirit's question?",a="Braug asks you to name the Earth Warder in Legacy of the Aspects. The answer is Neltharion, the Black Aspect who turned against his fellow dragons.",al={"braug question answer","test of lore answer","legacy of the aspects question"},gp=true},{q="What happens if you answer incorrectly?",a="A wrong answer brings immediate magical banishment to Camp Taurajo in the Barrens. You must travel back to Braug’s perch in the Stonetalon Mountains to try again.",al={"wrong answer test of lore","failed test of lore","teleported to taurajo"},gp=true},{q="Who is Braug Dimspirit?",a="Braug Dimspirit is an elder hermit in the Stonetalon Mountains who tests the Horde’s knowledge and lore. He continues the spiritual trials Dorn Plainstalker began in Thousand Needles.",al={"braug dimspirit","who gives test of lore"},it="identity"},{q="How does this connect to the trials in Thousand Needles?",a="Dorn Plainstalker began the trials at the Weathered Nook in Thousand Needles with the Test of Faith. After testing physical and spiritual trust, Dorn sends worthy initiates across Kalimdor to elders who test their intellect, resolve, and strength.",al={"dorn plainstalker connection","test of faith chain"},it="origin"},{q="What book is Braug quizzing you about?",a="Braug tests your understanding of Legacy of the Aspects, an ancient treatise about the titans blessing the five Great Dragon Aspects to guard Azeroth.",al={"what book braug","legacy of the aspects"},it="item"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="Passing Braug’s test of the Dragon Aspects leads to further investigations into ancient history. Seekers must search distant regions for lost records and ancestral knowledge.",al={"what is after test of lore","next quest in test of lore"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is Braug Dimspirit testing you?",a="Braug Dimspirit serves as an examiner in the trials that began in Thousand Needles. While other trials challenge your martial prowess or faith, the Test of Lore is designed to ensure you do not rely solely on brute force. By requiring you to retrieve ancient texts and comprehend their contents, Braug seeks to cultivate wisdom and historical understanding in those who aspire to represent the Horde.",al={"why does braug test you","braug dimspirit purpose","why test of lore"},it="motive",add="a70a9b29"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face trials in Kalimdor that demand more than brute force. Warriors and shamans alike are expected to understand the ancient scars and draconic powers that shaped the continent.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor ancestral wisdom and ancient history. This trial asks young champions to understand the world’s balance before they march into danger.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you may recognize the skill behind Braug’s teleportation ward. Stonetalon’s hermits wield ancient magic to discipline careless scholars."},kw={"aspects","braug dimspirit","earth warder","neltharion","stonetalon","taurajo","test of faith","weathered nook"},rel={"quest:1152","quest:1149","npc:dorn-plainstalker","zone:stonetalon","subzone:camp-taurajo","subzone:weathered-nook","zone:barrens","zone:thousandneedles"},m={start="Braug Dimspirit",level="30",faction="Horde",id=6627},src={"Test of Lore (3)"}}
E["quest:6628"] = {t="quest",n="Test of Lore",z="thousandneedles",s="In the Undercity, initiates face a test of history with Parqual Fintallas. They have scoured the world for historical texts, and this examination is part of spiritual trials begun in Thousand Needles.",h="In the Undercity, initiates face a test of history with Parqual Fintallas.",sec={{t="A Trial of Knowledge",b="The Test of Lore is one of the spiritual trials begun in Thousand Needles. Dorn Plainstalker set the trials at the Weathered Nook. This examination carries candidates from the wind-carved canyons of Thousand Needles to the Undercity, where Parqual Fintallas tests their knowledge of history and holds each seeker to a high standard.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge's Genesis",b="Parqual Fintallas tests initiates on the book 'Beginnings of the Undead Threat,' which tells how the Scourge began in Lordaeron. He asks about the being on the Frozen Throne: Ner'zhul, once an elder shaman, whose essence the Burning Legion forged into the Lich King. This grim lineage helps explain the Forsaken's existence and the dangers facing Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the answer to Parqual's question?",a="Parqual Fintallas asks for the Lich King's original name: Ner'zhul, the ancient orc shaman whose spirit was bound to the Frozen Throne.",al={"lich king answer","parqual question","test of lore answer"},gp=true},{q="What happens if you answer the question wrong?",a="A wrong answer gives you the Mark of Shame debuff. You must wait out the penalty before Parqual lets you try the examination again.",al={"mark of shame","wrong answer test of lore"},gp=true},{q="Where does this quest chain begin?",a="Dorn Plainstalker begins the wider series of spiritual trials at the Weathered Nook in Thousand Needles, among its towering spires.",al={"where does test of lore start","dorn plainstalker questline"},gp=true},{q="Where is Parqual Fintallas located?",a="Parqual Fintallas is in the Undercity, among the Forsaken's underground libraries and corridors, where he examines prospective students.",al={"find parqual","parqual fintallas location"},gp=true},{q="What text is this trial based on?",a="The test draws on 'Beginnings of the Undead Threat,' a book about the origins of the Plague of Undeath and the making of the Lich King.",al={"which book for test of lore","beginnings book"},it="item"},{q="Why is a Thousand Needles quest sending people to Undercity?",a="The tauren's trials challenge every part of an adventurer. For this examination, candidates cross the sea to seek scholarly records kept in the ruins of Lordaeron.",al={"why go to undercity","thousand needles undercity"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Parqual Fintallas want this done?",a="Parqual Fintallas is putting your dedication to the pursuit of knowledge to the ultimate test. He believes that knowledge is paramount to survival in this perilous world—the more you learn and observe, the more of the truth you will see. Having tasked you with procuring the tome on the Undead Threat, he demands proof that you actually studied and absorbed its grim history rather than merely running an errand.",al={"parqual motive","why is parqual testing me","why test of lore"},it="motive",add="b37475e3"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you follow an elder tradition that sends you to learn the grim histories of your northern Forsaken allies and the world beyond Kalimdor.",["race:Undead"]="As undead, you face a history bound to Forsaken identity: Ner'zhul's tragic transformation and the curse that bound you before Sylvanas broke the Lich King's grip.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you strengthen ties between Kalimdor's tribes and the kingdom beneath Lordaeron, and learn that wisdom matters as much to survival as strength."},kw={"dorn plainstalker","lich king","mark of shame","nerzhul","parqual fintallas","test of lore","thousand needles","undercity","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:parqual-fintallas","quest:1599","quest:1149","npc:dorn-plainstalker","zone:undercity","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:weathered-nook","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Parqual Fintallas",level="30",faction="Horde",id=6628},src={"Test of Lore (6)"}}
E["quest:8682"] = {t="quest",n="Skyseer the Elder",z="thousandneedles",s="During the Lunar Festival, Skyseer the Elder waits atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Travelers come to honor the ancestors and receive his blessing.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Skyseer the Elder waits atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Needles",b="Wooden bluffs tower over Freewind Post. Elder Skyseer rests among them in a shaft of celestial light, near the bridges leading to the great mechanical lifts. Winds sweep across the mesas of Thousand Needles around his ghostly form.",sp=0},{t="The Ancestral Path",b="During the Lunar Festival, Elder Skyseer welcomes travelers who come to honor the past. He can guide them to his kin across Kalimdor, including Elder Morningdew and Elder Runetotem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Skyseer located?",a="Elder Skyseer stands on Freewind Post's upper mesa in Thousand Needles. He is near the suspension bridges by the cliffside lifts.",al={"skyseer location","where is skyseer","freewind post elder"}},{q="What is the purpose of seeking out Elder Skyseer?",a="During the Lunar Festival, travelers visit ancestral spirits such as Elder Skyseer to pay their respects, receive a Coin of Ancestry, and learn where to find other elders.",al={"why visit skyseer","skyseer quest objective","lunar festival skyseer"}},{q="Why is Elder Skyseer glowing?",a="A bright shaft of moonlight shines on Elder Skyseer, as it does on other honored spirits visiting during the festival. It marks him as an ancestor communing with the living.",al={"why is skyseer in light","elder light beam"}},{q="Which other elders does Skyseer provide directions for?",a="Elder Skyseer can guide travelers to nearby ancestral spirits, including Elder Morningdew, Elder Runetotem, Elder Dreamseer, and Elder Wildmane.",al={"other elders","who does skyseer mention","skyseer directions"}},{q="Can Alliance travelers speak with Elder Skyseer?",a="Yes. Freewind Post is a heavily fortified Horde settlement. Alliance travelers must move carefully around the guards and avoid provoking bloodshed to reach the elder.",al={"can alliance talk to skyseer","alliance freewind post elder"}},{q="What happens when you speak to Elder Skyseer?",a="When you greet Elder Skyseer and pay homage, he commends your spirit and grants a token of ancestral blessing. The encounter is brief.",al={"skyseer reward","completing skyseer the elder"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Elder Skyseer rests within the Horde stronghold of Freewind Post. As an Alliance pilgrim, you must navigate its perilous heights and hostile guards to pay your respects.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, greeting an honored elder atop one of your people's most iconic mesa aeries reflects the Shu'halo's deep reverence for their ancestors.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, communing with ancient spirits beneath the moonlight follows the teachings of Cenarius and honors those who walked the land before."},kw={"ancestor","coins of ancestry","elder skyseer","freewind post","lunar festival","skyseer","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:elder-skyseer","subzone:freewind-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:elder-morningdew","npc:elder-runetotem","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Skyseer",id=8682},src={"Skyseer the Elder"}}
E["quest:8724"] = {t="quest",n="Morningdew the Elder",z="thousandneedles",s="In Thousand Needles, pilgrims seek Morningdew the Elder beneath a beam of starlight during the Lunar Festival. She offers wisdom and directions to elders across Kalimdor.",h="In Thousand Needles, pilgrims seek Morningdew the Elder beneath a beam of starlight during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Celestial Presence in the Canyons",b="During the Lunar Festival, ancient ancestor spirits appear across Azeroth to bless travelers. In Thousand Needles, Morningdew the Elder stands beneath a shaft of lunar light, amid red stone and industrial noise. She urges mortal travelers to turn from earthly concerns and look to the stars.",sp=0},{t="Wisdom of the Heavens",b="Morningdew points seekers toward the countless stars for answers to earthly mysteries. She also guides festival pilgrims to other honored spirits across the lands: Elder High Mountain, Elder Grimtotem, Elder Mistwalker, Elder Moonwarden, and Elder Windtotem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Morningdew?",a="Morningdew the Elder is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival. Beneath starlight, she offers wisdom and guides travelers who come to honor the elders.",al={"elder morningdew","morningdew lore","who is morningdew"}},{q="Where can Elder Morningdew be found?",a="You can find Morningdew the Elder in Thousand Needles, beneath a bright pillar of light from the sky.",al={"morningdew location","where is elder morningdew","find elder morningdew"}},{q="What is the purpose of visiting Elder Morningdew?",a="During the Lunar Festival, travelers visit Morningdew to honor the ancestors, receive their blessings, and learn where other elders can be found.",al={"why visit morningdew","morningdew purpose","lunar festival elder"}},{q="Which other elders does Morningdew know about?",a="Morningdew gives directions to Elder High Mountain, Elder Grimtotem, Elder Mistwalker, Elder Moonwarden, and Elder Windtotem.",al={"morningdew other elders","elders list morningdew","who does morningdew mention"}},{q="Why is there a pillar of light shining down on her?",a="A beam of celestial starlight shines on each ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival, marking their presence and bond with the heavens.",al={"morningdew light beam","shaft of light elder","why does elder glow"}},{q="What does Morningdew teach pilgrims?",a="Morningdew teaches pilgrims to seek answers to earthly mysteries among the countless stars. She urges the wise and fortunate to look upward for truth.",al={"morningdew advice","morningdew dialogue","what does morningdew say"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the Lunar Festival's celestial elders as a link to Elune, nature, and the ancestral communion honored by Cenarion circles.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know that communion with honored spirits like Morningdew helps you understand the balance between ancestors and elements throughout the world.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you recognize in the elders beneath starlight an ancient tradition of honoring the heavens and Kalimdor's old wisdom.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know that reverence for ancestral elders is central to your culture. A pilgrimage to spirits like Morningdew holds deep meaning."},kw={"ancestor","elder morningdew","elders","lunar festival","morningdew the elder","shimmering flats","starlight","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:elder-morningdew","zone:thousandneedles","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Morningdew",id=8724},src={"Morningdew the Elder"}}
E["subzone:camp-e-thok"] = {t="subzone",n="Camp E'thok",z="thousandneedles",s="In northwestern Thousand Needles, caravans risk ambush below Camp E'thok. Galak centaur hunt travelers in the canyon.",h="In northwestern Thousand Needles, caravans risk ambush below Camp E'thok.",sec={{t="A Galak Stronghold",b="Galak centaur hunt travelers in the canyon at Camp E'thok. Their camp lies in northwestern Thousand Needles. From there, the clan ambushes merchant caravans crossing the riverbed below. One caravan carried the goblin Wizlo Bearingshiner. The centaur seized its goods, but Wizlo's fierce pet panther kept his prized gadget beyond their reach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Camp E'thok?",a="The Galak clan of centaur lives at Camp E'thok. The aggressive tribe dominates parts of northwestern Thousand Needles.",al={"who is in camp ethok","camp ethok inhabitants","who controls camp ethok"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to Wizlo Bearingshiner here?",a="Galak centaur from Camp E'thok ambushed Wizlo Bearingshiner's caravan and seized its goods. They could not take his prized gadget, secured around the collar of his fierce pet panther.",al={"wizlo bearingshiner raid","goblin caravan attacked","what did centaur steal from wizlo"},it="history"},{q="Where is Camp E'thok located?",a="Camp E'thok lies in northwestern Thousand Needles along the base of the canyon walls.",al={"camp ethok location","where is camp ethok","camp ethok map"},gp=true},{q="What is Camp E'thok?",a="Camp E'thok is an active encampment of the Galak centaur tribe, settled in the canyons of northwestern Thousand Needles. The centaur use this fortified site as a base to stage violent ambushes and raids against travelers and merchant caravans passing through the gorges below.",al={"what is camp ethok","camp ethok lore","tell me about camp ethok"},it="place",add="740a44e0"},{q="Is Camp E'thok dangerous?",a="Camp E'thok is extremely dangerous. The Galak centaurs dwelling here attack outsiders on sight, preying upon any trade caravans daring to traverse the canyon. Anyone wandering into the camp will find themselves facing hostile warriors, shamans, and whatever plunder they have violently gathered.",al={"is camp ethok hostile","how dangerous is camp ethok","danger camp ethok"},it="danger",add="7ec291b4"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may recall the ancestral war between tauren and centaur across southern Kalimdor when you see the Galak centaur's aggression at Camp E'thok."},kw={"camp e'thok","centaur","ethok","galak","thousand needles","wizlo bearingshiner"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","npc:wizlo-bearingshiner","topic:goblin"},src={"Camp E'thok"}}
E["subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkcloud Pinnacle",z="thousandneedles",s="Grimtotem tauren hold Darkcloud Pinnacle above the canyon east of the Great Lift. From their linked mesas, they disrupt the region and pursue secret dealings.",h="Grimtotem tauren hold Darkcloud Pinnacle above the canyon east of the Great Lift.",sec={{t="A Clifftop Stronghold",b="Darkcloud Pinnacle rises above the canyon basin across three main mesas, joined by rope bridges. You can climb a steep natural slope from the canyon floor, then cross wooden bridges. A high crossing near Razorfen Downs offers another way up. From these windswept rocks, Grimtotem watchers survey the valley. The heights guard them from easy attack and leave them apart from the wider tauren tribes.",sp=0},{t="Schemes on the Mesas",b="Arnak Grimtotem and Harb Foulmountain are among the leaders directing Darkcloud Pinnacle. Correspondence found on the mesa points to Grimtotem dealings with dark, unknown powers. Their ambitions reach beyond the peace Cairne Bloodhoof forged in Thunder Bluff.",sp=1,bt={"q4542.4"}}},faq={{q="Who controls Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="The Grimtotem clan holds Darkcloud Pinnacle. These aggressive, reclusive tauren are hostile to most outsiders and deeply distrustful of the Horde.",al={"who lives at darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle owners","who is at darkcloud pinnacle"},it="residents"},{q="How do you reach Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="You can climb a natural ramp from the canyon floor to an adjacent mesa, then cross wooden rope bridges. Another route crosses a bridge near Razorfen Downs.",al={"how to get up darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle path","entrance to darkcloud pinnacle"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Who leads the Grimtotem here?",a="Arnak Grimtotem and Harb Foulmountain are among the prominent Grimtotem figures overseeing the settlement.",al={"darkcloud pinnacle leaders","who leads darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem bosses"},it="leader"},{q="What are the Grimtotem plotting here?",a="The Grimtotem at Darkcloud Pinnacle keep secret communications with an unknown dark influence. Their shadowy goals threaten stability in Thousand Needles.",al={"what is happening at darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem conspiracy"},sp=1,it="threat",bt={"q4542.4"}},{q="What is Darkcloud Pinnacle?",a="Darkcloud Pinnacle is a fortified tauren village perched high above the canyon floor of Thousand Needles, just east of the Great Lift. It spans three inhabited mesas linked together by suspended rope bridges. The settlement serves as a major stronghold for the Grimtotem tribe, an aggressive and isolationist tauren clan that jealously defends its territory from outsiders.",al={"what is darkcloud pinnacle","darkcloud pinnacle info","about darkcloud pinnacle"},it="place",add="0ab7147f"},{q="Is Darkcloud Pinnacle dangerous?",a="Very dangerous. The Grimtotem tauren who occupy Darkcloud Pinnacle are violently hostile to trespassers and maintain a heavy guard across the entire settlement. With its high mesas and narrow rope bridges, fighting here carries the constant peril of falling into the canyon below, and the tribe's shamans and warriors are prepared to kill anyone who ventures up the slopes.",al={"darkcloud pinnacle danger","how dangerous is darkcloud pinnacle","is darkcloud dangerous"},it="danger",add="44a431c5"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the Grimtotem's treachery on these mesas set against the unity and peace Cairne Bloodhoof seeks among the tribes.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you find the Grimtotem hostile here. They menace travelers passing from the Great Lift into Thousand Needles."},kw={"arnak grimtotem","darkcloud pinnacle","grimtotem","harb foulmountain","mesa","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:great-lift","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","topic:tauren"},src={"Darkcloud Pinnacle"}}
E["subzone:freewind-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Freewind Post",z="thousandneedles",s="Freewind Post guards the Horde’s hold in Thousand Needles from a high canyon mesa. Tauren lifts and winding rope bridges lead to its refuge, where the Horde faces centaur warbands and prepares for the frontier.",h="Freewind Post guards the Horde’s hold in Thousand Needles from a high canyon mesa.",sec={{t="A Fortress in the Sky",b="Freewind Post clings to the canyon mesas, where height helps guard its people. Galak centaur command the arid floor, but cannot climb the sheer cliffs or easily breach the heavy wooden lifts that carry Horde travelers upward. Rope and plank bridges link the post to neighboring spires, sheltering the outpost above.\n\nHarpies screech along the bluffs, while the tauren tend the nearby wyvern grounds at Highperch. There, they cull wild eggs and raise the hatchlings as loyal wind rider mounts for the Horde.",sp=0},{t="Shadows from Darkcloud Pinnacle",b="Freewind Post watches the Grimtotem tribe at Darkcloud Pinnacle, northwest across the canyon. Once tolerated as stubborn traditionalists, the Grimtotem under Chieftain Arnak now turn to kidnapping, murder, and violence. Suspicious rituals and whispers of dark power surround the nearby peaks.\n\nThe local tauren watch the skies and rope bridges with growing dread. Their most dangerous enemies may sit entrenched across the canyon winds, not prowl the salt flats below.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Freewind Post built so high up on a mesa?",a="Freewind Post rises above the canyon floor to guard against hostile Galak centaur warbands. Centaur excel on flat ground, but cannot climb sheer cliffs or easily breach the tauren’s mechanical wooden lifts.",al={"why is freewind post in the sky","why mesa","freewind post elevation"},it="purpose"},{q="How do you get up and down from the post?",a="Most travelers ride the large mechanical wooden lifts at the base of the main mesa. A back route winds between neighboring rock pillars over rope bridges and wooden ramps. One careless step can mean a lethal fall to the canyon floor.",al={"how to get up freewind post","freewind post elevator","freewind entrance"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="What is the relationship between Freewind Post and the Grimtotem?",a="Relations between Freewind Post and the Grimtotem are deeply strained. The Grimtotem at Darkcloud Pinnacle, northwest of the post, face accusations of murder, kidnapping, and unprovoked hostility toward other tauren. The post’s defenders keep watch on their neighbors.",al={"grimtotem freewind post","darkcloud pinnacle freewind","why are grimtotem bad here"},it="conflict"},{q="What importance does Highperch have to the post?",a="Highperch is an ancestral nesting ground for wild wyverns just across the canyon. The tauren of Freewind Post watch the beasts and cull eggs from their nests, then raise them as wind rider mounts for the Horde.",al={"why highperch","highperch wyverns freewind"},it="ties"},{q="What is Freewind Post?",a="Freewind Post is a fortified Horde outpost situated high atop a towering stone needle in the middle of Thousand Needles. Populated predominantly by tauren loyal to Thunder Bluff, it serves as a central hub of trade, defense, and communication for travelers navigating the canyons between the Southern Barrens, Feralas, and Tanaris.",al={"what is freewind post","freewind post","about freewind post"},it="place",add="1f4dfdb3"},{q="What happened at Freewind Post?",a="The tauren established Freewind Post atop the high mesas to build a defensible stronghold beyond the reach of the rampaging Galak centaur below. Over time, it grew into an essential outpost for securing the canyons, studying and harvesting wyvern mounts from nearby Highperch, and monitoring the increasingly hostile Grimtotem clan at Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"freewind post history","history of freewind post","what happened here"},it="history",add="17ef52e2"},{q="Who lives in or runs Freewind Post?",a="The post is inhabited and defended by Horde-aligned tauren loyal to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Alongside brave braves guarding the bridges and lifts, it is home to merchants, wind rider masters, and elders who coordinate patrols against regional threats like the Galak centaur, screeching harpies, and treachery from the nearby Grimtotem.",al={"who runs freewind post","freewind post residents","who lives here"},it="residents",add="5739dc9d"},{q="Is Freewind Post dangerous?",a="The outpost itself is well protected, but its sheer height makes a misstep off the edges or swaying rope bridges fatal. Beyond its perimeter, the surrounding canyon floor crawls with hostile Galak centaur, ravaging harpies roost in the canyon spires, and the sinister Grimtotem tribe plots against the town from neighboring Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"is freewind post dangerous","freewind post dangers","threats to freewind post"},it="danger",add="880e92a9"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a shu'halo, you can see how Freewind Post uses mesa heights to guard against traditional centaur marauders while tending the bluffs’ ancestral wyverns.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can rely on Freewind Post as a major sanctuary and flight connection between the Southern Barrens and Tanaris. It supports travel across central Kalimdor."},kw={"darkcloud pinnacle","elevator","freewind post","galak","highperch","mesa","tauren","thousand needles","wyverns"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:highperch","topic:grimtotem-tribe","topic:centaur","topic:tauren","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Freewind Post"}}
E["subzone:great-lift"] = {t="subzone",n="Great Lift",z="thousandneedles",s="At the Great Lift, travelers cross between the southern Barrens and Thousand Needles. Tauren platforms carry people and supplies between the rim and canyon floor, while quilboar threaten the southern road.",h="At the Great Lift, travelers cross between the southern Barrens and Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Gateway Carved from Wood and Rope",b="At the rim between the southern Barrens and Thousand Needles, two wooden platforms hang over the canyon. Heavy timber, braided rope, and counterweighted pulleys carry caravans, couriers, and warriors across the sheer drop. Brave Moonhorn watches from the top platform, and Grish Longrunner keeps watch below. They guide travelers along the road and help cargo pass safely.",sp=0},{t="Dangers at the Rim",b="The road to the Great Lift crosses hostile ground in the southern Barrens. Quilboar tribes have pushed south and now threaten the route between Thousand Needles and the northern trails. Travelers making the long journey must fend off razorfen raiders before they reach the wooden platforms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built the Great Lift?",a="Tauren designed and built the Great Lift to bridge the sheer gap between the Barrens and Thousand Needles' canyon floor.",al={"who made the great lift","great lift builders","tauren elevator origin"},it="origin"},{q="Why is traveling to the lift dangerous?",a="Quilboar from the southern Barrens have pushed toward the rim. Their raiding parties harass or ambush caravans and couriers on the way to the lift.",al={"why are there quilboar here","southern barrens danger","lift road blocked"},it="threat"},{q="Who watches over the Great Lift?",a="Brave Moonhorn and Grish Longrunner watch over the Great Lift. They assist Horde travelers and keep watch over the routes and surrounding wilderness.",al={"who guards the lift","lift keepers","tauren at the lift"},it="residents"},{q="Where does the Great Lift lead?",a="The platforms carry travelers down to Thousand Needles' canyon floor and up into the southern Barrens.",al={"where does lift go","what is below the lift","lift destination"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Great Lift?",a="The Great Lift is a massive tauren-engineered elevator situated along the precipice dividing the southern Barrens from the canyon floor of Thousand Needles. It serves as the primary route for travelers, merchants, and messengers seeking to descend the towering cliffs safely without braving treacherous drop-offs.",al={"what is great lift","great lift info","about great lift"},it="place",add="15c17117"},{q="Is the Great Lift dangerous?",a="The mechanical platform itself is sound, but the surrounding approaches are fraught with peril. Aggressive quilboar tribes in the southern Barrens have expanded their territory right up to the cliffs, ambushing caravans and threatening to cut off travelers attempting to reach the elevator edge.",al={"is great lift dangerous","great lift safe","threats near great lift"},it="danger",add="9d5e1aa9"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the lift links central Kalimdor to Thousand Needles and Shimmering Flats. It opens a vital route to those isolated reaches.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, your people built the lift from sturdy timber and counterweights. It carries travelers across rugged country without scarring the earth."},kw={"brave moonhorn","elevator","great lift","grish longrunner","quilboar","the barrens","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens","npc:brave-moonhorn","npc:grish-longrunner","topic:tauren","topic:quilboar"},src={"Great Lift"}}
E["subzone:highperch"] = {t="subzone",n="Highperch",z="thousandneedles",s="Wild wyverns nest among the crags of Highperch, above the western Thousand Needles canyon. Their prides guard the heights and their young.",h="Wild wyverns nest among the crags of Highperch, above the western Thousand Needles canyon.",sec={{t="Aerie of the Wyverns",b="Highperch rises from the canyon floor, giving Kalimdor’s native wyverns a rugged refuge. Its height shields them from predators and offers a clear launch for hunts across Thousand Needles.\n\nWyvern prides guard their nests under watchful patriarchs and matriarchs. They fiercely defend their territory from any intruder who reaches their high domain.",sp=0},{t="A Refuge in the Heights",b="The cliffs draw a few travelers and hunters willing to brave the climb. Pao'ka Swiftmountain, a tauren scout, is stranded on the heights and needs help reaching Whitereach Post.\n\nThose who climb the cliffs face dozens of razor-sharp talons and venomous tails.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures live at Highperch?",a="Wild wyverns and wind riders live at Highperch. Protective patriarchs, consorts, and soaring adults defend their clifftop nests.",al={"highperch beasts","what is at highperch","highperch mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Where is Highperch located?",a="Highperch rises in western Thousand Needles. A winding ramp follows the canyon’s southern wall to the heights.",al={"highperch location","how to find highperch","where is highperch"},gp=true},{q="Why is Highperch significant to the Horde?",a="Wyverns, also called wind riders, are vital flying mounts of the Horde. They allied with the orcs during the Third War, and roosts like Highperch hold a thriving wild population.",al={"horde connection to highperch","wyverns and horde","why do orcs care about highperch"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Pao'ka Swiftmountain?",a="Pao'ka Swiftmountain is a tauren scout stranded among Highperch’s wyvern nests. He needs an escort to Whitereach Post.",al={"paoka swiftmountain","tauren at highperch","who got trapped at highperch"},it="people"},{q="What is Highperch?",a="Highperch is an elevated mesa and nesting ground rising above the western canyons of the Thousand Needles. It serves as one of the primary natural habitats for the region's proud wild wyverns, filled with their roosts and soaring flocks.",al={"what is highperch","highperch info","about highperch"},it="place",add="0cf6e9b4"},{q="What happened at Highperch?",a="For generations, wild wyverns have made their nests high upon this cliffside haven. The tauren scout Pao'ka Swiftmountain is stranded amidst the crags and seeks help returning to Whitereach Post.",al={"highperch history","what happened here","highperch past"},it="history",add="a95be4dc"},{q="Is Highperch dangerous?",a="Yes. The wild wyverns nesting across the crags are fiercely protective of their clutches and territory. Consorts and powerful patriarchs will swoop down upon any trespasser climbing up from the canyon floor who ventures too close to their roosts.",al={"is highperch dangerous","highperch dangers","danger highperch"},it="danger",add="b4e36f31"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, you can see the wild kin of the wind riders that carry your people across Kalimdor.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can watch wild wyverns hunt and guard their nests in their natural home."},kw={"aerie","highperch","nest","pao'ka swiftmountain","thousand needles","wind rider","wyvern"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","npc:pao-ka-swiftmountain","quest:4767"},src={"Highperch"}}
E["subzone:ironstone-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Ironstone Camp",z="thousandneedles",s="At Ironstone Camp, Horde fighters now face the silithid swarm at Rustmaul Digsite. They came to drive out Alliance dwarven excavators, but the attack has changed their purpose.",h="At Ironstone Camp, Horde fighters now face the silithid swarm at Rustmaul Digsite.",sec={{t="A Change of Mission",b="Ironstone Camp stands where Thousand Needles meets the western edge of the Shimmering Flats. Moktar Krin led the Horde fighters sent to drive Alliance dwarven excavators from nearby Rustmaul Digsite.\n\nThen silithid burst from a cavern and overran the dig. They attacked both sides, so the surviving defenders now fight the swarm before it spreads across the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Ironstone Camp?",a="The Horde established Ironstone Camp to drive Alliance dwarven excavators from Rustmaul Digsite. After silithid burst from a nearby cavern and overran the dig, its fighters turned to containing the swarm.",al={"why is ironstone camp here","ironstone camp purpose","horde camp shimmering flats"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the forces at Ironstone Camp?",a="Moktar Krin leads the Horde fighters at Ironstone Camp. With silithid overrunning the digsite, he directs the defense against the swarm.",al={"ironstone camp leader","moktar krin","who runs ironstone camp"},it="leader"},{q="Where is Ironstone Camp located?",a="Ironstone Camp stands in Thousand Needles, on the western edge of the Shimmering Flats. It lies near the path from the canyon floor to the salt flats.",al={"ironstone camp location","where is ironstone camp","how to find ironstone camp"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Ironstone Camp?",a="Ironstone Camp is a small Horde outpost pitched right at the border of Thousand Needles and the Shimmering Flats. Its forces were originally sent into the salt flats to confront and drive off the dwarven excavators working the nearby Rustmaul Digsite. Instead of a straightforward skirmish with the Alliance, the scouts found themselves facing a far deadlier nightmare boiling up from beneath the earth.",al={"what is ironstone camp","ironstone camp lore","about ironstone camp"},it="place",add="219f846c"},{q="What happened at Ironstone Camp?",a="The camp was established to monitor and dismantle the dwarven operation at Rustmaul Digsite. Before the Horde forces could complete their mission, ravenous silithid erupted from a nearby cave system and overran the area. The insectoid swarm slaughtered and displaced the excavators and quickly turned its aggression on this camp, forcing the Horde scouts to abandon their original plans and fight desperately for survival.",al={"ironstone camp history","what happened here ironstone","ironstone camp background"},it="history",add="48968e37"},{q="Who lives in Ironstone Camp?",a="The camp is inhabited by a detachment of Horde soldiers, scouts, and overseers, including Moktar Krin. Cut off and pressured by the sudden silithid emergence, they remain entrenched on the rim of the flats, seeking able-bodied adventurers of the Horde to assist in repelling the encroaching insectoid threat.",al={"who is at ironstone camp","ironstone camp residents","who lives here ironstone"},it="residents",add="72b09178"},{q="Is Ironstone Camp dangerous?",a="Within the borders of the camp itself, Horde travelers will find safe harbor among their allies, though Alliance members will be met with immediate hostility. The surrounding terrain, however, is perilous. Aggressive silithid from the neighboring subterranean hives swarm the nearby digsite, threatening to overwhelm anyone who ventures out unprepared.",al={"is ironstone camp safe","ironstone camp dangers","threats at ironstone camp"},it="danger",add="b6eea169"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can stop at the camp before crossing the open salt flats. Its commanders are fighting the silithid swarm threatening their position.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance explorer, keep clear of Ironstone Camp. The Horde established it to drive dwarven excavators from Rustmaul Digsite."},kw={"horde outpost","ironstone camp","moktar krin","rustmaul digsite","shimmering flats","silithid","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde"},src={"Ironstone Camp"}}
E["subzone:mirage-raceway"] = {t="subzone",n="Mirage Raceway",z="thousandneedles",s="Rocket cars race across the salt flats at Mirage Raceway. Goblin tinkerer Pozzik and gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts test their machines as Horde and Alliance supporters gather to wager and cheer.",h="Rocket cars race across the salt flats at Mirage Raceway.",sec={{t="Speed, Salt, and Rivalry",b="Across the white salt flats, Pozzik and Fizzle Brassbolts keep up their fierce rivalry. The goblin tinkerer and gnome engineer each built a rocket-powered drag car, then gathered a crew to race it in daily showdowns. Their contest draws invention, sabotage, and testing to the flats. Each crew hunts for a mechanical advantage.",sp=0},{t="A Neutral Crossroads",b="Horde and Alliance supporters gather at the raceway. Spectators cheer for gnome precision or goblin firepower, while gamblers and shady opportunists thrive on wagers over the results. The camps also serve as a busy trading depot for travelers journeying between Thousand Needles and the blazing sands of Tanaris.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Mirage Raceway?",a="Across the salt flats of Thousand Needles, rocket cars race at Mirage Raceway. Rival engineers built the strip to prove whether goblin or gnome mechanics are superior.",al={"what is mirage raceway","raceway purpose","shimmering flats track"},it="place"},{q="Who runs the races here?",a="Gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts and goblin tinkerer Pozzik maintain the track together. Each has a crew and workshop along the raceway, where they field competing rocket cars.",al={"who leads raceway","fizzle and pozzik","who built this track"},it="residents"},{q="Can Horde and Alliance both use this area?",a="Yes. Horde and Alliance supporters gather at Mirage Raceway to cheer for their favorites, wager on races, and aid the rival engineering crews.",al={"is mirage raceway neutral","can alliance visit","can horde visit"}},{q="Why race out in the salt flats?",a="The Shimmering Flats provide a smooth, wide, open surface. Miles of room let rocket cars reach top speeds and slow down safely.",al={"why thousand needles","why race on salt","why in shimmering flats"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the history of the Mirage Raceway?",a="The raceway was born from the fierce technological rivalry between the goblin Pozzik and the gnome Fizzle Brassbolts. Determined to prove which race possessed superior engineering, the two built high-speed rocket cars and assembled dedicated racing crews. Over time, their personal contest evolved into an organized spectacle, drawing daily competitions, seedy gamblers, and spectators from across both the Alliance and the Horde to watch the rival machines clash across the salt.",al={"mirage raceway history","how did mirage raceway start","origin of mirage raceway"},it="history",add="df07332a"},{q="Is the Mirage Raceway dangerous?",a="The raceway draws Alliance and Horde supporters to wager and watch the competitions. However, the machines themselves are volatile, experimental contraptions prone to catastrophic failure. Furthermore, stepping beyond the perimeter of the racing camp puts you right into the untamed Shimmering Flats, which are crawling with aggressive scorpids, basilisks, and hostile scavengers.",al={"is mirage raceway safe","mirage raceway danger","dangers at mirage raceway"},it="danger",add="2d853a10"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For tinkerers of any faction, Mirage Raceway brings goblin risk-taking against gnomish meticulous design. Its crews field-test raw speed, volatile fuel, and experimental vehicle parts.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see Fizzle Brassbolts fly the banner of Gnomeregan here. He relies on fellow gnomes and allies to prove disciplined innovation outperforms reckless goblin combustion."},kw={"fizzle brassbolts","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:pozzik","npc:fizzle-brassbolts","zone:thousandneedles","topic:gnome","topic:goblin","subzone:gadgetzan"},src={"Mirage Raceway"}}
E["subzone:razorfen-downs"] = {t="subzone",n="Razorfen Downs",z="thousandneedles",s="Scourge power now stains Razorfen Downs, the quilboar’s sacred burial maze in southern Kalimdor. Their dead still rest among Agamaggan’s thorns, though necromancy has taken hold.",h="Scourge power now stains Razorfen Downs, the quilboar’s sacred burial maze in southern Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Sacred City Corrupted",b="Razorfen Downs holds the quilboar’s ancestral dead among the petrified briars of Agamaggan. The thorn maze rises from the fallen demigod, and legend says its arched entrance was carved from the Great Boar’s own maw. For centuries, high priests of the Death's Head tribe tended its deep, winding burrows and honored the dead. Now a catastrophe darker than any quarrel over water in the Barrens has struck this sacred ground.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge Reaches Kalimdor",b="After the Third War, the Scourge reached southern Kalimdor in silence. Amnennar the Coldbringer, a frost-wielding lich, led agents of death into the thorn maze and turned the Death's Head priesthood from within. Now the quilboar harbor rotting ghouls, skeletons, and necromancers where they once honored their ancestors. Scourge power threatens to spread across the Barrens, and the quilboar’s holiest ground has become a base for its ambitions in the west.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Downs holds the quilboar’s ancestral capital and burial grounds. Enormous thorn brambles grew from fallen Ancient Agamaggan, and the place remains the spiritual heart of quilboar culture. The Death's Head tribe’s high priesthood makes its headquarters here.",al={"what is the downs","razorfen downs lore","who lives in razorfen downs"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Scourge inside Razorfen Downs?",a="After the Third War, Amnennar the Coldbringer came to establish a Kalimdor stronghold for the Lich King. He corrupted the Death's Head priesthood and raised quilboar dead, turning the thorn maze into a hidden seat of necromantic power.",al={"why are there undead in razorfen downs","amnennar razorfen downs","scourge in razorfen"},it="threat"},{q="How does Razorfen Downs differ from Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul is the quilboar’s main military redoubt and living warren, ruled by the crone Charlga Razorflank. Razorfen Downs lies farther south as their traditional capital and sacred burial ground. Now the Scourge controls it, and necromancy holds sway.",al={"difference between kraul and downs","downs vs kraul","kraul or downs"}},{q="Where is the entrance located?",a="Razorfen Downs lies at the Barrens’ southern edge, overlooking the great drop into Thousand Needles. Its entrance is a natural arched fissure in the towering, tangled brambles. Legend says it was carved from Agamaggan’s gaping maw.",al={"downs entrance","where is razorfen downs","how to get into razorfen downs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened at Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Downs was once the proud capital and ancestral burial grounds of the quilboar, shaped from the colossal thorny vines said to have sprouted from the blood of the demigod Agamaggan. Following the Third War, however, tragedy struck the city. Agents of the Scourge infiltrated the thorn maze and spread their deadly plague. Led by the lich Amnennar the Coldbringer, the undead subjugated many of the Death's Head tribe, turning a sacred homeland into a festering bastion of undeath.",al={"razorfen downs history","what happened to razorfen downs","downs history lore"},it="history",add="e1cd26cb"},{q="Who rules Razorfen Downs?",a="The stronghold has fallen under the iron grip of Amnennar the Coldbringer, a powerful Scourge lich sent to establish a foothold in southern Kalimdor. Beneath him serve the Death's Head quilboar, whose corrupted high priests have turned to necromancy, alongside hordes of mindless ghouls, skeletons, and other undead horrors.",al={"who runs razorfen downs","who leads razorfen downs","razorfen downs boss"},it="residents",add="ac7f90f4"},{q="Is Razorfen Downs dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. Unlike the feral tribes of Razorfen Kraul, the defenders here are bolstered by the chilling magic of the Scourge. Plagued quilboar, necromancers, and swarms of risen dead wander the tangled tunnels. Deep within waits Amnennar the Coldbringer, whose presence threatens to unleash the undead plague across all of the Barrens and Thousand Needles.",al={"how dangerous is razorfen downs","razorfen downs threats","is the downs safe"},it="danger",add="42eaec66"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The quilboar trouble the Crossroads, and a Lich King outpost at the Barrens’ edge threatens the Horde. You cannot afford to ignore it.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you know the chill of finding a Scourge lich working in secret on Kalimdor. The master you rebelled against still commands such threats, and they must be destroyed swiftly."},kw={"agamaggan","amnennar","coldbringer","death speaker blackthorn","death's head","downs","quilboar","razorfen downs","scourge"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:quilboar","topic:scourge","topic:agamaggan","zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens","topic:horde","quest:5052"},src={"Razorfen Downs"}}
E["subzone:roguefeather-den"] = {t="subzone",n="Roguefeather Den",z="thousandneedles",s="In the southern cliffs of Thousand Needles, Roguefeather harpies guard their roost. Deep in the cavern, they keep scavenged provisions and stolen supplies.",h="In the southern cliffs of Thousand Needles, Roguefeather harpies guard their roost.",sec={{t="A Roost in the Canyons",b="Among the sandstone bluffs of southern Thousand Needles, Roguefeather harpies guard their roost. Their screeching carries through the cavern as they defend the food and stolen supplies gathered in its dark recesses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Roguefeather Den?",a="Along the southern cliffs of Thousand Needles, Roguefeather Den shelters a small cavern where Roguefeather harpies roost and store supplies.",al={"what is this cave","roguefeather den info","where is roguefeather"},it="place"},{q="What creatures inhabit the cave?",a="Hostile, screeching harpies inhabit the cavern. They fiercely defend their nesting grounds and gathered food.",al={"who lives in roguefeather den","mobs in roguefeather den"},it="residents"},{q="What is kept deep inside Roguefeather Den?",a="Deep in the cavern, the harpies keep scavenged and stolen food. They guard it fiercely.",al={"what is in the back of the cave","roguefeather food"},it="purpose"},{q="Is Roguefeather Den dangerous?",a="Yes, entering the den is exceptionally perilous. The cavern is cramped and overrun by aggressive, screeching harpies who fiercely protect their territory. Anyone venturing inside risks being swarmed in the dark tunnels, especially near the back of the cave where the flock zealously defends its hoarded supplies.",al={"is roguefeather den dangerous","roguefeather den dangers","how dangerous is roguefeather den"},it="danger",add="2910d8e2"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler heading toward the Shimmering Flats, you face an aggressive flock that threatens from the air. They can ambush you along the southern canyon floor."},kw={"cavern","harpies","roguefeather","roguefeather den","roost","thousand needles"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Roguefeather Den"}}
E["subzone:rustmaul-dig-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Rustmaul Dig Site",z="thousandneedles",s="Silithid swarm over Rustmaul Dig Site, a ruined camp in the southern Shimmering Flats. The Ironforge Explorers' League dug here for ancient ruins until Moktar Krin's Horde war party slaughtered the miners and a swarm rose from below. No mortals remain.",h="Silithid swarm over Rustmaul Dig Site, a ruined camp in the southern Shimmering Flats.",sec={{t="A Slaughter in the Salt",b="Ironforge's Explorers' League sent prospectors to Rustmaul Dig Site, seeking forgotten artifacts beneath the salt flats. Their work ended when Moktar Krin led a fierce Horde war party against the camp and killed the dwarven excavators. Yet the attackers found no lasting victory. Their clash apparently disturbed a dormant cave network below, and silithid poured out. The battered survivors could not hold against the swarm and fled.",sp=0},{t="The Awakening Swarm",b="Silithid now overrun Rustmaul, leaving the surface races with no hold there. Alien carapaces and skittering mandibles cover the mining gear and scaffolds. Frightened by the unceasing tide of insects from below, the survivors of Moktar Krin's war party fled north to Ironstone Camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rustmaul Dig Site?",a="Rustmaul Dig Site lies in the Shimmering Flats of Thousand Needles. Dwarven explorers founded the camp to uncover ancient ruins, but silithid swarms have overrun it.",al={"what is rustmaul","rustmaul lore","shimmering flats dig site"},it="place"},{q="Who used to live and work here?",a="Prospectors and excavators from the dwarven Explorers' League worked at the dig. They sought artifacts and ruins beneath the salt flats.",al={"who dug rustmaul","who owned rustmaul","dwarves at rustmaul"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the dig site abandoned and full of bugs?",a="Moktar Krin led a Horde war party that attacked and slaughtered the dwarves. The clash apparently disturbed a subterranean silithid nest in the mine cave, and the swarm drove the surviving attackers away.",al={"what happened at rustmaul","why are there bugs at rustmaul","who attacked rustmaul"},it="ruin"},{q="Where did the surviving attackers go?",a="The battered survivors of Moktar Krin's Horde war party fled north across the flats to Ironstone Camp. Messengers carried warnings as far as Orgrimmar.",al={"where is moktar krin","survivors of rustmaul","ironstone camp connection"}},{q="What happened at the Rustmaul Dig Site?",a="Dwarven archaeologists from the Explorers' League were unearthing ancient ruins here when a Horde war party led by Moktar Krin ambushed them, slaughtering every dwarf at the site. The violent clash apparently disturbed a subterranean hive of silithid deep within the cave. A relentless swarm erupted from the depths, overwhelming and driving out the bloodied Horde raiders and claiming the entire excavation.",al={"rustmaul dig site history","what happened at rustmaul","rustmaul massacre"},it="history",add="55b33fa4"},{q="Is the Rustmaul Dig Site dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Ravenous silithid insects crawl throughout the trenches and infest the central cave in endless swarms. Any traveler who enters risks being swarmed and devoured by the hive, just as the battered surviving raiders were driven off by their sheer numbers.",al={"is rustmaul dangerous","rustmaul dig site threats","rustmaul danger"},it="danger",add="d4492c4a"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Rustmaul is a grim reminder of the dangers facing the Explorers' League. Its scholars were slaughtered here before monstrous insects burst from the earth.",["faction:Horde"]="Moktar Krin's war party defeated the dwarven excavators, but silithid emerged after the battle. Their creeping menace now threatens the entire region."},kw={"explorers' league","ironstone camp","moktar krin","rustmaul dig site","shimmering flats","silithid","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:ironstone-camp","topic:explorers-league","topic:horde","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Rustmaul Dig Site"}}
E["subzone:shimmering-flats"] = {t="subzone",n="Shimmering Flats",z="thousandneedles",s="At Thousand Needles' southeastern edge, the Shimmering Flats stretch between the salt pan and Tanaris. The old lakebed now draws racers to the Mirage Raceway, where gnome and goblin tinkerers test their machines among desert beasts.",h="At Thousand Needles' southeastern edge, the Shimmering Flats stretch between the salt pan and Tanaris.",sec={{t="A Bed of Salt and Speed",b="Beneath the southern sun, the Shimmering Flats lie bare, with bleached turtle bones and the wooden wreck of an ancient sailing vessel. Their level salt crust makes them Kalimdor's chief ground for testing experimental vehicles. At the heart of the flats, the Mirage Raceway gathers gnome and goblin tinkerers for fierce contests. Rocket cars, gyrocopters and engines roar across the salt. Their makers chase speed, and fiery crashes leave smoking craters behind.",sp=0},{t="Hazards of the Salt",b="Beyond the raceway, hardened basilisks, aggressive scorpids and circling vultures hunt across the open flats. Farther south, the ground turns treacherous around the Rustmaul Dig Site. Dwarven prospectors first excavated the quarry, then the Horde contested it. The site was abandoned when picks broke into underground tunnels and unleashed vicious silithid across the southern edge of the flats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a ruined ship out in the middle of the desert?",a="The Shimmering Flats were once a vast inland lake. The wreck in their northern stretch is a remnant of that lake, which dried up long ago and left the salt pan and vessel behind.",al={"ship in shimmering flats","boat in salt flats","wrecked boat thousand needles"},it="history"},{q="Why are gnomes and goblins here together?",a="The level salt crust gives rocket cars and other machines ideal testing ground. Gnomes and goblins founded the Mirage Raceway instead of fighting over territory. Now their tinkerers strive to outdo one another in speed, engineering and daring.",al={"raceway lore","why are they racing","gnomes and goblins salt flats"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to the dwarven dig site in the south?",a="Dwarven archaeologists established the Rustmaul Dig Site, then a Horde raiding party led by Moktar Krin attacked them. The diggers broke into an underground silithid hive. The swarms drove everyone out and overran the southern flats.",al={"rustmaul dig site lore","what happened to rustmaul","bugs in salt flats"}},{q="Where does the road through the Shimmering Flats lead?",a="The tracks southeast across the Shimmering Flats lead through a mountain pass into Tanaris, to the neutral port of Gadgetzan.",al={"where does shimmering flats go","how to get to tanaris","exit to tanaris"}},{q="What are the Shimmering Flats?",a="The Shimmering Flats is a vast, blinding white salt flat situated at the southeastern end of Thousand Needles, bordering the desert of Tanaris. It is a completely dried-out lakebed entirely devoid of plant life, offering an immense, flat expanse where inventors test their wildest creations and aggressive desert beasts roam the cracked earth.",al={"what is shimmering flats","shimmering flats lore","about shimmering flats"},it="place",add="a9a42c0c"},{q="Is the Shimmering Flats dangerous?",a="Despite its barren appearance, the flats are quite perilous. Deadly native predators like salt basilisks, scorpids, and vultures prowl the open basin, while the volatile rocket cars and testing accidents of goblin and gnome racers leave fiery debris everywhere. Furthermore, a subterranean silithid hive has recently erupted in the southern reaches, overrunning an ancient dwarven excavation.",al={"is shimmering flats dangerous","shimmering flats hazards","how dangerous is shimmering flats"},it="danger",add="bc39548e"},{q="Why is it called the Shimmering Flats?",a="The name comes from the blinding visual effect of the sun beating down across the ancient, crystallized salt bed. The harsh glare off the white, arid mineral crust creates a dazzling, shimmering mirage across the horizon, visible for miles across the dried basin.",al={"why shimmering flats","shimmering flats name origin","why is it called shimmering flats"},it="name",add="b2b7f543"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For engineers, the salt flats offer scrap, fuel experiments and high-speed trials. Goblin and gnomish machinists keep the rivalry at the Mirage Raceway alive.",["race:Gnome"]="At the Mirage Raceway, gnomish pilots defend their engineering pride against the volatile, explosive designs of their goblin rivals."},kw={"mirage raceway","pozzik","rustmaul","salt flats","shimmering flats","silithid","tanaris","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:mirage-raceway","zone:thousandneedles","zone:tanaris","subzone:rustmaul-dig-site","npc:pozzik","quest:1179","quest:5762"},src={"Shimmering Flats"}}
E["subzone:splithoof-crag"] = {t="subzone",n="Splithoof Crag",z="thousandneedles",s="Galak centaur patrol the northern cliffs of Splithoof Crag and guard their canyon stronghold. Their settlement surrounds Splithoof Hold, while they contest the ravine below the Grimtotem heights.",h="Galak centaur patrol the northern cliffs of Splithoof Crag and guard their canyon stronghold.",sec={{t="A Galak Stronghold",b="On the northern rock face of Thousand Needles, east of Darkcloud Pinnacle, Galak centaur keep their stronghold. Crude tents and dirt paths fill the enclave. Against the cliff stands Splithoof Hold, a cavern beneath the settlement. There, the Galak guard the Cloven Hoof, an ancient centaur relic kept beside a sacred brazier.",sp=0},{t="Defending the Caverns",b="Galak centaur attack travelers, Horde expeditions, and tauren scouts passing beneath their bluffs. The Grimtotem occupy nearby high pinnacles. Yet the Galak hold the canyon ravine and the caverns beneath its stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Splithoof Crag?",a="The Galak centaur tribe lives in Splithoof Crag, one of the prominent clans of Thousand Needles. The hostile Grimtotem tauren live nearby.",al={"who is at splithoof crag","splithoof crag mobs","centaur in splithoof crag"},it="residents"},{q="Where is Splithoof Crag located?",a="Splithoof Crag runs along the northern canyon wall of Thousand Needles, directly east of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"where is splithoof crag","splithoof crag location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is inside Splithoof Hold?",a="Splithoof Hold is the village's central cavern. Deep within, the Galak guard the Cloven Hoof, an ancient tribal artifact protected by a sacred flame in a brazier.",al={"what is splithoof hold","cave in splithoof crag"}},{q="Are the centaur here allied with the nearby Grimtotem?",a="No alliance between the Galak and Grimtotem is known. The Galak hold their canyon village and caverns, while the Grimtotem occupy the heights of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"grimtotem and galak","centaur and tauren relation"},it="allies"},{q="What is Splithoof Crag?",a="Splithoof Crag is a fortified settlement carved into the northern rock walls of Thousand Needles, situated just east of Darkcloud Pinnacle. It serves as a major stronghold for the local Galak centaur, featuring clustered encampments along the canyon floor and an inner cavern known as Splithoof Hold.",al={"what is this place","splithoof crag info","about splithoof crag"},it="place",add="fc440e32"},{q="Is Splithoof Crag dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for outsiders. The Galak centaur are fiercely aggressive, territorial, and attack intruders on sight. Furthermore, the settlement's inner sanctum, Splithoof Hold, is heavily defended to protect their sacred relics.",al={"is it safe here","danger splithoof crag","splithoof crag threats"},it="danger",add="76cca678"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the long-standing hostility between your people and the centaur makes Splithoof Crag a concern. Horde scouts watch for hostile activity in Thousand Needles.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you need the passage beneath the crags kept clear. It allows safe travel between the southern Barrens, Freewind Post, and the Shimmering Flats."},kw={"centaur","cloven hoof","darkcloud pinnacle","galak","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:splithoof-hold","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle"},src={"Splithoof Crag"}}
E["subzone:splithoof-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Splithoof Hold",z="thousandneedles",s="Galak centaur guard Splithoof Hold in the caves of Splithoof Crag. Within, the Ancient Brazier keeps their sacred flame burning without end.",h="Galak centaur guard Splithoof Hold in the caves of Splithoof Crag.",sec={{t="A Centaur Bastion",b="Within Splithoof Crag, Galak centaur defend their cavern against rival tribes and travelers crossing Thousand Needles. Its deep shelter protects them from the windswept canyon floor. Chokepoints guard the way in, with a secure refuge inside the rock.",sp=0},{t="The Sacred Flame",b="Deep within Splithoof Hold, the Ancient Brazier cradles the Sacred Flame. The mystic fire burns without end. The centaur honor it in ritual, while spiritual wanderers from across the canyon come to wonder at its power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Splithoof Hold located?",a="Splithoof Hold lies within Splithoof Crag, along the northern cliffs of Thousand Needles. Enter through a cave opening in the main centaur settlement.",al={"splithoof hold location","where is splithoof hold","how to find splithoof hold"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who controls Splithoof Hold?",a="The Galak centaur hold Splithoof Hold and defend it fiercely against outsiders, beasts, and the nearby tauren of Freewind Post.",al={"who lives in splithoof hold","splithoof hold mobs","who owns splithoof hold"},it="residents"},{q="What is inside the hold?",a="Beyond its hostile Galak centaur defenders, the cave holds the Ancient Brazier. Its power keeps the mystical Sacred Flame burning without end in the depths of the rock.",al={"what is in splithoof hold","ancient brazier location","sacred flame splithoof"},it="place"},{q="What is Splithoof Hold?",a="Splithoof Hold is a cavern stronghold carved into the rock of Splithoof Crag in Thousand Needles. The fierce Galak centaur tribe claimed the natural cave and adapted it into a fortified base within the canyon, keeping their sacred relics and clan hearth sheltered inside.",al={"what is splithoof hold","splithoof hold lore","about splithoof hold"},it="place",add="9edfe937"},{q="Is Splithoof Hold dangerous?",a="Splithoof Hold is extremely perilous to outsiders. It serves as a major redoubt for the aggressive Galak centaur, who fiercely guard their cavern, warbands, and the eternal Sacred Flame kept within its depths from any trespassers.",al={"is splithoof hold dangerous","splithoof hold danger","threat splithoof hold"},it="danger",add="8bfe11a3"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you face sworn blood enemies in the Galak centaur. Their stronghold in Thousand Needles threatens the peace of Freewind Post.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may be drawn to the eternal flame deep within the dark stone cavern. Its elemental fire remains a mystery."},kw={"ancient brazier","galak centaur","sacred flame","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:splithoof-crag","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","quest:1195"},src={"Splithoof Hold"}}
E["subzone:tahonda-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Tahonda Ruins",z="thousandneedles",s="Salt and sand cover Tahonda Ruins, where Saltstone basilisks stalk the remains of an ancient tauren settlement in the Shimmering Flats.",h="Salt and sand cover Tahonda Ruins, where Saltstone basilisks stalk the remains of an ancient tauren...",sec={{t="Sunken beneath the Salt",b="Tahonda Ruins lie in the southern Shimmering Flats, near the pass into Tanaris. Salt crusts cover the weathered remains of this abandoned tauren village, and strange marks scar the surviving structures.\n\nTwo sets of three parallel tears cut through the leather of a ruined lodge. No one knows whether Saltstone basilisks drove the villagers away. The marks point to a violent end at the claws of powerful predators or hostile invaders, before the desert claimed what remained.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were the Tahonda Ruins originally?",a="Tahonda was once a tauren village on the dry Shimmering Flats. Shifting sands and salt crusts gradually swallowed it into ruin.",al={"what is tahonda ruins","who built tahonda","tahonda ruins history"},it="place"},{q="Why was the village abandoned?",a="No written history records why the village was abandoned. Saltstone basilisks overrun the ruins now and may have driven the settlers away. Deep, three-clawed tears in the surviving leather lodges also suggest a sudden, violent attack.",al={"why is tahonda ruined","what destroyed tahonda","what happened to tahonda"},it="ruin"},{q="What creatures live in the ruins now?",a="Hostile Saltstone basilisks infest the village remains now. They sun themselves among rotting wooden poles and tattered hide shelters.",al={"tahonda mobs","what is at tahonda ruins","tahonda beasts"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to the Tahonda Ruins?",a="Very little is recorded of Tahonda's past. It was once an ancient tauren settlement that eventually collapsed and was gradually buried by the shifting sands of the Shimmering Flats. While the encroaching Saltstone basilisks may have forced the villagers out, claw marks torn across the weathered leather dwellings suggest the settlement met a violent end at the hands of savage beasts or hostile raiders before it was lost to time.",al={"tahonda ruins history","what happened at tahonda ruins","tahonda ruins story"},it="history",add="601f2090"},{q="Are the Tahonda Ruins dangerous?",a="Yes. The sunken remnants of the village have become a breeding ground for aggressive Saltstone basilisks. Wandering through the half-buried leather tents and collapsed poles leaves you exposed to these stone-gazing predators, who make the desolate corner of the salt flats perilous for unwary travelers passing toward Tanaris.",al={"is tahonda ruins dangerous","tahonda ruins threats","dangers in tahonda ruins"},it="danger",add="d43cf6cc"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Among the salt of Thousand Needles, a forgotten tauren settlement recalls the dangers your nomadic ancestors faced while wandering Kalimdor."},kw={"saltstone basilisks","shimmering flats","tahonda","tahonda ruins","tauren village","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","zone:tanaris"},src={"Tahonda Ruins"}}
E["subzone:weathered-nook"] = {t="subzone",n="Weathered Nook",z="thousandneedles",s="High above Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer make their home in a quiet cliffside shelter. From there, they look out across the stone spires, far from the canyon floor.",h="High above Thousand Needles, Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer make their home in a quiet cliffside...",sec={{t="Haven on the Cliffs",b="North of Freewind Post, a narrow ramp climbs the sandstone cliff to a sheltered ledge and cave. From below, travelers can easily miss the Weathered Nook high above the canyon basin. Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer live here, away from any large settlement or military post. The ledge shelters them from the prevailing winds and gives them a broad view across the needle plateaus.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Weathered Nook located?",a="The Weathered Nook lies along Thousand Needles' northern cliff wall. From Freewind Post, travel north to the towering rock face, then follow the cliffs east to a winding ramp up the mesa wall.",al={"how to find weathered nook","weathered nook location","where is nook"},gp=true},{q="Who lives in the Weathered Nook?",a="Dorn Plainstalker and Prate Cloudseer live in the Weathered Nook. The two solitary tauren dwell on this remote ledge above the canyon, rather than atop Freewind Post's crowded towers.",al={"who is here","weathered nook residents","npcs in nook"},it="residents"},{q="Is the Weathered Nook affiliated with the Horde?",a="The Weathered Nook is a personal camp and wilderness home, not a formal Horde garrison. Its residents are tauren among their own kindred.",al={"is this a horde camp","horde weathered nook"},it="side"},{q="What is the Weathered Nook?",a="The Weathered Nook is a small, secluded shelter carved into the northern cliff walls overlooking the canyons of Thousand Needles. Far from the bustling pathways of Freewind Post and the Shimmering Flats, this quiet crevice serves as a humble encampment for travelers seeking respite from the harsh elements and wandering beasts of the canyon floor.",al={"weathered nook what is","what is weathered nook","weathered nook info"},it="place",add="3c15de53"},{q="Is the Weathered Nook dangerous?",a="The nook itself is relatively tranquil compared to the surrounding canyon floor, serving as a sanctuary for its inhabitants. However, the path along the towering bluffs can be treacherous, and aggressive beasts such as prowling cougars, wyverns, and centaur raiders roam the rocky heights and passes nearby.",al={"weathered nook dangerous","is weathered nook safe","threats at weathered nook"},it="danger",add="4c65fc70"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can find a quiet place for self-reliance at the Weathered Nook. The ledge offers a peaceful view across the canyon, away from Freewind Post's busy bridges.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde wanderer, you can find friendly kindred sheltering along the canyon's northern cliffs."},kw={"cave","cliff","dorn plainstalker","freewind post","prate cloudseer","thousand needles","weathered nook"},rel={"npc:dorn-plainstalker","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post"},src={"Weathered Nook"}}
E["subzone:weazel-s-crater"] = {t="subzone",n="Weazel's Crater",z="thousandneedles",s="Saltstone basilisks now sun themselves in the deep hollow of Weazel's Crater, while its origins remain unknown.",h="Saltstone basilisks now sun themselves in the deep hollow of Weazel's Crater, while its origins remain...",sec={{t="A Volatile Legacy",b="Weazel's Crater cuts deep into the northern Shimmering Flats. Experimental goblin and gnome rocket-cars still race across the blinding salt, pushing mechanical limits. Scorched earth, debris, and impact hollows mark the plain, but none match the crater's size and depth. No one knows what formed it. The wreckage has largely settled, and aggressive Saltstone basilisks now sun themselves in the hollow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What caused Weazel's Crater?",a="No one knows what caused Weazel's Crater. Its origins remain unexplained.",al={"how was weazel's crater formed","weazels crater origin","why is there a crater here"},it="history"},{q="What lives in the crater now?",a="Dangerous Saltstone basilisks inhabit the crater, lurking along its rocky edges and bottom.",al={"weazels crater mobs","what is inside the crater"},it="residents"},{q="What is Weazel's Crater?",a="Weazel's Crater is a large, deep depression gouged into the northern expanse of the Shimmering Flats in Thousand Needles. While it resembles an impact site, it sits right along the paths where goblins and gnomes test their volatile, rocket-powered racing machines, making it a prominent and hazardous landmark amid the salt desert.",al={"weazels crater","what is this crater","weazel crater shimmering flats"},it="place",add="76b07605"},{q="Is Weazel's Crater dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the risk of reckless rocket racers careening across the flats, the crater itself has become an infested den for aggressive Saltstone basilisks. Anyone stepping down into the hollow risks being turned to stone or mauled by the territorial beasts lurking within.",al={"is weazels crater dangerous","weazel crater threats","danger weazels crater"},it="danger",add="4a4cb038"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Weazel's Crater lies amid experimental racing machines and debris in the Shimmering Flats. As an engineer visiting the speedway, you have reason to study its hazardous terrain."},kw={"gnome engineering","goblin raceway","saltstone basilisks","shimmering flats","thousand needles","weazel's crater"},rel={"subzone:shimmering-flats","zone:thousandneedles","topic:goblin","topic:gnome"},src={"Weazel's Crater"}}
E["subzone:whitereach-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Whitereach Post",z="thousandneedles",s="Horde travelers find rest at Whitereach Post beside the canyon path in Thousand Needles. Near Camp E'thok, the small camp overlooks the harsh road between Feralas and the salt flats beneath the sandstone pillars.",h="Horde travelers find rest at Whitereach Post beside the canyon path in Thousand Needles.",sec={{t="A Waystation in the Canyons",b="Whitereach Post watches over the canyon road through Thousand Needles. Near Camp E'thok, this modest Horde foothold is one of several posts in the rugged wastes. Scouts monitor travel along the canyon floor between the mesas. Couriers and travelers crossing the contested wastes can stop here, though the post has fewer defenses than the great lift or the major tribal settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Whitereach Post?",a="Whitereach Post is a small Horde outpost beside Thousand Needles' main canyon path, near Camp E'thok.",al={"whitereach","whitereach camp","where is whitereach post"},it="place"},{q="Which faction controls Whitereach Post?",a="The Horde controls Whitereach Post, where tauren scouts watch the gorge trails.",al={"is whitereach horde","whitereach faction"},it="side"},{q="Who can be found stationed here?",a="Horde scouts and wanderers are stationed at Whitereach Post. Kanati Greycloud, a tauren, watches the canyon passage.",al={"whitereach npcs","who lives at whitereach post"},it="residents"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you can rest at Whitereach Post while scouts keep watch over Thousand Needles' perilous canyons.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you help secure this roadside camp, where tribesfolk traveling between Mulgore, Feralas, and the Shimmering Flats can rest."},kw={"camp e'thok","horde outpost","kanati greycloud","tauren","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","topic:horde","subzone:camp-e-thok","npc:kanati-greycloud"},src={"Whitereach Post"}}
E["subzone:windbreak-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Windbreak Canyon",z="thousandneedles",s="Wind serpents hunt travelers along the northern road through Windbreak Canyon. The canyon lies between Freewind Post and the Shimmering Flats.",h="Wind serpents hunt travelers along the northern road through Windbreak Canyon.",sec={{t="A Serpent Nest in the Needles",b="East of Freewind Post, Windbreak Canyon cuts through the sheer northern walls above the canyon floor. Whistling winds race between the stone spires, leaving little shelter. Wild wind serpents perch among the rocks, lay clutches on the ledges, and strike travelers who stray from the main road. Winding trails climb through the canyon toward the Weathered Nook.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Windbreak Canyon?",a="Windbreak Canyon runs along the northern side of Thousand Needles, between Freewind Post and the eastern approach to the Shimmering Flats.",al={"windbreak canyon location","where is windbreak canyon","windbreak map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures live in Windbreak Canyon?",a="Aggressive wild wind serpents nest among the canyon's crags and defend their clutches from intruders.",al={"windbreak monsters","what is in windbreak canyon","windbreak mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Where does the trail inside the canyon lead?",a="Winding trails climb through the canyon toward the Weathered Nook in the cliffs above.",al={"windbreak path","trail in windbreak canyon","where does windbreak go"},gp=true},{q="What is Windbreak Canyon?",a="Windbreak Canyon is a sprawling, rugged gorge nestled in Thousand Needles. Stretching across much of the northern expanse between Freewind Post and the Shimmering Flats, the canyon is best known for its dense population of nesting wind serpents and the winding trail leading up to the Weathered Nook.",al={"what is windbreak canyon","windbreak canyon overview","tell me about windbreak canyon"},it="place",add="7c7f9a22"},{q="Is Windbreak Canyon dangerous?",a="Yes. The gorge is teeming with wild wind serpents guarding their nests along the rocky floor and canyon walls. Anyone traversing the canyon toward the Weathered Nook must stay alert, as these territorial beasts strike quickly against any intruders who stray too close to their brood.",al={"is windbreak canyon dangerous","dangers of windbreak canyon","windbreak canyon threats"},it="danger",add="4bddac98"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can study and tame the agile wind serpents that nest throughout the canyon and spit lightning."},kw={"freewind post","thousand needles","weathered nook","wind serpents","windbreak canyon"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:weathered-nook","subzone:shimmering-flats"},src={"Windbreak Canyon"}}
E["zone:thousandneedles"] = {t="zone",n="Thousand Needles",z="thousandneedles",s="In southern Kalimdor, Thousand Needles stands over a dry canyon of sandstone pillars. Tauren hold the mesas, while gnomes and goblins race rocket cars across the Shimmering Flats.",h="In southern Kalimdor, Thousand Needles stands over a dry canyon of sandstone pillars.",sec={{t="A Forest of Stone",b="Before the Great Sundering, inland waterways fed a lush river canyon that ran toward the sea. The cataclysm shattered ancient Kalimdor, raised the riverbed above the water table, and changed the river's course. Dry stone and sandstone spires remain. Dozens of slender, cylindrical columns rise from the canyon floor like a forest turned to stone.\n\nTauren built villages atop the columns and joined the peaks with precarious rope bridges. They sought escape from hostile centaur marauders patrolling the shadow-draped floor below.",sp=0},{t="Peril on the Mesas",b="Life atop the needle-like spires is far from peaceful. At Freewind Post, tauren loyal to the Horde face predatory wind serpents and wyverns from Highperch, and treacherous kin of the militant Grimtotem clan, entrenched at Darkcloud Pinnacle. Cliffwatcher Longhorn directs the plateau's defense. He seeks bold fighters to strike Grimtotem agitators and secure the fragile bridges between peaks.\n\nTo the north, enormous mechanical winches at the Great Lift carry travelers down from the southern Barrens. Crossing the canyon floor remains a deadly gamble.",sp=0},{t="The Mirage Raceway",b="To the southeast, the canyon walls open onto the Shimmering Flats, an enormous dried-up salt pan below sea level. Gnomes and goblins keep an uneasy neutrality around the Mirage Raceway in this harsh, blinding expanse. Rival engineers Pozzik and Fizzle Brassbolts race experimental rocket cars across the hard salt, each seeking to prove their race's technological superiority.\n\nThe pit stop draws scoundrels, swindlers like Kravel Koalbeard, and hunters pursuing the hardy scorpions, turtles, and basilisks that roam the searing basin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How did Thousand Needles get its name?",a="Thousand Needles takes its name from the dozens of massive, cylindrical sandstone spires rising from the canyon floor. Rushing rivers carved them before the Great Sundering, and now they resemble a forest of giant needles.",al={"why is it called thousand needles","needle pillars origin","spires lore"},it="name"},{q="How do you get down into Thousand Needles from the Barrens?",a="Travelers ride the Great Lift, an immense double-car elevator run by Horde guards on the Barrens' southern border. A fall from the edge is fatal, so wait for the platform. Alliance travelers can also hike in from the west through Thalanaar in Feralas.",al={"how to get to thousand needles","great lift entrance","elevator to needles"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why do the tauren live on top of the mesas?",a="Centaur warbands once drove the nomadic tauren nearly to extinction. Outposts like Freewind Post, atop inaccessible stone pillars, kept them safe from centaur ground charges. Wooden suspension bridges linked the mesas, letting tauren travel above the predators and raiders below.",al={"why are tauren on pillars","freewind post history","tauren high ground"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Mirage Raceway?",a="The Mirage Raceway is an engineering proving ground on the Shimmering Flats salt pan. Gnomish and goblin tinkerers race experimental rocket-propelled cars across the flat salt bed to settle their rivalry over which race builds the finest machinery.",al={"salt flats track","gnome goblin race","rocket car track"}},{q="What is the Grimtotem presence in the canyon?",a="The Grimtotem clan occupies Darkcloud Pinnacle, a fortified cluster of spires directly opposing Freewind Post. Unlike the other tauren tribes, who pledged to the Horde, the Grimtotem attack their kin and conspire to dominate the mesas.",al={"grimtotem thousand needles","darkcloud pinnacle tauren","evil tauren needles"},it="threat"},{q="What are the Shimmering Flats?",a="The Shimmering Flats are a vast, dried lakebed east of the canyon mesas. Its salt crust formed when the ancient inland sea evaporated after the Sundering. Searing heat, blinding white salt, and harsh predators make it an inhospitable desert used mainly for high-speed vehicle testing.",al={"salt pan","white desert needles","eastern desert"},it="place"},{q="What is Thousand Needles?",a="Thousand Needles is a vast, arid canyon dividing central and southern Kalimdor. Its canyon floor is thick with towering sandstone spires that stretch toward the sky like a petrified forest, linked above by delicate rope and wood bridges. In the east, the canyon gives way to the Shimmering Flats, a blinding white salt pan.",al={"what is this place","about thousand needles","tell me about thousand needles"},it="place",add="d1fb42e2",nx={8}},{q="Why is it all canyons and pillars?",a="Ages ago, before the Great Sundering, this region was a verdant river canyon carved out by rushing waters flowing eastward from Feralas into an inland sea. When the world shattered, the cataclysm thrust the riverbed upward and altered the river's course. Deprived of water, the land dried out, leaving behind towering sandstone pillars and a parched salt bed.",al={"why are there spires","how did the needles form","why sandstone pillars"},it="origin",add="98fcff4e"},{q="Is Thousand Needles dangerous?",a="It is quite dangerous. Barbaric Galak centaur patrol the canyon floor in raiding bands, while predatory vultures, scorpids, and rogue harpies haunt the cliffs. Even the rope bridges between high pinnacles carry peril, as birds of prey frequently swoop down upon unwary travelers or damage the spans.",al={"how dangerous is thousand needles","dangers here","is it safe"},it="danger",add="05d5c74f"},{q="Why did the Horde send me to Thousand Needles?",a="The Horde maintains a vital presence here to aid the local tauren tribes who are under relentless assault. Freewind Post stands as a critical bastion connecting the Barrens with the southern deserts, and the Horde needs brave champions to drive back marauding centaur and quell internal threats.",al={"horde mission thousand needles","why am i here horde","what does horde want here"},it="arrival",add="1b8e8bea",nx={11}},{q="Is this tauren land?",a="Yes. The barren canyons and high mesas of Thousand Needles have traditionally been the ancestral territory of several tauren tribes for countless generations, though vicious centaur clans pushed them to the brink of survival before the Horde arrived.",al={"do tauren own thousand needles","tauren territory","is this shu'halo land"},it="ties",add="a7c3b539"},{q="What is Freewind Post?",a="Freewind Post is the primary Horde outpost in Thousand Needles. Built atop a massive mesa high above the valley floor, it features wooden elevators, a flight tower, and a network of suspension bridges reaching adjacent pinnacles.",al={"freewind post","what is freewind","freewind village"},it="place",add="fef8bf7c"},{q="Who are the Galak centaur and why are they attacking us?",a="The Galak tribe are the local centaur who claim the canyon floor. Like all centaur, they are fiercely territorial, nomadic, and violent. They hunt down any travelers passing through the gorges and seek to eradicate the tauren settlements completely.",al={"galak centaur","why centaur attack","galak tribe"},it="threat",add="6ac472b0",nx={14}},{q="Why do they hate the tauren?",a="The enmity between tauren and centaur is ancient and unrelenting. For generations across the plains of Kalimdor, roving centaur hunted tauren for sport and launched brutal, unprovoked wars that kept the peaceful tribes constantly on the run.",al={"why do centaur hate tauren","centaur tauren feud","centaur grudge"},it="conflict",add="9f0b1de8"},{q="Why are goblins and gnomes racing rocket cars in the desert?",a="The flat, open salt of the Shimmering Flats provides the perfect proving ground for testing high-speed engines. Gnomes and goblins established the Mirage Raceway to permanently settle the long-standing dispute over which race possesses superior engineering.",al={"why racing cars","goblin gnome race","rocket car rivalry"},it="other",add="0eee4587"},{q="What's the deal with Darkcloud Pinnacle and those secret notes?",a="Darkcloud Pinnacle is the Grimtotem tribe's heavily guarded stronghold on the mesas east of the Great Lift. Secret correspondence discovered there reveals covert contact between Grimtotem leaders like Arnak Grimtotem and an unknown dark power, suggesting treacherous ambitions far beyond simple tribal feuds.",al={"darkcloud pinnacle notes","grimtotem notes","darkcloud pinnacle mystery"},sp=1,it="purpose",add="e421f132",nx={17},bt={"q4542.4"}},{q="What are the Grimtotem planning?",a="The Grimtotem fundamentally reject Cairne Bloodhoof's leadership and the cultural shifts brought by joining the Horde. They seek to depose Cairne, undermine Horde authority, and even consort with sinister powers and summon entities of vengeance to assert their dominance.",al={"grimtotem plan","what do grimtotem want","grimtotem conspiracy"},sp=1,it="motive",add="7b560411"},{q="What is Highperch and why do we want wyvern eggs?",a="Highperch is the ancestral nesting ground of wild wyverns in Thousand Needles. Tauren from Freewind Post climb to these high perches to gather fertile wyvern eggs so they can be carefully raised and trained as loyal flying mounts for the Horde.",al={"highperch wyverns","why collect wyvern eggs","highperch eggs"},it="purpose",add="853c4dd1"},{q="How did I end up in Thousand Needles?",a="Most travelers arrive from the north by riding south through the Barrens past Camp Taurajo, eventually reaching the sheer cliff edge where the massive tauren-engineered Great Lift lowers you straight down into the canyon floor. Alternatively, adventurers trekking eastward through the dense forests of Feralas enter the western gorge by foot, while daring explorers braving the perils of Dustwallow Marsh or sailing into Theramore slip through the contested gaps. A long overland march north from the deserts of Tanaris also brings you directly into the sprawling salt expanse of the Shimmering Flats.",al={"how did i get here","how do i reach thousand needles","getting to thousand needles"},it="arrival",add="dc3189d8"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Thousand Needles?",a="Your presence here depends on your allegiances and ambitions. Horde champions are tasked with aiding Freewind Post: pushing back the Galak centaur bands that roam the canyon floor, monitoring harpy roosts, collecting wyvern eggs from Highperch, and combating the treacherous Grimtotem tribe entrenched atop Darkcloud Pinnacle. For unaligned wanderers and Alliance travelers, the dramatic expanse serves as a hazardous overland crossroads between central and southern Kalimdor, leading toward the Shimmering Flats where goblin and gnome daredevils pay good coin for parts, fuel, and assistance with their perpetual rocket-car rivalry.",al={"why am i here","what is my purpose here","what do i do in thousand needles"},it="purpose",add="16801326"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see how high your people climbed to escape centaur slaughter. Freewind Post is also a staging ground against the treacherous Grimtotem at Darkcloud Pinnacle.",["race:Gnome"]="At the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats, you can show the precision and elegance of gnomish engineering beside shoddy goblin contraptions.",["profession:Engineering"]="The salt flats draw tinkerers seeking to study rocket fuel, vehicle parts, and high-speed propulsion at the Mirage Raceway.",["faction:Horde"]="The Great Lift links the Barrens to your stronghold at Freewind Post, marking a strategic southern boundary against centaur clans and rebel tauren."},kw={"cliffwatcher longhorn","darkcloud pinnacle","fizzle brassbolts","freewind post","great lift","grimtotem","kravel koalbeard","mirage raceway","pozzik","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},rel={"subzone:freewind-post","subzone:shimmering-flats","subzone:mirage-raceway","subzone:great-lift","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","zone:barrens","zone:feralas","zone:tanaris"},m={levels="25-35"},src={"Thousand Needles (Classic)","Thousand Needles"}}
